{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T00:50:57.084Z","ordinal":7115,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0c3176283919dd68016aa1fea7dee487d0a93b39d8dcf68956","status":"completed","call_id":"call_8NvtVDkX7pZa3nzV8HzegQrt","name":"exec","input":"const remove = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Delete File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/references/github.md\\n*** Delete File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md\\n*** End Patch\";\nconst add = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/references/github.md\\n+# GitHub Reference\\n+\\n+## Pull requests\\n+\\n+A PR body gives a reviewer with no prior context enough information to understand the outcome, inspect the risky decisions, and verify the change. Ground it in the live base-branch diff and observed checks.\\n+\\n+```markdown\\n+## Summary\\n+- Outcome and why it matters\\n+- Important behavioral or architectural decision, when needed for review\\n+\\n+## Verification\\n+- [x] `exact command or inspection` — observed result\\n+- [ ] Not run: reason and resulting coverage gap\\n+\\n+## Risk and follow-up\\n+<!-- Include only migrations, compatibility risks, limitations, rollout work, or intentional deferrals. -->\\n+\\n+## Related\\n+<!-- Include only links that exist: issue, requirement, spec, plan, or changeset. -->\\n+```\\n+\\n+Omit empty optional sections and placeholder links. Use enough summary bullets to explain one coherent change; if the bullets reveal independent topics, split the PR or explain why they must ship together.\\n+\\n+Verification records evidence already observed. Never turn an unrun check into an unchecked instruction without stating why it was not run and what remains unverified.\\n+\\n+Call out breaking behavior under `Risk and follow-up` with the old behavior, new behavior, and required migration.\\n+\\n+## Voice\\n+\\n+- Lead with user-visible or architectural intent, not a file inventory or development chronology.\\n+- Use direct, active language and concrete outcomes.\\n+- State material concerns, evidence, consequence, and confidence without softening blockers or overstating certainty.\\n+- Keep technical detail that changes approval; link to deeper artifacts instead of copying them.\\n+- Do not restate the diff.\\n+\\n+## Review comments\\n+\\n+Prefix intent when it prevents ambiguity. Use one vocabulary consistently:\\n+\\n+- Conventional Comments: `praise:`, `nitpick:`, `suggestion:`, `issue:`, `question:`, `thought:`; add `(non-blocking)` when needed.\\n+- Google style: `Nit:`, `Optional:`, `Consider:`, `FYI:` for non-blocking feedback.\\n+\\n+Do not manufacture praise. When a material issue exists, state the problem, cite the evidence, explain the consequence, and mark whether it blocks approval. Recommend one fix only when the constraints make it uniquely correct; otherwise describe the required outcome.\\n+\\n+## Review focus\\n+\\n+- Does the change satisfy its linked requirement or specification?\\n+- Does every changed behavior have discriminating evidence at the relevant boundary?\\n+- Are skipped checks and residual risks explicit?\\n+- Are breaking changes, migrations, and consumer-facing effects documented?\\n+- Do shared contracts, generated artifacts, and supported harnesses remain aligned when affected?\\n+- Does the change contain unrelated scope or unresolved sibling defects?\\n+\\n+## `gh` commands\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+gh pr create --title \\\"feat(ranger): add cross-language audit\\\" --body-file body.md\\n+gh pr list\\n+gh pr diff <number>\\n+gh pr status\\n+gh pr review <number> --approve\\n+gh pr review <number> --request-changes --body-file review.md\\n+gh pr merge <number> --squash --delete-branch\\n+```\\n+\\n+Show the exact target, title, body, labels, and review text before any remote mutation. Never invent issue links, results, or artifact paths.\\n+\\n+## Issues\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+gh issue create --title \\\"...\\\" --body-file issue.md --label bug\\n+gh issue list --label enhancement\\n+gh issue close <number>\\n+```\\n+\\n+## GitHub Actions annotations\\n+\\n+```text\\n+::error file=src/lib.rs,line=42,col=5::Error message here\\n+::warning file=src/lib.rs,line=10::Warning message here\\n+::notice file=src/lib.rs,line=1::Notice message here\\n+```\\n+\\n+## Labels\\n+\\n+| Label | Meaning |\\n+| :--- | :--- |\\n+| `bug` | Confirmed defect |\\n+| `enhancement` | New capability or improvement |\\n+| `breaking` | Consumer migration required |\\n+| `needs-spec` | Specification required before implementation |\\n+| `needs-plan` | Plan required before implementation |\\n+| `in-progress` | Active work |\\n+| `blocked` | External resolution required |\\n*** Add File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md\\n+## Summary\\n+\\n+<!-- State the outcome and why it matters. Add an important behavioral or architectural decision only when it helps review. -->\\n+\\n+-\\n+\\n+## Verification\\n+\\n+<!-- Record checks already run and their observed results. For an unrun check, state why and what remains unverified. -->\\n+\\n+- [ ] `command or inspection` — observed result\\n+\\n+## Risk and follow-up\\n+\\n+<!-- Remove this section when there are no migrations, compatibility risks, limitations, rollout steps, or intentional deferrals. -->\\n+\\n+## Related\\n+\\n+<!-- Remove this section when there is no issue, requirement, spec, plan, or changeset to link. -->\\n*** End Patch\";\nawait tools.apply_patch(remove);\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(add));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a088c6-48bb-7040-a264-83f7cdb1775a","create_time":1789001369.753829}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T00:50:57.102Z","ordinal":7116,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a088c6-48bb-7040-a264-83f7cdb1775a","session_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","root_turn_id":"01a088c6-48bb-7040-a264-83f7cdb1775a","response_id":"resp_0c3176283919dd68016aa1fe9993a087d0b2a28f1b739ccd4b","usage":{"input_tokens":184753,"cached_input_tokens":183936,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1651,"reasoning_output_tokens":396,"total_tokens":186404},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2121243,"cached_input_tokens":2092288,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":9254,"reasoning_output_tokens":4557,"total_tokens":2130497},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":106131112,"cached_input_tokens":104117376,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":476630,"reasoning_output_tokens":157212,"total_tokens":106607742}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T00:50:59.234Z","ordinal":7117,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a088c6-48bb-7040-a264-83f7cdb1775a","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-2d8d34b9-51bd-46d3-b409-76149d65ae10","changes":{"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md":{"type":"delete","content":"## Summary\n- What changed (1-3 bullets, user-facing language)\n- Why it was needed\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] How to verify the change works\n- [ ] Edge cases to check\n- [ ] Regression check\n\n## Related\nCloses #<issue>\nSpec: <link to spec doc, if any>\n"},"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/references/github.md":{"type":"delete","content":"# GitHub Reference\n\n## PR Description Template\n\n```markdown\n## Summary\n- What changed (1-3 bullets, user-facing language)\n- Why it was needed\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] How to verify the change works\n- [ ] Edge cases to check\n- [ ] Regression check\n\n## Related\nCloses #<issue>\nSpec: <link to spec doc>\n```\n\n## Voice\n\nSummary bullets first, test plan as a checklist — never a prose recap of the diff. Lead with the conclusion (why this matters to a reviewer), not a chronology of what was touched. Active voice; if a sentence keeps running, split it rather than trimming words to make it fit. No banned words (*delve, leverage, seamless, robust, elevate, foster, unlock, empower, testament, pivotal, showcase, meticulous, game-changer, utilize*). Full standard: `shared/references/docs-voice.md`.\n\nWhen triaging or drafting comments on someone else's PR, prefix intent: `praise:` `nitpick:` `suggestion:` `issue:` `question:` (Conventional Comments), or `Nit:` / `Optional:` / `FYI:` (Google style) — pick one vocabulary and stay consistent.\n\n## PR Review Checklist\n\nWhen reviewing a PR:\n- Does the change match the linked spec/requirement?\n- Are tests present for each acceptance criterion?\n- Are breaking changes documented in the changeset?\n- Is the commit history clean (conventional commits, no \"WIP\" merges)?\n\n## gh CLI Commands\n\n```bash\n# Create PR\ngh pr create --title \"feat(ranger): add cross-language recon agent\" --body \"$(cat body.md)\"\n\n# List open PRs\ngh pr list\n\n# View PR diff\ngh pr diff <number>\n\n# Check PR status\ngh pr status\n\n# Review a PR\ngh pr review <number> --approve\ngh pr review <number> --request-changes --body \"...\"\n\n# Merge\ngh pr merge <number> --squash --delete-branch\n\n# Link issue to PR\ngh pr create --title \"...\" --body \"Closes #123\"\n```\n\n## Issues\n\n```bash\n# Create issue\ngh issue create --title \"...\" --body \"...\" --label \"bug\"\n\n# List issues\ngh issue list --label \"enhancement\"\n\n# Close issue\ngh issue close <number>\n```\n\n## GitHub Actions Annotations\n\n```\n::error file=src/lib.rs,line=42,col=5::Error message here\n::warning file=src/lib.rs,line=10::Warning message here\n::notice file=src/lib.rs,line=1::Notice message here\n```\n\n## Labels Convention\n\n| Label | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `bug` | Confirmed defect |\n| `enhancement` | New feature or improvement |\n| `breaking` | Breaking change |\n| `needs-spec` | Requires a scribe spec before implementation |\n| `needs-plan` | Requires a navigator plan before implementation |\n| `in-progress` | Actively being worked |\n| `blocked` | Cannot proceed without external resolution |\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nD /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/references/github.md\nD /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1789001457432,"completed_at_ms":1789001459233}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T00:51:00.571Z","ordinal":7118,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a088c6-48bb-7040-a264-83f7cdb1775a","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-c638294b-d274-4993-a6e4-011897a16501","changes":{"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md":{"type":"add","content":"## Summary\n\n<!-- State the outcome and why it matters. Add an important behavioral or architectural decision only when it helps review. -->\n\n-\n\n## Verification\n\n<!-- Record checks already run and their observed results. For an unrun check, state why and what remains unverified. -->\n\n- [ ] `command or inspection` — observed result\n\n## Risk and follow-up\n\n<!-- Remove this section when there are no migrations, compatibility risks, limitations, rollout steps, or intentional deferrals. -->\n\n## Related\n\n<!-- Remove this section when there is no issue, requirement, spec, plan, or changeset to link. -->\n"},"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/references/github.md":{"type":"add","content":"# GitHub Reference\n\n## Pull requests\n\nA PR body gives a reviewer with no prior context enough information to understand the outcome, inspect the risky decisions, and verify the change. Ground it in the live base-branch diff and observed checks.\n\n```markdown\n## Summary\n- Outcome and why it matters\n- Important behavioral or architectural decision, when needed for review\n\n## Verification\n- [x] `exact command or inspection` — observed result\n- [ ] Not run: reason and resulting coverage gap\n\n## Risk and follow-up\n<!-- Include only migrations, compatibility risks, limitations, rollout work, or intentional deferrals. -->\n\n## Related\n<!-- Include only links that exist: issue, requirement, spec, plan, or changeset. -->\n```\n\nOmit empty optional sections and placeholder links. Use enough summary bullets to explain one coherent change; if the bullets reveal independent topics, split the PR or explain why they must ship together.\n\nVerification records evidence already observed. Never turn an unrun check into an unchecked instruction without stating why it was not run and what remains unverified.\n\nCall out breaking behavior under `Risk and follow-up` with the old behavior, new behavior, and required migration.\n\n## Voice\n\n- Lead with user-visible or architectural intent, not a file inventory or development chronology.\n- Use direct, active language and concrete outcomes.\n- State material concerns, evidence, consequence, and confidence without softening blockers or overstating certainty.\n- Keep technical detail that changes approval; link to deeper artifacts instead of copying them.\n- Do not restate the diff.\n\n## Review comments\n\nPrefix intent when it prevents ambiguity. Use one vocabulary consistently:\n\n- Conventional Comments: `praise:`, `nitpick:`, `suggestion:`, `issue:`, `question:`, `thought:`; add `(non-blocking)` when needed.\n- Google style: `Nit:`, `Optional:`, `Consider:`, `FYI:` for non-blocking feedback.\n\nDo not manufacture praise. When a material issue exists, state the problem, cite the evidence, explain the consequence, and mark whether it blocks approval. Recommend one fix only when the constraints make it uniquely correct; otherwise describe the required outcome.\n\n## Review focus\n\n- Does the change satisfy its linked requirement or specification?\n- Does every changed behavior have discriminating evidence at the relevant boundary?\n- Are skipped checks and residual risks explicit?\n- Are breaking changes, migrations, and consumer-facing effects documented?\n- Do shared contracts, generated artifacts, and supported harnesses remain aligned when affected?\n- Does the change contain unrelated scope or unresolved sibling defects?\n\n## `gh` commands\n\n```bash\ngh pr create --title \"feat(ranger): add cross-language audit\" --body-file body.md\ngh pr list\ngh pr diff <number>\ngh pr status\ngh pr review <number> --approve\ngh pr review <number> --request-changes --body-file review.md\ngh pr merge <number> --squash --delete-branch\n```\n\nShow the exact target, title, body, labels, and review text before any remote mutation. Never invent issue links, results, or artifact paths.\n\n## Issues\n\n```bash\ngh issue create --title \"...\" --body-file issue.md --label bug\ngh issue list --label enhancement\ngh issue close <number>\n```\n\n## GitHub Actions annotations\n\n```text\n::error file=src/lib.rs,line=42,col=5::Error message here\n::warning file=src/lib.rs,line=10::Warning message here\n::notice file=src/lib.rs,line=1::Notice message here\n```\n\n## Labels\n\n| Label | Meaning |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `bug` | Confirmed defect |\n| `enhancement` | New capability or improvement |\n| `breaking` | Consumer migration required |\n| `needs-spec` | Specification required before implementation |\n| `needs-plan` | Plan required before implementation |\n| `in-progress` | Active work |\n| `blocked` | External resolution required |\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/references/github.md\nA /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1789001459653,"completed_at_ms":1789001460571}}
