{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T02:38:00.709Z","ordinal":7130,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0c3176283919dd68016aa217faa25887d09c741772daebc6cf","status":"completed","call_id":"call_QAvX0mUJzgLIVXlQbF4MkPqo","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/references/conventional-commits.md\\n@@\\n ## Voice\\n \\n-Active voice, imperative mood. If a sentence keeps running, it's usually doing two jobs — split it rather than trimming words to make it fit. No banned words: *delve, leverage, seamless, robust, elevate, foster, unlock, empower, testament, pivotal, showcase, meticulous, game-changer, utilize* (use \\\"use\\\"). Full standard: `shared/references/docs-voice.md`.\\n+Use active voice and imperative mood. Name the technical outcome in the subject and explain only the non-obvious reason in the body. Remove adjectives that stand in for mechanism or evidence. Full standard: `shared/references/docs-voice.md`.\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/references/changesets.md\\n@@\\n ## Voice\\n \\n-Separate *what changed* (factual) from *why* (one clause) — don't blend them. Detail scales with `semver_impact`: `patch`/`internal-only` gets one clause, `minor` gets one sentence plus an optional one-clause why, `major` requires each `breaking_changes` entry to state old behavior → new behavior → what the caller does about it. No banned words (*delve, leverage, seamless, robust, elevate, foster, unlock, empower, testament, pivotal, showcase, meticulous, game-changer, utilize*). Full standard: `shared/references/docs-voice.md`.\\n+Lead with observable consumer impact. Include the reason only when it changes understanding or action. Detail follows impact: a small fix may need one clause; a new capability needs enough context to use it; every breaking entry states old behavior, new behavior, and required action. Remove implementation detail and adjectives that do not help the consumer. Full standard: `shared/references/docs-voice.md`.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a088c6-48bb-7040-a264-83f7cdb1775a","create_time":1789007860.279731}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T02:38:00.783Z","ordinal":7131,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a088c6-48bb-7040-a264-83f7cdb1775a","session_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","root_turn_id":"01a088c6-48bb-7040-a264-83f7cdb1775a","response_id":"resp_0c3176283919dd68016aa217f39df087d08859e1638c366b5b","usage":{"input_tokens":187129,"cached_input_tokens":10880,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":552,"reasoning_output_tokens":109,"total_tokens":187681},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2494800,"cached_input_tokens":2287744,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":10484,"reasoning_output_tokens":4681,"total_tokens":2505284},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":106504669,"cached_input_tokens":104312832,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":477860,"reasoning_output_tokens":157336,"total_tokens":106982529}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T02:38:00.958Z","ordinal":7132,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a088c6-48bb-7040-a264-83f7cdb1775a","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-32593b4b-abfc-4713-bc63-bedf051ffb94","changes":{"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/references/conventional-commits.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -45,3 +45,3 @@\n \n-Active voice, imperative mood. If a sentence keeps running, it's usually doing two jobs — split it rather than trimming words to make it fit. No banned words: *delve, leverage, seamless, robust, elevate, foster, unlock, empower, testament, pivotal, showcase, meticulous, game-changer, utilize* (use \"use\"). Full standard: `shared/references/docs-voice.md`.\n+Use active voice and imperative mood. Name the technical outcome in the subject and explain only the non-obvious reason in the body. Remove adjectives that stand in for mechanism or evidence. Full standard: `shared/references/docs-voice.md`.\n \n","move_path":null},"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/references/changesets.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -49,3 +49,3 @@\n \n-Separate *what changed* (factual) from *why* (one clause) — don't blend them. Detail scales with `semver_impact`: `patch`/`internal-only` gets one clause, `minor` gets one sentence plus an optional one-clause why, `major` requires each `breaking_changes` entry to state old behavior → new behavior → what the caller does about it. No banned words (*delve, leverage, seamless, robust, elevate, foster, unlock, empower, testament, pivotal, showcase, meticulous, game-changer, utilize*). Full standard: `shared/references/docs-voice.md`.\n+Lead with observable consumer impact. Include the reason only when it changes understanding or action. Detail follows impact: a small fix may need one clause; a new capability needs enough context to use it; every breaking entry states old behavior, new behavior, and required action. Remove implementation detail and adjectives that do not help the consumer. Full standard: `shared/references/docs-voice.md`.\n \n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/references/conventional-commits.md\nM /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/references/changesets.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1789007880838,"completed_at_ms":1789007880958}}
