{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T02:42:53.635Z","ordinal":7212,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0c3176283919dd68016aa219213d9487d09948c99f7b317056","status":"completed","call_id":"call_YpVHGOTMdu7VySwqZqYvSYaQ","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Delete File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/references/mcp-protocol.md\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/README.md\\n@@\\n-| `typescript-tooling.md` | TS test commands (Stryker, Vitest), non-negotiables | mutator, remediator |\\n+| `typescript-tooling.md` | Risk-based TypeScript/JavaScript verification capabilities and conditional quality checks | mutator, remediator |\\n@@\\n-| `mcp-protocol.md` | MCP server lifecycle, tool definition format, A2A AgentCard | — |\\n-| `modern-cli-tools.md` | ripgrep, fd, bat, jq, delta, fzf usage patterns | — |\\n-| `interface-implementers.md` | Deterministic pre-scan for enumerating trait/interface implementers per language | challenger |\\n-| `boundary-value-shapes.md` | Sum-type-over-bool default posture for boundary-crossing values, per-language examples | implementer |\\n+| `modern-cli-tools.md` | Capability-aware preferences for search, inspection, structured data, Git, and GitHub | — |\\n+| `interface-implementers.md` | Evidence-led implementer coverage across Rust, TypeScript/JavaScript, Python, and Go | challenger |\\n+| `boundary-value-shapes.md` | Cross-language state modeling for absent, invalid, stale, or failed boundary values | implementer |\\n@@\\n-| `docs-voice.md` | Reader-focused prose and review-label conventions | Courier authoring references |\\n+| `docs-voice.md` | Audience-aware, succinct, friendly, and radically candid writing guidance | Courier authoring references |\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a088c6-48bb-7040-a264-83f7cdb1775a","create_time":1789008158.122192}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T02:42:53.690Z","ordinal":7213,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a088c6-48bb-7040-a264-83f7cdb1775a","session_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","root_turn_id":"01a088c6-48bb-7040-a264-83f7cdb1775a","response_id":"resp_0c3176283919dd68016aa2191cec9887d0aac1f3e8c04b4e56","usage":{"input_tokens":196417,"cached_input_tokens":195328,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":428,"reasoning_output_tokens":34,"total_tokens":196845},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":4425051,"cached_input_tokens":4206848,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":18657,"reasoning_output_tokens":5665,"total_tokens":4443708},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":108434920,"cached_input_tokens":106231936,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":486033,"reasoning_output_tokens":158320,"total_tokens":108920953}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T02:42:53.844Z","ordinal":7214,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a088c6-48bb-7040-a264-83f7cdb1775a","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-f8105d4f-6956-4167-96f8-20b3f9793b55","changes":{"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/references/mcp-protocol.md":{"type":"delete","content":"# MCP Protocol Reference\n\nModel Context Protocol (MCP) is the cross-platform protocol for exposing tools and resources to LLMs. Both Claude Code and Google ADK/AGY support MCP natively.\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n**Tool:** A function the LLM can call. Has a name, description, and JSON Schema input spec.\n**Resource:** A readable artifact (file, URL, database record) the LLM can fetch.\n**Prompt:** A template the LLM can use to pre-fill a message.\n\n## Server Lifecycle\n\n```\n1. initialize    → server declares protocol version + capabilities\n2. initialized   → client acknowledges\n3. tools/list    → client fetches available tools\n4. tools/call    → client invokes a tool by name with JSON arguments\n5. (resources/list, prompts/list as needed)\n```\n\n## Tool Definition\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"sentinel_verify\",\n  \"description\": \"Verify an artifact against its criteria. Returns a verdict@3 schema.\",\n  \"inputSchema\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"required\": [\"artifact_type\", \"artifact_path\", \"criteria\"],\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"artifact_type\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"artifact_path\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"criteria\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## CallToolResult Shape\n\n```json\n{\n  \"content\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"text\": \"Rendered output for the assistant\",\n      \"annotations\": { \"audience\": [\"assistant\"] }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"isError\": false,\n  \"structuredContent\": { \"verdict\": \"pass\", \"confidence\": \"high\", \"...\" }\n}\n```\n\n`structuredContent` is the typed machine-readable result. `content[0].text` is the human-readable render. Never duplicate content between them — they serve different consumers.\n\n## A2A AgentCard\n\nFor cross-service discovery, plugins publish an AgentCard at `/.well-known/agent.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"sentinel\",\n  \"description\": \"Cross-cutting verification gate for the Wisp Plugins ecosystem\",\n  \"url\": \"https://plugins.orin.dev/sentinel\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"capabilities\": {\n    \"streaming\": false,\n    \"pushNotifications\": false\n  },\n  \"skills\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"verify-spec\",\n      \"name\": \"Verify Spec\",\n      \"description\": \"Verify a spec@1 artifact against its acceptance criteria\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Trust Boundaries\n\nPlugin output always goes in `tool_result` blocks, JSON-encoded. Never elevate plugin output into the system prompt context without sanitization. If a tool's output could contain injected instructions, JSON-encode it before including in messages.\n\n## Claude Code vs ADK\n\n| Concern | Claude Code | ADK |\n|---|---|---|\n| MCP server config | `~/.claude/mcp.json` or `.mcp.json` | `McpToolset(server_params=...)` |\n| Tool invocation | Native MCP client | `McpToolset.from_server()` |\n| Subagent invocation | `--subagent` flag or Agent tool | `Agent(sub_agents=[...])` |\n| Cross-platform | MCP tools work on both | MCP tools work on both |\n"},"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/README.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -301,3 +301,3 @@\n | `typescript-smells.md` | TS architectural smells and interface/type designs | architect, Smith reviewer |\n-| `typescript-tooling.md` | TS test commands (Stryker, Vitest), non-negotiables | mutator, remediator |\n+| `typescript-tooling.md` | Risk-based TypeScript/JavaScript verification capabilities and conditional quality checks | mutator, remediator |\n | `typescript.md` | Thin index → routes to the files above | — |\n@@ -318,6 +318,5 @@\n | `changesets.md` | Changeset vs commit distinction, semver decision guide | courier |\n-| `mcp-protocol.md` | MCP server lifecycle, tool definition format, A2A AgentCard | — |\n-| `modern-cli-tools.md` | ripgrep, fd, bat, jq, delta, fzf usage patterns | — |\n-| `interface-implementers.md` | Deterministic pre-scan for enumerating trait/interface implementers per language | challenger |\n-| `boundary-value-shapes.md` | Sum-type-over-bool default posture for boundary-crossing values, per-language examples | implementer |\n+| `modern-cli-tools.md` | Capability-aware preferences for search, inspection, structured data, Git, and GitHub | — |\n+| `interface-implementers.md` | Evidence-led implementer coverage across Rust, TypeScript/JavaScript, Python, and Go | challenger |\n+| `boundary-value-shapes.md` | Cross-language state modeling for absent, invalid, stale, or failed boundary values | implementer |\n | `implementation-review.md` | Routes implementation review to language hazards, architecture smells, and comment rules | Smith reviewer |\n@@ -326,3 +325,3 @@\n | `workspace-conventions.md` | Persisted spec, plan, and architecture-model locations | recon and coverage auditors |\n-| `docs-voice.md` | Reader-focused prose and review-label conventions | Courier authoring references |\n+| `docs-voice.md` | Audience-aware, succinct, friendly, and radically candid writing guidance | Courier authoring references |\n | `orin-visual-standard.md` | Shared Mermaid palette and diagram conventions | documentation authors |\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/README.md\nD /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/references/mcp-protocol.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1789008173699,"completed_at_ms":1789008173844}}
