{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T02:51:12.515Z","ordinal":7364,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a088c6-48bb-7040-a264-83f7cdb1775a","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0c3176283919dd68016aa21b1e2fa487d092b9df839521b7f4","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The reference rewrite exposes a real runtime behavior change, not just editorial cleanup: every Claude agent now has the candor invariant, and several Courier/Mason workflows changed their decisions and output contracts. I’m treating that as a patch release across all plugins so the manifests honestly identify the behavior users receive."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1789008670210,"completed_at_ms":1789008672515}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T02:51:12.518Z","ordinal":7365,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0c3176283919dd68016aa21b1e2fa487d092b9df839521b7f4","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The reference rewrite exposes a real runtime behavior change, not just editorial cleanup: every Claude agent now has the candor invariant, and several Courier/Mason workflows changed their decisions and output contracts. I’m treating that as a patch release across all plugins so the manifests honestly identify the behavior users receive."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a088c6-48bb-7040-a264-83f7cdb1775a","create_time":1789008662.676932,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T02:51:56.252Z","ordinal":7366,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0c3176283919dd68016aa21b2069bc87d0a832e42f97608f4b","status":"completed","call_id":"call_aCLuRjhE7dUPBRHH8IWjiwVG","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/CHANGELOG.md\\n@@\\n Individual plugin changelogs live in `plugins/<plugin-id>/CHANGELOG.md`.\\n+\\n+## [4.4.1] - 2026-09-09 — Direct, evidence-led guidance\\n+\\n+- Added a shared radical-candor rule: report material concerns with evidence, consequence, and calibrated confidence; do not soften blockers or manufacture praise.\\n+- Reframed runtime references around outcomes, applicability, confirming and refuting evidence, and explicit dispositions. Ordered procedures remain only where sequence affects correctness.\\n+- Reworked Rust and TypeScript hazard, architecture, and tooling references to avoid universal style rules and predetermined designs; aligned Python and Go packs with the same evidence standard.\\n+- Updated Courier's PR guidance and GitHub template to report observed verification, disclose gaps, and omit empty ceremony.\\n+- Updated Mason to scaffold and audit reference quality, cross-language claims, and candid evidence.\\n+- Added a non-blocking density warning for references over 800 words while retaining the 120-line hard cap.\\n \\n ## [4.4.0] - 2026-09-09 — Evidence-depth and behavioral evaluation\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/courier/CHANGELOG.md\\n@@\\n — courier\\n+\\n+## [3.0.2] - 2026-09-09\\n+\\n+### Changed\\n+- PR guidance now reports observed verification and unresolved gaps, omits empty sections, and separates independent topics.\\n+- Agents state material concerns directly with evidence, consequence, and calibrated confidence.\\n \\n ## [3.0.1] - 2026-09-09\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/mason/CHANGELOG.md\\n@@\\n — mason\\n+\\n+## [3.2.1] - 2026-09-09\\n+\\n+### Changed\\n+- Scaffolding and audits now assess runtime references by outcome, applicability, confirming and refuting evidence, and disposition.\\n+- Cross-language claims must cover each named language or disclose the gap; agents also apply the shared radical-candor rule.\\n \\n ## [3.2.0] - 2026-09-09\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/muse/CHANGELOG.md\\n@@\\n — muse\\n+\\n+## [1.0.1] - 2026-09-09\\n+\\n+### Changed\\n+- Agents now report material concerns directly with evidence, consequence, and calibrated confidence.\\n \\n ## [1.0.0] - 2026-08-27\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/navigator/CHANGELOG.md\\n@@\\n — navigator\\n+\\n+## [2.3.1] - 2026-09-09\\n+\\n+### Changed\\n+- Agents now report material concerns directly with evidence, consequence, and calibrated confidence.\\n+- Implementer discovery guidance now covers Rust, TypeScript/JavaScript, Python, and Go without assuming a language-specific abstraction.\\n \\n ## [2.3.0] - 2026-09-02\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/CHANGELOG.md\\n@@\\n — ranger\\n+\\n+## [3.2.1] - 2026-09-09\\n+\\n+### Changed\\n+- Hazard references now distinguish candidate signals from confirmation and refutation across Rust, TypeScript/JavaScript, Python, and Go.\\n+- Agents apply the shared radical-candor rule; style preferences no longer masquerade as verified defects.\\n \\n ## [3.2.0] - 2026-09-09\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/scribe/CHANGELOG.md\\n@@\\n — scribe\\n+\\n+## [3.3.1] - 2026-09-09\\n+\\n+### Changed\\n+- Architecture-smell guidance now starts from live responsibilities and invariants, tests competing explanations, and leaves implementation shape open unless evidence constrains it.\\n+- Agents state structural concerns directly with evidence, consequence, and calibrated confidence.\\n \\n ## [3.3.0] - 2026-09-09\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/sentinel/CHANGELOG.md\\n@@\\n — sentinel\\n+\\n+## [2.1.1] - 2026-09-09\\n+\\n+### Changed\\n+- Agents now report blockers and material concerns directly with evidence, consequence, and calibrated confidence.\\n \\n ## [2.1.0] - 2026-09-09\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/smith/CHANGELOG.md\\n@@\\n — smith\\n+\\n+## [2.4.1] - 2026-09-09\\n+\\n+### Changed\\n+- Language tooling and boundary guidance now selects project-native capabilities by risk and records confirming, refuting, and missing evidence.\\n+- Rust and TypeScript guidance no longer treats style preferences or predetermined designs as universal requirements; agents also apply the shared radical-candor rule.\\n \\n ## [2.4.0] - 2026-09-09\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/vanguard/CHANGELOG.md\\n@@\\n — vanguard\\n+\\n+## [2.0.1] - 2026-09-09\\n+\\n+### Changed\\n+- Agents now report material concerns directly with evidence, consequence, and calibrated confidence.\\n \\n ## [2.0.0] - 2026-08-27\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/weaver/CHANGELOG.md\\n@@\\n — weaver\\n+\\n+## [3.0.2] - 2026-09-09\\n+\\n+### Changed\\n+- Agents now report requirement gaps and material concerns directly with evidence, consequence, and calibrated confidence.\\n \\n ## [3.0.1] - 2026-09-02\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a088c6-48bb-7040-a264-83f7cdb1775a","create_time":1789008662.676932}}}
