 plan batches, verifies risk at real boundaries, searches semantic defect siblings, and escalates shared model or architecture gaps.\"\n     },\n     {\n       \"id\": \"courier\",\n       \"name\": \"courier\",\n-      \"version\": \"3.0.1\",\n+      \"version\": \"3.0.2\",\n       \"path\": \"./plugins/courier\",\n       \"description\": \"Shipping plugin. Shepherds completed code through commit, PR creation, review response, and changeset documentation. Skills: commit, pr, changeset, receive-feedback, post-review, release.\"\n     }\n  +11 -11\n\nplugins/courier/skills/pr/SKILL.md\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n name: pr\n description: >-\n   Trigger when the user asks to open a PR or write a PR description: \"open a PR\", \"create a pull request\", \"write the PR description\". Given a diff, a linked spec, and a linked requirement, produces a PR title and body a reviewer with zero context can act on, then opens the PR via `gh pr create` after user confirmation.\n-version: 2.0.0\n+version: 2.0.1\n ---\n \n # Courier — PR\n@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@ Produces a PR title and body from a diff plus optional linked spec/requirement,\n </dispatch>\n \n <references>\n-`shared/references/github.md` — PR template, label conventions, `gh` commands, and the voice standard for this artifact (summary bullets first, test plan as a checklist).\n+`shared/references/github.md` — outcome-led PR structure, observed verification, risk disclosure, review voice, labels, and `gh` commands.\n </references>\n \n <io>\n  +2 -2\n\nplugins/navigator/plugin.json\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n {\n   \"id\": \"navigator\",\n   \"name\": \"navigator\",\n-  \"version\": \"2.3.0\",\n+  \"version\": \"2.3.1\",\n   \"description\": \"Planning plugin. Decomposes specs into sequenced, bite-sized implementation plans with an implementation approach, exact code as a baseline, and the tests proving each criterion — no write-test-first mandate. Tasks are sized to compilation boundaries, not a clock-time estimate. No TBDs. A developer with zero domain context can execute the plan mechanically.\",\n   \"author\": {\n     \"name\": \"Gabriel Castro\",\n@@ -19,4 +19,4 @@\n   \"produces\": [\n     \"plan@1\"\n   ]\n-}\n+}\n  +2 -2\n\nplugins/vanguard/plugin.json\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n {\n   \"id\": \"vanguard\",\n   \"name\": \"vanguard\",\n-  \"version\": \"2.0.0\",\n+  \"version\": \"2.0.1\",\n   \"description\": \"Research plugin. Investigates questions and requirements to build a documented evidence base before committing to a solution direction. Distinguishes confirmed findings from assumptions. Produces research-report@1 for consumption by scribe (spec).\",\n   \"author\": {\n     \"name\": \"Gabriel Castro\",\n@@ -20,4 +20,4 @@\n   \"produces\": [\n     \"research-report@1\"\n   ]\n-}\n+}\n  +2 -2\n\nplugins/weaver/plugin.json\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n {\n   \"id\": \"weaver\",\n   \"name\": \"weaver\",\n-  \"version\": \"3.0.1\",\n+  \"version\": \"3.0.2\",\n   \"description\": \"Need definition plugin. Captures and structures requirements before implementation begins. Integrates with GitHub Issues by default; extensible to any issue tracker that produces the requirement@1 schema. Skills: capture-need, clarify-requirement, prioritize-backlog, connect-requirement, audit-backlog.\",\n   \"author\": {\n     \"name\": \"Gabriel Castro\",\n@@ -18,4 +18,4 @@\n   \"produces\": [\n     \"requirement@1\"\n   ]\n-}\n+}\n  +2 -2\n"},"started_at_ms":1789009076784,"completed_at_ms":1789009076784}}
