{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T02:57:56.824Z","ordinal":7631,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a08940-2258-72b1-ab71-e1687d3a13cb","call_id":"call_wMwxB2NJCyOuk0f5Sw5yguqZ","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"harnesses/codex/plugins/courier/skills/pr/SKILL.md | 13 +++++++++----\n marketplace.json                                   | 22 +++++++++++-----------\n plugins/courier/skills/pr/SKILL.md                 |  4 ++--\n plugins/navigator/plugin.json                      |  4 ++--\n plugins/vanguard/plugin.json                       |  4 ++--\n plugins/weaver/plugin.json                         |  4 ++--\n 6 files changed, 28 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)\n\nChanges:\n\nharnesses/codex/plugins/courier/skills/pr/SKILL.md\n@@ -3,6 +3,8 @@ name: pr\n description: Draft or open a reviewer-ready pull request from verified work. Use when the user asks to create a PR or write its description; require confirmation before any remote action.\n ---\n \n+State material concerns, evidence, consequence, and confidence directly. Do not soften blockers, manufacture praise, or claim certainty beyond the evidence.\n+\n # Open a reviewable pull request\n \n Ground the PR in the actual branch diff, target branch, linked lifecycle artifacts, and executed verification. A reviewer should be able to understand the intent, evidence, and residual risk without reconstructing the branch history.\n@@ -18,10 +20,13 @@ Ground the PR in the actual branch diff, target branch, linked lifecycle artifac\n \n Write a concise title and body with:\n \n-- Summary of user-visible or architectural intent.\n-- Scope and non-scope.\n-- Evidence: criteria, tests, and relevant paths.\n-- Risks, migration notes, or follow-up work.\n+- An outcome-led summary of user-visible or architectural intent.\n+- Observed verification with exact commands or inspections and results.\n+- Reasons and coverage gaps for checks not run.\n+- Risks, migrations, limitations, or follow-up only when they apply.\n+- Existing issue, requirement, spec, plan, or changeset links only when they help review.\n+\n+Use enough summary bullets to explain one coherent change. If the summary reveals independent topics, recommend separate PRs or state the dependency that requires one delivery.\n \n Show the exact title, body, labels, base branch, and repository target before creating anything remotely. Create the PR only after explicit user confirmation.\n \n  +9 -4\n\nmarketplace.json\n@@ -1,13 +1,13 @@\n {\n   \"$schema\": \"https://antigravity.google/schemas/marketplace.json\",\n   \"name\": \"wisp-plugins\",\n-  \"version\": \"4.4.0\",\n+  \"version\": \"4.4.1\",\n   \"description\": \"Wisp Plugins marketplace for AGY and Claude Code, published by Orin DX\",\n   \"plugins\": [\n     {\n       \"id\": \"mason\",\n       \"name\": \"mason\",\n-      \"version\": \"3.2.0\",\n+      \"version\": \"3.2.1\",\n       \"path\": \"./plugins/mason\",\n       \"description\": \"Build, audit, and behaviorally evaluate plugins; design shared schemas and scaffold conformant agents. Skills: scaffold-plugin, audit-plugin, design-schema, scaffold-subagent, evaluate.\",\n       \"supersedes\": \"agent-plugin-builder\"\n@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@\n     {\n       \"id\": \"ranger\",\n       \"name\": \"ranger\",\n-      \"version\": \"3.2.0\",\n+      \"version\": \"3.2.1\",\n       \"path\": \"./plugins/ranger\",\n       \"description\": \"Bug hunting for Rust, TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, and Go. Confirms reachable defects, searches semantic siblings, and routes structural families for architectural correction.\",\n       \"supersedes\": [\n@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@\n     {\n       \"id\": \"sentinel\",\n       \"name\": \"sentinel\",\n-      \"version\": \"2.1.0\",\n+      \"version\": \"2.1.1\",\n       \"path\": \"./plugins/sentinel\",\n       \"description\": \"Cross-cutting verification gate. Confirms that any stage artifact meets its criteria before the next stage begins. One skill, one recon-verify-judge pipeline, reused unchanged against any artifact type.\",\n       \"supersedes\": \"verify-first\"\n@@ -34,49 +34,49 @@\n     {\n       \"id\": \"weaver\",\n       \"name\": \"weaver\",\n-      \"version\": \"3.0.1\",\n+      \"version\": \"3.0.2\",\n       \"path\": \"./plugins/weaver\",\n       \"description\": \"Need definition plugin. Captures and structures requirements before implementation begins. Integrates with GitHub Issues by default; extensible to Linear, Jira, or any issue tracker that produces the requirement@1 schema. Skills: capture-need, clarify-requirement, prioritize-backlog, connect-requirement, audit-backlog.\"\n     },\n     {\n       \"id\": \"vanguard\",\n       \"name\": \"vanguard\",\n-      \"version\": \"2.0.0\",\n+      \"version\": \"2.0.1\",\n       \"path\": \"./plugins/vanguard\",\n       \"description\": \"Research plugin. Investigates questions and requirements to build a documented evidence base before committing to a solution direction. Produces research-report@1 for consumption by scribe (spec).\"\n     },\n     {\n       \"id\": \"scribe\",\n       \"name\": \"scribe\",\n-      \"version\": \"3.3.0\",\n+      \"version\": \"3.3.1\",\n       \"path\": \"./plugins/scribe\",\n       \"description\": \"Specification plugin. Turns requirements and research reports into unambiguous, testable specs. Checks specs against a persisted whole-system architecture model. Detects spec drift against actual code. Skills: draft-spec, verify-spec, spec-drift, audit-spec, audit-architecture, gate-spec, correct-spec, architect.\"\n     },\n     {\n       \"id\": \"muse\",\n       \"name\": \"muse\",\n-      \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n+      \"version\": \"1.0.1\",\n       \"path\": \"./plugins/muse\",\n       \"description\": \"Component specification plugin. Turns UI/design intent into unambiguous, testable component specs \\u2014 props, variants, per-state behavior, and accessibility criteria as testable propositions, gated before planning. Audits the spec, not the implementation \\u2014 see ranger's accessibility hazard taxonomy for code-level scanning.\"\n     },\n     {\n       \"id\": \"navigator\",\n       \"name\": \"navigator\",\n-      \"version\": \"2.3.0\",\n+      \"version\": \"2.3.1\",\n       \"path\": \"./plugins/navigator\",\n       \"description\": \"Planning plugin. Decomposes specs into sequenced, bite-sized implementation plans with an implementation approach, exact code as a baseline, and the tests proving each criterion \\u2014 no write-test-first mandate. Tasks are sized to compilation boundaries, not a clock-time estimate. No TBDs. A developer with zero domain context can execute the plan mechanically.\"\n     },\n     {\n       \"id\": \"smith\",\n       \"name\": \"smith\",\n-      \"version\": \"2.4.0\",\n+      \"version\": \"2.4.1\",\n       \"path\": \"./plugins/smith\",\n       \"description\": \"Implementation plugin. Executes tested plan batches, verifies risk at real boundaries, searches semantic defect siblings, and escalates shared model or architecture gaps.\"\n     },\n     {\n       \"id\": \"courier\",\n       \"name\": \"courier\",\n-      \"version\": \"3.0.1\",\n+      \"version\": \"3.0.2\",\n       \"path\": \"./plugins/courier\",\n       \"description\": \"Shipping plugin. Shepherds completed code through commit, PR creation, review response, and changeset documentation. Skills: commit, pr, changeset, receive-feedback, post-review, release.\"\n     }\n  +11 -11\n\nplugins/courier/skills/pr/SKILL.md\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n name: pr\n description: >-\n   Trigger when the user asks to open a PR or write a PR description: \"open a PR\", \"create a pull request\", \"write the PR description\". Given a diff, a linked spec, and a linked requirement, produces a PR title and body a reviewer with zero context can act on, then opens the PR via `gh pr create` after user confirmation