s/intake.md                    |   1 +\n plugins/weaver/agents/prioritizer.md               |   1 +\n plugins/weaver/plugin.json                         |   4 +-\n scripts/check-reference-size.sh                    |  21 ++-\n shared/agent-best-practices.md                     |  21 +++\n shared/constitution.md                             |   8 ++\n shared/references/boundary-value-shapes.md         |  81 ++++-------\n shared/references/changesets.md                    | 135 ++++++++----------\n shared/references/conventional-commits.md          |   2 +-\n shared/references/docs-voice.md                    |  64 +++++----\n shared/references/github.md                        | 106 +++++++-------\n shared/references/go-hazards-t7-t10.md             |   2 +\n shared/references/go-hazards.md                    |   2 +\n shared/references/go-smells.md                     |   2 +\n shared/references/interface-implementers.md        |  46 ++++---\n shared/references/mcp-protocol.md                  |  92 -------------\n shared/references/modern-cli-tools.md              |  94 +++++--------\n shared/references/python-hazards-t7-t10.md         |   2 +\n shared/references/python-hazards.md                |   2 +\n shared/references/python-smells.md                 |   2 +\n shared/references/rust-hazards-t7-t10.md           |  83 ++++-------\n shared/references/rust-hazards.md                  | 132 +++++++-----------\n shared/references/rust-smells.md                   | 110 +++------------\n shared/references/rust-tooling.md                  |  58 ++++----\n shared/references/rust.md                          |   2 +-\n shared/references/typescript-hazards-t7-t10.md     |  84 ++++-------\n shared/references/typescript-hazards.md            | 153 ++++++++-------------\n shared/references/typescript-smells.md             |  84 ++++-------\n shared/references/typescript-tooling.md            |  51 ++++---\n shared/references/typescript.md                    |   2 +-\n shared/references/workspace-conventions.md         |  30 ++--\n 231 files changed, 1532 insertions(+), 2082 deletions(-)\n\ncf27386 docs: refresh Mermaid diagrams and visual standard\nc9e474a feat(ecosystem): release evidence-aware verification (#8)\n47239f2 feat(ecosystem): add defect-family review and concise guidance (#7)\n863c522 Merge pull request #6 from orin-dx/feat/codex-marketplace-and-cross-harness-authoring\n21f7e90 fix(codex): discover marketplace from git root\n60e226e Merge pull request #5 from orin-dx/feat/codex-marketplace-and-cross-harness-authoring\ne4bbda4 feat(ecosystem): Codex marketplace, cross-harness authoring, Wisp Plugins rebrand\n68762c6 Merge pull request #4 from orin-dx/docs/wisp-plugins-brand\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":2292},"formatted_output":"# Conventional Commits Reference\n\n**Format:** `<type>(<scope>): <description>`\n\nTypes: `feat` `fix` `docs` `style` `refactor` `test` `chore` `perf` `ci` `build` `revert`\n\nBreaking change: append `!` after type/scope, or add `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer.\n\n## Rules\n\n- Subject line: imperative mood, no period, under 72 characters\n- Body (optional): explain the *why*, not the what. Do not artificially wrap lines — one paragraph per line, let the terminal/renderer soft-wrap.\n- Footer: `BREAKING CHANGE: <description>`, `Fixes #123`, `Refs #456`\n- Scope is optional; when used, it names the module or component\n\n## Examples\n\n```\nfeat(courier): add changeset generation skill\n\nfix(sentinel): retry gate passes specific failure message to producer\n\ndocs(shared): add conventional-commits reference\n\nrefactor(ranger): extract language detection into recon subagent\n\nfeat!: rename bug-hunter-rust to proof\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: plugin ID changed from bug-hunter-rust to proof.\nUpdate marketplace.json and skill trigger references.\n\nfeat!: rename proof to ranger\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: plugin ID changed from proof to ranger.\nUpdate marketplace.json and skill trigger references.\n```\n\n## Commit Message Body\n\nThe body answers: why was this change needed? What problem does it solve?\n\nDon't describe what the code does (the diff shows that). Write what a reviewer needs to understand the intent.\n\n## Voice\n\nUse active voice and imperative mood. Name the technical outcome in the subject and explain only the non-obvious reason in the body. Remove adjectives that stand in for mechanism or evidence. Full standard: `shared/references/docs-voice.md`.\n\n## Scope Conventions (this repo)\n\n| Scope | Covers |\n|---|---|\n| `sentinel` | sentinel plugin and subagents |\n| `ranger` | ranger plugin and subagents |\n| `courier` | courier plugin and subagents |\n| `weaver` | weaver plugin and subagents |\n| `scribe` | scribe plugin and subagents |\n| `vanguard` | vanguard plugin and subagents |\n| `navigator` | navigator plugin and subagents |\n| `smith` | smith plugin and subagents |\n| `mason` | mason plugin and subagents |\n| `muse` | muse plugin and subagents |\n| `shared` | shared schemas, references, agent-best-practices |\n* fix/evidence-led-agent-guidance\nM  .github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md\nM  AGENTS.md\nM  ARCHITECTURE.md\nM  CHANGELOG.md\nM  CONTRIBUTING.md\nM  README.md\nM  dist/codex/plugins/courier/.codex-plugin/plugin.json\nM  dist/codex/plugins/courier/agent-roles/README.md\nM  dist/codex/plugins/courier/shared/references/changesets.md\nM  dist/codex/plugins/courier/shared/references/conventional-commits.md\nM  dist/codex/plugins/courier/shared/references/docs-voice.md\nM  dist/codex/plugins/courier/skills/changeset/SKILL.md\nM  dist/codex/plugins/courier/skills/commit/SKILL.md\nM  dist/codex/plugins/courier/skills/post-review/SKILL.md\nM  dist/codex/plugins/courier/skills/pr/SKILL.md\nM  dist/codex/plugins/courier/skills/receive-feedback/SKILL.md\nM  dist/codex/plugins/courier/skills/release/SKILL.md\nM  dist/codex/plugins/mason/.codex-plugin/plugin.json\nM  dist/codex/plugins/mason/agent-roles/README.md\nM  dist/codex/plugins/mason/skills/a