{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T17:48:10.074Z","ordinal":7996,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a08c6c-2bb7-7db0-a8c0-517545c5865e","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0c3176283919dd68016aa2ed4a831c87d0bd67acbd31403fde","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Yes. At 34 files, the flat directory is becoming harder to scan. Organize by cognitive concern first, then language. That matches how agents select references at runtime.\n\n```text\nshared/references/\n├── hazards/\n│   ├── rust.md\n│   ├── rust-boundaries.md\n│   ├── typescript.md\n│   ├── typescript-boundaries.md\n│   ├── python.md\n│   ├── python-boundaries.md\n│   ├── go.md\n│   └── go-boundaries.md\n├── architecture/\n│   ├── rust.md\n│   ├── typescript.md\n│   ├── python.md\n│   ├── go.md\n│   ├── remediation.md\n│   └── boundary-values.md\n├── verification/\n│   ├── rust.md\n│   ├── typescript.md\n│   ├── python.md\n│   ├── go.md\n│   ├── evidence.md\n│   ├── implementation-review.md\n│   └── interface-coverage.md\n├── delivery/\n│   ├── changesets.md\n│   ├── commits.md\n│   └── github.md\n├── authoring/\n│   ├── voice.md\n│   ├── comments.md\n│   └── diagrams.md\n├── evaluation/\n│   └── behavioral.md\n├── workspace/\n│   └── conventions.md\n├── tooling/\n│   └── cli.md\n└── README.md\n```\n\nWhy this pattern:\n\n- It mirrors cognitive modes: scanning, architecture, verification, delivery, and authoring.\n- It keeps references shared across plugins instead of assigning artificial plugin ownership.\n- Exact paths remain self-describing: `hazards/rust.md` is clearer than `rust-hazards.md`.\n- Agents still load one exact file; nesting adds no runtime context.\n- Cross-language comparisons stay easy because equivalent files share a directory.\n\nI would also:\n\n- Replace the four thin language indexes with one human-facing `shared/references/README.md`.\n- Move the 34-row table out of the root README. A directory-level map is less likely to drift.\n- Add a reference-reachability check: every runtime reference must have a prompt or catalog caller; authoring-only references must be declared as such.\n- Reject `misc`, `common`, and plugin-owned reference folders.\n- Keep the tree shallow—two directory levels are enough.\n\nOne important caveat: these paths are runtime dependencies in [harness-authoring.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/harness-authoring.md) and [catalog.json](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/harnesses/codex/catalog.json). Moving them requires updating Claude `<load_first>` blocks, Codex skills, transitive reference links, catalog entries, documentation, and generated distribution artifacts.\n\nI recommend doing the moves in a separate follow-up PR after #9 merges. Against #9’s rewritten files, Git may render many moves as delete/add pairs, making the substantive guidance review much harder.\n\nI also found semantic drift that should be corrected in #9 before merge:\n\n- [agent-best-practices.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/agent-best-practices.md:64) still says 38 agents and promises grep patterns.\n- [ranger README](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/README.md:58) still describes scanner behavior as running predefined grep patterns.\n- [ranger README](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/README.md:149) repeats those outdated reference descriptions.\n- [challenger.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/navigator/agents/challenger.md:19) claims `interface-implementers.md` supplies language-specific grep patterns and a deterministic pre-scan, which the rewritten reference no longer does.\n\nConfidence: high. The concern-first structure follows the repository’s actual loading architecture; the main uncertainty is whether any external consumers treat current reference paths as stable."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1789062474545,"completed_at_ms":1789062490074}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T17:48:10.078Z","ordinal":7997,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0c3176283919dd68016aa2ed4a831c87d0bd67acbd31403fde","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Yes. At 34 files, the flat directory is becoming harder to scan. Organize by cognitive concern first, then language. That matches how agents select references at runtime.\n\n```text\nshared/references/\n├── hazards/\n│   ├── rust.md\n│   ├── rust-boundaries.md\n│   ├── typescript.md\n│   ├── typescript-boundaries.md\n│   ├── python.md\n│   ├── python-boundaries.md\n│   ├── go.md\n│   └── go-boundaries.md\n├── architecture/\n│   ├── rust.md\n│   ├── typescript.md\n│   ├── python.md\n│   ├── go.md\n│   ├── remediation.md\n│   └── boundary-values.md\n├── verification/\n│   ├── rust.md\n│   ├── typescript.md\n│   ├── python.md\n│   ├── go.md\n│   ├── evidence.md\n│   ├── implementation-review.md\n│   └── interface-coverage.md\n├── delivery/\n│   ├── changesets.md\n│   ├── commits.md\n│   └── github.md\n├── authoring/\n│   ├── voice.md\n│   ├── comments.md\n│   └── diagrams.md\n├── evaluation/\n│   └── behavioral.md\n├── workspace/\n│   └── conventions.md\n├── tooling/\n│   └── cli.md\n└── README.md\n```\n\nWhy this pattern:\n\n- It mirrors cognitive modes: scanning, architecture, verification, delivery, and authoring.\n- It keeps references shared across plugins instead of assigning artificial plugin ownership.\n- Exact paths remain self-describing: `hazards/rust.md` is clearer than `rust-hazards.md`.\n- Agents still load one exact file; nesting adds no runtime context.\n- Cross-language comparisons stay easy because equivalent files share a directory.\n\nI would also:\n\n- Replace the four thin language indexes with one human-facing `shared/references/README.md`.\n- Move the 34-row table out of the root README. A directory-level map is less likely to drift.\n- Add a reference-reachability check: every runtime reference must have a prompt or catalog caller; authoring-only references must be declared as such.\n- Reject `misc`, `common`, and plugin-owned reference folders.\n- Keep the tree shallow—two directory levels are enough.\n\nOne important caveat: these paths are runtime dependencies in [harness-authoring.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/harness-authoring.md) and [catalog.json](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/harnesses/codex/catalog.json). Moving them requires updating Claude `<load_first>` blocks, Codex skills, transitive reference links, catalog entries, documentation, and generated distribution artifacts.\n\nI recommend doing the moves in a separate follow-up PR after #9 merges. Against #9’s rewritten files, Git may render many moves as delete/add pairs, making the substantive guidance review much harder.\n\nI also found semantic drift that should be corrected in #9 before merge:\n\n- [agent-best-practices.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/agent-best-practices.md:64) still says 38 agents and promises grep patterns.\n- [ranger README](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/README.md:58) still describes scanner behavior as running predefined grep patterns.\n- [ranger README](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/README.md:149) repeats those outdated reference descriptions.\n- [challenger.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/navigator/agents/challenger.md:19) claims `interface-implementers.md` supplies language-specific grep patterns and a deterministic pre-scan, which the rewritten reference no longer does.\n\nConfidence: high. The concern-first structure follows the repository’s actual loading architecture; the main uncertainty is whether any external consumers treat current reference paths as stable."}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08c6c-2bb7-7db0-a8c0-517545c5865e","create_time":1789062466.827082,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T17:48:10.131Z","ordinal":7998,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a08c6c-2bb7-7db0-a8c0-517545c5865e","session_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","root_turn_id":"01a08c6c-2bb7-7db0-a8c0-517545c5865e","response_id":"resp_0c3176283919dd68016aa2ed42a1f887d0b3616c9e741cb204","usage":{"input_tokens":190421,"cached_input_tokens":184576,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1160,"reasoning_output_tokens":286,"total_tokens":191581},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1379503,"cached_input_tokens":1337856,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":8773,"reasoning_output_tokens":6846,"total_tokens":1388276},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":118953150,"cached_input_tokens":116366848,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":531210,"reasoning_output_tokens":176591,"total_tokens":119484360}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T17:48:10.132Z","ordinal":7999,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"token_count","info":{"total_token_usage":{"input_tokens":116974156,"cached_input_tokens":114412928,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":501103,"reasoning_output_tokens":176591,"total_tokens":117475259},"last_token_usage":{"input_tokens":190421,"cached_input_tokens":184576,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1160,"reasoning_output_tokens":286,"total_tokens":191581},"model_context_window":258400},"rate_limits":{"limit_id":"codex","limit_name":null,"primary":{"used_percent":59.0,"window_minutes":10080,"resets_at":1789436456},"secondary":null,"credits":{"has_credits":false,"unlimited":false,"balance":"0"},"individual_limit":null,"spend_control_reached":null,"plan_type":"prolite","rate_limit_reached_type":null}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T17:48:11.180Z","ordinal":8000,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"task_complete","turn_id":"01a08c6c-2bb7-7db0-a8c0-517545c5865e","last_agent_message":"Yes. At 34 files, the flat directory is becoming harder to scan. Organize by cognitive concern first, then language. That matches how agents select references at runtime.\n\n```text\nshared/references/\n├── hazards/\n│   ├── rust.md\n│   ├── rust-boundaries.md\n│   ├── typescript.md\n│   ├── typescript-boundaries.md\n│   ├── python.md\n│   ├── python-boundaries.md\n│   ├── go.md\n│   └── go-boundaries.md\n├── architecture/\n│   ├── rust.md\n│   ├── typescript.md\n│   ├── python.md\n│   ├── go.md\n│   ├── remediation.md\n│   └── boundary-values.md\n├── verification/\n│   ├── rust.md\n│   ├── typescript.md\n│   ├── python.md\n│   ├── go.md\n│   ├── evidence.md\n│   ├── implementation-review.md\n│   └── interface-coverage.md\n├── delivery/\n│   ├── changesets.md\n│   ├── commits.md\n│   └── github.md\n├── authoring/\n│   ├── voice.md\n│   ├── comments.md\n│   └── diagrams.md\n├── evaluation/\n│   └── behavioral.md\n├── workspace/\n│   └── conventions.md\n├── tooling/\n│   └── cli.md\n└── README.md\n```\n\nWhy this pattern:\n\n- It mirrors cognitive modes: scanning, architecture, verification, delivery, and authoring.\n- It keeps references shared across plugins instead of assigning artificial plugin ownership.\n- Exact paths remain self-describing: `hazards/rust.md` is clearer than `rust-hazards.md`.\n- Agents still load one exact file; nesting adds no runtime context.\n- Cross-language comparisons stay easy because equivalent files share a directory.\n\nI would also:\n\n- Replace the four thin language indexes with one human-facing `shared/references/README.md`.\n- Move the 34-row table out of the root README. A directory-level map is less likely to drift.\n- Add a reference-reachability check: every runtime reference must have a prompt or catalog caller; authoring-only references must be declared as such.\n- Reject `misc`, `common`, and plugin-owned reference folders.\n- Keep the tree shallow—two directory levels are enough.\n\nOne important caveat: these paths are runtime dependencies in [harness-authoring.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/harness-authoring.md) and [catalog.json](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/harnesses/codex/catalog.json). Moving them requires updating Claude `<load_first>` blocks, Codex skills, transitive reference links, catalog entries, documentation, and generated distribution artifacts.\n\nI recommend doing the moves in a separate follow-up PR after #9 merges. Against #9’s rewritten files, Git may render many moves as delete/add pairs, making the substantive guidance review much harder.\n\nI also found semantic drift that should be corrected in #9 before merge:\n\n- [agent-best-practices.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/agent-best-practices.md:64) still says 38 agents and promises grep patterns.\n- [ranger README](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/README.md:58) still describes scanner behavior as running predefined grep patterns.\n- [ranger README](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/README.md:149) repeats those outdated reference descriptions.\n- [challenger.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/navigator/agents/challenger.md:19) claims `interface-implementers.md` supplies language-specific grep patterns and a deterministic pre-scan, which the rewritten reference no longer does.\n\nConfidence: high. The concern-first structure follows the repository’s actual loading architecture; the main uncertainty is whether any external consumers treat current reference paths as stable.","started_at":1789062294,"completed_at":1789062491,"duration_ms":196688,"time_to_first_token_ms":3930}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T17:50:47.768Z","ordinal":8001,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"thread_settings_applied","thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","thread_settings":{"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","model_provider_id":"openai","service_tier":"default","approval_policy":"on-request","approvals_reviewer":"auto_review","permission_profile":{"type":"managed","file_system":{"type":"restricted","entries":[{"path":{"type":"special","value":{"kind":"root"}},"access":"read"},{"path":{"type":"path","path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins"},"access":"write"},{"path":{"type":"special","value":{"kind":"slash_tmp"}},"access":"write"},{"path":{"type":"special","value":{"kind":"tmpdir"}},"access":"write"},{"path":{"type":"path","path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/.git"},"access":"read","missing_path_behavior":"skip"},{"path":{"type":"path","path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/.agents"},"access":"read","missing_path_behavior":"skip"},{"path":{"type":"path","path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/.codex"},"access":"read","missing_path_behavior":"skip"}]},"network":"restricted"},"active_permission_profile":{"id":":workspace"},"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins","reasoning_effort":"high","personality":"pragmatic","collaboration_mode":{"mode":"default","settings":{"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","reasoning_effort":"high","developer_instructions":"# Collaboration Mode: Default\n\nYou are now in Default mode. Any previous instructions for other modes (e.g. Plan mode) are no longer active.\n\nYour active mode changes only when new developer instructions with a different `<collaboration_mode>...</collaboration_mode>` change it; user requests or tool descriptions do not change mode by themselves. Known mode names are Default and Plan.\n\n## request_user_input availability\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only when it is listed in the available tools for this turn.\n\nIn Default mode, strongly prefer making reasonable assumptions and executing the user's request rather than stopping to ask questions.\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only for optional questions where the answer would materially improve the quality of the work.\n\nIf `request_user_input` returns no answers, continue with best judgment instead of asking again or treating the turn as blocked.\n\nNever use the `request_user_input` tool for permission requests or permission-related escalations.\n\nIf explicit user input is required for another reason before progress can safely continue, do not use the `request_user_input` tool. Ask the user directly with one concise plain-text question instead. Never write a multiple choice question as a textual assistant message.\n"}}}}}
