{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:03:03.038Z","ordinal":8335,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0c3176283919dd68016aa2f0c3fde887d0ba4f1677c7748b2f","status":"completed","call_id":"call_dFWadoHrtMYJeB2x0uyNP9q7","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/constitution.md\\n@@\\n ## Reference Files\\n \\n-WHEN language-specific reference files are authored, they SHALL be split by concern: hazards, smells, tooling — one file per concern per language.\\n-\\n-WHEN the top-level language index file (`rust.md`, `typescript.md`) is referenced, it SHALL redirect to the appropriate split file rather than containing content directly.\\n+WHEN runtime references are organized, their first directory SHALL name the cognitive concern or reader task; language SHALL be the filename when evidence is language-specific.\\n+\\n+WHEN guidance applies across languages, THE SYSTEM SHALL keep one shared reference unless language-specific evidence changes the judgment.\\n+\\n+WHEN a reference index is authored, it SHALL serve human navigation and SHALL NOT become a runtime prerequisite or duplicate the referenced guidance.\\n@@\\n WHEN a reference claims cross-language or cross-platform coverage, it SHALL cover every named target or state the unsupported target as a coverage gap.\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/agent-best-practices.md\\n@@\\n-`<constitution>` fixes both by being the one place ecosystem-wide rules live, propagated by editing all 38 files together rather than one at a time. It also happens to be what makes the Static Prompt Prefix Invariant's cache-sharing claim literally true instead of describing an architecture nobody built.\\n+`<constitution>` fixes both by keeping ecosystem-wide rules in one byte-identical block, propagated across every agent together. It also makes the Static Prompt Prefix Invariant's cache-sharing claim real.\\n@@\\n <load_first>\\n-Read `shared/references/rust-hazards.md` before doing anything else. It contains\\n-the taxonomy definitions and grep patterns for this phase. Do not read\\n-rust-smells.md or rust-tooling.md.\\n+Read `shared/references/hazards/rust.md` before scanning Rust code. Use its\\n+candidate signals, confirming evidence, and refutation conditions.\\n </load_first>\\n@@\\n-**Reference file split by concern:**\\n-- `<language>-hazards.md` — scanner and non-boundary adversary work.\\n-- `<language>-hazards-t7-t10.md` — boundary tracing and T7/T10 adjudication.\\n-- `<language>-smells.md` — architecture analysis.\\n-- `<language>-tooling.md` — project-native verification tools.\\n+**Reference paths start with the decision:**\\n+\\n+- `hazards/<language>.md` — scanner and non-boundary adversary work.\\n+- `hazards/<language>-boundaries.md` — boundary tracing and T7/T10 adjudication.\\n+- `architecture/<language>.md` — semantic-model and architecture analysis.\\n+- `verification/<language>.md` — project-native verification capabilities.\\n \\n-Current packs cover Rust, TypeScript/JavaScript, Python, and Go. Load one concern and language at a time.\\n+Current language packs cover Rust, TypeScript/JavaScript, Python, and Go. Cross-language concerns keep one canonical reference. Load the smallest set needed for the current decision.\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/AGENTS.md\\n@@\\n-- [**`shared/references/tooling/cli.md`**](./shared/references/tooling/cli.md): Capability-aware preferences for modern CLI tools, with repository-native commands and safe fallbacks taking priority.\\n+- [**`shared/references/tooling/cli.md`**](./shared/references/tooling/cli.md): Capability-aware CLI preferences, with repository-native commands and safe fallbacks first.\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/CONTRIBUTING.md\\n@@\\n-- [ ] If a new `shared/references/*.md` file was added, it's listed in root `README.md`'s Shared References table\\n+- [ ] New references live under the reader's concern, have a real caller, and appear in `shared/references/README.md`'s directory map when they add a concern\\n@@\\n-- [ ] `plugin.json` version bumped (see the Semver Decision Guide in `shared/references/delivery/changesets.md`)\\n+- [ ] `plugin.json` version bumped (see `shared/references/delivery/changesets.md`)\\n@@\\n - **Clean writing:** omit AI filler, marketing language, and non-warning ALL CAPS.\\n+- **Diagrams:** follow `shared/references/authoring/diagrams.md` when Mermaid materially clarifies a relationship.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08c77-4ac1-77a0-808c-4dde87d268d4","create_time":1789063361.806789}}}
