{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:05:22.822Z","ordinal":8404,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a08c7e-ea06-7042-a42a-43231a69c0ae","call_id":"call_MUKSiwatQTMuS03V8S0Z0JfP","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"./docs/codex-marketplace-release-policy.md:53:The fixture is intentionally narrow. Before declaring a workflow change behaviorally equivalent across harnesses, run a representative task through each harness and compare durable JSON artifacts against the same schema and acceptance criteria. Follow [Cross-Harness Behavioral Evaluation](./codex-behavioral-evaluation.md) for the core case, record format, and pass criteria. Do not require identical transcripts, plans, or language; require valid artifacts, traceable evidence, and the intended lifecycle links.\n./harnesses/codex/catalog.json:68:      \"runtime_files\": [\"shared/schemas/implementation-result@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/implementation-review@2.json\", \"shared/schemas/mutation-report@2.json\", \"shared/schemas/plan@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/spec@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/verdict@3.json\", \"shared/schemas/workspace-manifest@1.json\", \"shared/references/authoring/comments.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/go.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md\", \"shared/references/architecture/go.md\", \"shared/references/verification/go.md\", \"shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/python.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md\", \"shared/references/architecture/python.md\", \"shared/references/verification/python.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/rust.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md\", \"shared/references/architecture/rust.md\", \"shared/references/verification/rust.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/typescript.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md\", \"shared/references/architecture/typescript.md\", \"shared/references/verification/typescript.md\", \"shared/references/verification/evidence.md\"]\n./shared/references/authoring/comments.md:3:Operational subset of the Reader-Scoped Writing rule (`constitution.md`) for doc comments (`///`, `/**`, docstrings) and inline comments, in any language. Companion to `docs-voice.md`, which covers commit messages, PR bodies, changesets, and prose docs — this file covers comments written inside code.\n./tests/test_codex_behavioral_evaluation.py:11:GUIDE_PATH = REPOSITORY_ROOT / \"docs/codex-behavioral-evaluation.md\"\n./tests/test_codex_behavioral_evaluation.py:58:        self.assertIn(\"codex-behavioral-evaluation.md\", release_policy)\n./shared/references/hazards/typescript.md:3:Patterns are leads, not findings. Confirm a reachable bad outcome in the target runtime and account for framework behavior. Use `typescript-hazards-t7-t10.md` for boundary taxonomies T7 and T10.\n./ARCHITECTURE.md:404:| Two harnesses produce different prose or reasoning | Not automatically a compatibility failure | Run [`docs/codex-behavioral-evaluation.md`](./docs/codex-behavioral-evaluation.md) and compare valid artifacts, evidence, and acceptance criteria |\n./shared/references/hazards/rust.md:3:Patterns are leads, not findings. Confirm a reachable bad outcome in live code and record evidence that rules out the plausible exception. Use `rust-hazards-t7-t10.md` for boundary taxonomies T7 and T10.\n./harnesses/codex/plugins/smith/skills/implement/SKILL.md:27:Before reviewing, load `shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md` and the evidence it selects. For each changed defect, assess:\n./plugins/smith/README.md:101:The reviewer loads `shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md`, which selects the language hazards, architecture smells, and comment standard relevant to the diff.\n./plugins/smith/agents/implementer.md:40:- Choosing a raw-value-plus-boolean shape when the task can produce the safe