{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:09:45.954Z","ordinal":8543,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0c3176283919dd68016aa2f264fcbc87d08c836640fb81b572","status":"completed","call_id":"call_mANRXcfcvQN1NmKHo3fUxazz","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md\\n@@\\n-Full scan: for each detected language, load its pair: `hazards/rust.md` and `hazards/rust-boundaries.md`; `hazards/typescript.md` and `hazards/typescript-boundaries.md`; `hazards/python.md` and `hazards/python-boundaries.md`; or `hazards/go.md` and `hazards/go-boundaries.md`, all beneath `shared/references/`.\\n+Full scan: load both files for each detected language:\\n+- Rust: `shared/references/hazards/rust.md` and `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md`.\\n+- TypeScript or JavaScript: `shared/references/hazards/typescript.md` and `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md`.\\n+- Python: `shared/references/hazards/python.md` and `shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md`.\\n+- Go: `shared/references/hazards/go.md` and `shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md`.\\n Focused scan: load only the applicable file from that list; T7 and T10 use the boundary file.\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/AGENTS.md\\n@@\\n-9. **Reference quality** — runtime guidance states outcome, applicability, evidence, refutation, and disposition; it does not universalize one project's preferences.\\n+9. **Reference routing and quality** — organize by cognitive concern, use language filenames only for language-specific evidence, and state outcome, applicability, evidence, refutation, and disposition.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08c77-4ac1-77a0-808c-4dde87d268d4","create_time":1789063771.886744}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:09:46.028Z","ordinal":8544,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a08c77-4ac1-77a0-808c-4dde87d268d4","session_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","root_turn_id":"01a08c77-4ac1-77a0-808c-4dde87d268d4","response_id":"resp_0c3176283919dd68016aa2f25bae4087d0844a772163824a9f","usage":{"input_tokens":111769,"cached_input_tokens":110592,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":676,"reasoning_output_tokens":280,"total_tokens":112445},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":4123643,"cached_input_tokens":4018176,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":33205,"reasoning_output_tokens":8381,"total_tokens":4156848},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":124694526,"cached_input_tokens":121975424,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":566615,"reasoning_output_tokens":185962,"total_tokens":125261141}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:09:46.146Z","ordinal":8545,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a08c77-4ac1-77a0-808c-4dde87d268d4","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-740657d8-5ab9-4d81-b5aa-3bd697b8ba07","changes":{"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/AGENTS.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -51,3 +51,3 @@\n 8. **Radical candor** — state material concerns, evidence, consequence, and confidence directly; do not soften blockers, manufacture praise, or overstate certainty.\n-9. **Reference quality** — runtime guidance states outcome, applicability, evidence, refutation, and disposition; it does not universalize one project's preferences.\n+9. **Reference routing and quality** — organize by cognitive concern, use language filenames only for language-specific evidence, and state outcome, applicability, evidence, refutation, and disposition.\n 10. **Verification evidence** — match checks to risk; require generators and oracles, independently derived semantic candidates, fresh state, terminal results, and explicit gaps when relevant.\n","move_path":null},"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -18,3 +18,7 @@\n <load_first>\n-Full scan: for each detected language, load its pair: `hazards/rust.md` and `hazards/rust-boundaries.md`; `hazards/typescript.md` and `hazards/typescript-boundaries.md`; `hazards/python.md` and `hazards/python-boundaries.md`; or `hazards/go.md` and `hazards/go-boundaries.md`, all beneath `shared/references/`.\n+Full scan: load both files for each detected language:\n+- Rust: `shared/references/hazards/rust.md` and `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md`.\n+- TypeScript or JavaScript: `shared/references/hazards/typescript.md` and `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md`.\n+- Python: `shared/references/hazards/python.md` and `shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md`.\n+- Go: `shared/references/hazards/go.md` and `shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md`.\n Focused scan: load only the applicable file from that list; T7 and T10 use the boundary file.\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md\nM /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/AGENTS.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1789063786020,"completed_at_ms":1789063786146}}
