xonomies T7 and T10.\nshared/references/hazards/rust.md:3:Patterns are leads, not findings. Confirm a reachable bad outcome in live code and record evidence that rules out the plausible exception. Use `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md` for boundary taxonomies T7 and T10.\nplugins/scribe/README.md:130:`scribe/verify-spec` checks source grounding; `audit-spec` checks internal quality; `audit-architecture` checks system fit. `scribe/architect` loads `shared/references/architecture/remediation.md` for the persisted-model location and language evidence. After Smith verifies the structural change, `audit-architecture` refreshes the model with the new boundary and invariant.\nshared/references/architecture/remediation.md:5:- Load `shared/references/workspace/conventions.md` to locate the persisted architecture model and gated specs.\nshared/references/architecture/remediation.md:6:- Rust: load `shared/references/architecture/rust.md`.\nshared/references/architecture/remediation.md:7:- TypeScript or JavaScript: load `shared/references/architecture/typescript.md`.\nshared/references/architecture/remediation.md:8:- Python: load `shared/references/architecture/python.md`.\nshared/references/architecture/remediation.md:9:- Go: load `shared/references/architecture/go.md`.\nplugins/scribe/agents/arch-auditor.md:19:Load `shared/references/workspace/conventions.md` before searching for the persisted model — it names where the architecture model and gated specs live on disk, and what an absent model does and doesn't prove.\nplugins/scribe/agents/architect.md:19:Load `shared/references/architecture/remediation.md`. It routes to the persisted-model and language evidence required for this design.\nplugins/scribe/agents/auditor.md:19:Load `shared/references/workspace/conventions.md` before checking scope-overlap or boundary-round-trip — it names where other gated specs live on disk and what an empty search there does and doesn't prove.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/scribe/skills/architect/SKILL.md:16:Validate the input against `shared/schemas/finding-report@2.json`, `shared/schemas/implementation-review@2.json`, or `shared/schemas/implementation-result@1.json`. Load `shared/references/architecture/remediation.md`, then the model and language evidence it selects.\nshared/references/verification/implementation-review.md:7:- Rust: load `shared/references/hazards/rust.md` and `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md` for defect checks; load `shared/references/architecture/rust.md` for semantic-model and architecture signals.\nshared/references/verification/implementation-review.md:8:- TypeScript or JavaScript: load `shared/references/hazards/typescript.md` and `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md` for defect checks; load `shared/references/architecture/typescript.md` for semantic-model and architecture signals.\nshared/references/verification/implementation-review.md:9:- Python: load `shared/references/hazards/python.md` and `shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md` for defect checks; load `shared/references/architecture/python.md` for semantic-model and architecture signals.\nshared/references/verification/implementation-review.md:10:- Go: load `shared/references/hazards/go.md` and `shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md` for defect checks; load `shared/references/architecture/go.md` for semantic-model and architecture signals.\nshared/references/verification/implementation-review.md:12:- If the diff adds or changes comments, load `shared/references/authoring/comments.md`.\nshared/references/verification/implementation-review.md:18:- Verification: method choice, boundary coverage, environment assumptions, and external-state freshness follow `shared/references/verification/evidence.md`.\nplugins/navigator/skills/plan/SKILL.md:26:- **Challenge a draft plan** — `challenger` checks coverage, order, specificity, batch size, error handling, and shared-interface siblings. It loads `shared/references/verification/interface-coverage.md` when a contract or implementation changes. Amended plans receive the same review.\nplugins/navigator/agents/challenger.md:19:When a task changes a shared trait, interface, protocol, or one implementation, load `shared/references/verification/interface-coverage.md` before evaluating interface-incompleteness. Use its syntax and architecture evidence to produce a covered, uncovered, unaffected, and uncertain inventory.\nplugins/navigator/agents/challenger.md:72:WHEN a task changes a shared contract or implementation, THE SYSTEM SHALL derive syntactic and semantic candidate implementations from `shared/references/verification/interface-coverage.md` and record their dispositions before evaluating interface-incompleteness.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/navigator/skills/plan/SKILL.md:20:5. Challenge the plan for orphaned criteria, invalid ordering, missing error paths, over-sized batches, test gaps, and shared-interface siblings. When a contract or implementation changes, use `shared/references/verification/interface-coverage.md` to derive syntactic and semantic candidates from live code and architecture. Revise only concrete blockers; cap review churn at two rounds.\nplugins/smith/README.md:101:The reviewer loads `shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md`, which selects the language hazards, architecture smells, and comment standard relevant to the diff.\nplugins/smith/agents/implementer.md:19:Load `shared/references/verification/evidence.md` when the task has boundary, input-space, environment, or external-state risk. Load `shared/references/architecture/boundary-values.md` when a value can be absent, wrong, or stale. Load `shared/references/authoring/comments.md` when the diff changes comments.\nplugins/smith/agents/implementer.md:39:- Writing a doc comment or inline comment that restates the signature or narrates the implementation process instead of stating the contract or non-obvious reason its reader actually needs — see `shared/references/authoring/comments.md`.\nplugins/smith/agents/implementer.md:40:- Choosing a raw-value-plus-boolean shape when the task can produce the safe sum type from `shared/references/architecture/boundary-values.md`.\nplugins/smith/agents/implementer.md:56:WHEN a criterion's value can be absent, wrong, or stale — especially at a process, crate, or serialization boundary — THE SYSTEM SHALL default to the sum-type/discriminated-union/Result shape from `shared/references/architecture/boundary-values.md` rather than a raw value paired with a separate boolean or sentinel.\nplugins/mason/agents/scaffolder.md:72:WHEN placing a runtime reference, THE AGENT SHALL use `shared/references/<concern>/<language>.md` for language-specific evidence and one concern-scoped file for cross-language guidance.\nplugins/mason/agents/evaluation-runner.md:20:Load `shared/references/evaluation/behavioral.md`. Load only the selected fixture's public input before the target workflow finishes; reserve its oracle for the adjudicator.\nplugins/mason/skills/evaluate/SKILL.md:33:- Protocol: `shared/references/evaluation/behavioral.md`\nplugins/mason/agents/auditor.md:63:Runtime references: inspect each file beneath `shared/references/` that the plugin loads directly or reaches through an exact route. Confirm the first directory names the cognitive concern, language-specific evidence uses the language filename, and runtime routes do not depend on a human index. Confirm the guidance states its decision or outcome, limits heuristics with applicability and refutation evidence, avoids prescribing a specific implementation unless correctness or safety requires it, and covers every language or platform it claims. Flag a project-specific type, command, policy, or abstraction presented as universal.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/smith/skills/implement/SKILL.md:19:4. Execute one cohesive subsystem batch. Choose the smallest safe implementation and verification methods from the changed risks and `shared/references/verification/evidence.md`.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/smith/skills/implement/SKILL.md:27:Before reviewing, load `shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md` and the evidence it selects. For each changed defect, assess:\nplugins/smith/agents/mutator.md:19:For Rust workspaces: shared/references/verification/rust.md\nplugins/smith/agents/mutator.md:20:For TypeScript/JavaScript workspaces: shared/references/verification/typescript.md\nplugins/smith/agents/mutator.md:21:For Python workspaces: shared/references/verification/python.md\nplugins/smith/agents/mutator.md:22:For Go workspaces: shared/references/verification/go.md\nharnesses/codex/plugins/mason/skills/evaluate/SKILL.md:10:Use `shared/references/evaluation/behavioral.md` and return `shared/schemas/harness-evaluation@2.json`.\nplugins/mason/README.md:159:- `shared/references/evaluation/behavioral.md` — hidden-oracle evaluation and provenance rules\nplugins/mason/agents/evaluation-adjudicator.md:20:Load `shared/references/evaluation/behavioral.md`, `shared/schemas/evaluation-run@1.json`, `shared/schemas/harness-evaluation@2.json`, and the selected fixture oracle after receiving a valid completed run.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/courier/skills/changeset/SKILL.md:15:2. Read `shared/references/delivery/changesets.md` before choosing `consumer_impact` or `semver_impact`.\nplugins/smith/agents/reviewer.md:19:Load `shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md`. It routes to the language and comment evidence required for this review.\nplugins/smith/agents/reviewer.md:50:WHEN reviewing changed code, THE SYSTEM SHALL apply the hazard and comment references selected by `shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md`.\nplugins/smith/skills/implement/SKILL.md:23:For each subsystem batch, read persisted criteria, implement the smallest safe solution, and choose verification from `shared/references/verification/evidence.md` plus capabilities in `workspace-manifest@1`. Record exact commands, observations, boundaries, and criterion locations in `implementation-result@1`. Commit only with explicit authorization.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/courier/skills/commit/SKILL.md:15:2. Read `shared/references/delivery/commits.md` for type, scope, and voice rules.\nplugins/vanguard/agents/recon.md:19:Load `shared/references/workspace/conventions.md` before mapping `internal_sources` — it names where gated specs live on disk so a relevant spec can be included in the agenda by path, without reading its contents.\nplugins/courier/agents/release-summarizer.md:19:shared/references/delivery/changesets.md\nplugins/courier/README.md:58:| `review-preprocessor` | Review Package Assembler | haiku / low | Bundles the diff, linked spec, test results, and open questions into a structured review package. Does not categorize comments — that's the caller's call, made with `shared/references/delivery/github.md`'s vocabulary. |\nplugins/courier/README.md:103:- `shared/references/delivery/commits.md` — type/scope conventions, commit message rules, voice\nplugins/courier/README.md:104:- `shared/references/delivery/github.md` — PR template, label conventions, review-comment vocabulary, voice\nplugins/courier/README.md:105:- `shared/references/delivery/changesets.md` — changeset format, consumer/semver classification tables, voice\nplugins/courier/README.md:106:- `shared/references/authoring/voice.md` — the full voice standard these three embed a subset of\nplugins/courier/agents/pr-narrator.md:7:  Delegate to this subagent when the user needs a pull request title and body written for a set of staged or committed changes. Input is a git diff and optionally a linked spec@1 or requirement@1. The agent reads the PR template from shared/references/delivery/github.md and writes from the reviewer's perspective — what does a reviewer with zero prior context need to know to approve this confidently? Output is a JSON object with title, body, labels, and a reasoning scratchpad. The body covers what changed, why it was needed, and how to verify correctness. It explains the change's purpose, not a summary of the diff. Labels are inferred from the change type.\nplugins/courier/agents/pr-narrator.md:19:shared/references/delivery/github.md\nplugins/courier/agents/pr-narrator.md:44:  \"body\": \"string (markdown — outcome-led Summary, observed Verification, and only the Risk and Related sections that apply; matches shared/references/delivery/github.md)\",\nplugins/weaver/agents/auditor.md:19:Load `shared/references/workspace/conventions.md` before searching for spec or plan coverage — it names where gated specs and persisted plans live on disk, and what an empty search there does and doesn't prove.\nplugins/courier/agents/changeset-analyzer.md:7:  Delegate to this subagent when you need changeset@2 artifacts produced from a git diff. Input is a git diff, optionally a linked spec@1, and optionally smith's criteria_evidence from the TDD run that produced this diff. A diff spanning multiple independent topics produces one changeset@2 per topic, never one bundled entry — see judgment for how topics are distinguished. For each topic, classifies consumer_impact (behavior-change, new-capability, internal-only) and semver_impact (major, minor, patch, none) per shared/references/delivery/changesets.md's decision table, identifies that topic's own changed files, detects breaking changes, and maps acceptance_criteria IDs. Uses smith's criteria_evidence directly when supplied; otherwise reconstructs best-effort file-level evidence from the diff. Summary detail scales with semver_impact — terse for patch/internal-only, full old-to-new-to-required-action detail for major. Output is one or more changeset@2 objects conforming to shared/schemas/changeset@2.json, routed to pr-narrator or release-summarizer.\nplugins/courier/agents/changeset-analyzer.md:19:shared/references/delivery/changesets.md\nplugins/courier/agents/commit-analyzer.md:7:  Delegate to this subagent when the user has staged git changes and needs a conventional commit message written. Input is the staged diff. The agent reads shared/references/delivery/commits.md for type and scope conventions. Output is a JSON object containing commit_message, type (feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, test, chore, perf, ci, or build), scope (or null), a breaking flag, and a reasoning scratchpad. The commit message explains why the change was made, not what changed — the diff already shows what changed. The reasoning field is a private scratchpad explaining type and scope selection; it is not forwarded downstream.\nplugins/courier/agents/commit-analyzer.md:19:shared/references/delivery/commits.md\nplugins/ranger/README.md:138:| `Cargo.toml` | Rust | `shared/references/hazards/rust.md` and/or `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md`, per agent scope |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:139:| `package.json` | TypeScript / JavaScript | `shared/references/hazards/typescript.md` and/or `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md`, per agent scope |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:140:| `pyproject.toml`, `requirements.txt`, Python files | Python | `shared/references/hazards/python.md` and/or `shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md` |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:141:| `go.mod`, Go files | Go | `shared/references/hazards/go.md` and/or `shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md` |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:149:| `shared/references/hazards/rust.md` | Rust T1-T6, T8, and T9 candidate, confirmation, and refutation evidence | scanner (always), adversary (non-T7/T10 candidates) |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:150:| `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md` | Rust taxonomies T7 and T10 — boundary-tracer's entire scope | boundary-tracer (always), scanner (full scans), adversary (T7/T10 candidates) |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:151:| `shared/references/hazards/typescript.md` | TypeScript/JavaScript T1-T6, T8, and T9 candidate, confirmation, and refutation evidence | scanner (always), adversary (non-T7/T10 candidates) |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:152:| `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md` | TypeScript taxonomies T7 and T10 — boundary-tracer's entire scope | boundary-tracer (always), scanner (full scans), adversary (T7/T10 candidates) |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:153:| `shared/references/hazards/python.md` | Python taxonomies outside T7/T10 | scanner, adversary |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:154:| `shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md` | Python T7/T10 boundary hazards | scanner, boundary-tracer, adversary |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:155:| `shared/references/hazards/go.md` | Go taxonomies outside T7/T10 | scanner, adversary |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:156:| `shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md` | Go T7/T10 boundary hazards | scanner, boundary-tracer, adversary |\nplugins/courier/skills/commit/SKILL.md:21:`shared/references/delivery/commits.md` — type/scope conventions, commit message rules, and the voice standard for this artifact.\nplugins/courier/skills/release/SKILL.md:21:`shared/references/delivery/changesets.md` — the Semver Decision Guide (now machine-enforced via each changeset's `semver_impact`) and Release Notes Generation format.\nplugins/courier/skills/pr/SKILL.md:21:`shared/references/delivery/github.md` — outcome-led PR structure, observed verification, risk disclosure, review voice, labels, and `gh` commands.\nplugins/courier/skills/receive-feedback/SKILL.md:4:  Trigger when the user asks to process or triage incoming review feedback: \"address the feedback\", \"respond to review comments\", \"what do these comments mean\", \"triage this review\". Assembles a review package — diff summary, linked spec, test results, open questions — so the author has full context to respond without re-reading the whole thread. Does not categorize individual comments by priority; that's the caller's judgment call, made with `shared/references/delivery/github.md`'s vocabulary in hand. This is for feedback received on the user's own PR — critiquing someone else's PR is the built-in `code-review` skill's job, not this one.\nplugins/courier/skills/receive-feedback/SKILL.md:11:Bundles a review package — diff summary, linked spec, test results, open questions — so the author can respond without re-reading the whole thread. Delegates entirely to `review-preprocessor`. Mechanical assembly only; `review-preprocessor`'s own judgment explicitly refuses to categorize comment priority, since it has no visibility into whether the underlying code is right — that's what produced the comments in the first place, and it's the caller's call to make, informed by `shared/references/delivery/github.md`'s vocabulary.\nplugins/courier/skills/receive-feedback/SKILL.md:21:`shared/references/delivery/github.md` — the Conventional Comments / Google review-label vocabulary (`praise:`/`nitpick:`/`issue:`/`suggestion:`/`question:` or `Nit:`/`Optional:`/`FYI:`) the caller applies by hand when triaging the assembled package; `review-preprocessor` does not load or apply it.\nplugins/courier/skills/receive-feedback/SKILL.md:26:**Produces**: review package (diff summary, linked spec, test results, open questions) — the caller triages the incoming comments against it using `shared/references/delivery/github.md`'s vocabulary; `review-preprocessor` does not categorize them.\nplugins/courier/skills/post-review/SKILL.md:19:`shared/references/delivery/github.md` — `gh` CLI commands for posting reviews and comments.\nplugins/courier/skills/changeset/SKILL.md:4:  Trigger when the user asks to add a changeset or document a change: \"add a changeset\", \"document this change\", \"what changed here\". Extracts the consumer-facing meaning of a diff: classifies consumer_impact (behavior-change, new-capability, internal-only) and semver_impact (major, minor, patch, none) per shared/references/delivery/changesets.md's decision table, then writes a summary scaled to that classification. A diff spanning multiple independent topics — common on a backlog/catch-up run, not just a single PR — produces one changeset per topic, not one bundled entry. When the change came via smith, pass along implementer's criteria_evidence — changeset-analyzer uses those exact locations instead of reconstructing approximate ones from the diff.\nplugins/courier/skills/changeset/SKILL.md:21:`shared/references/delivery/changesets.md` — changeset format, the Consumer Impact Classification table, the Semver Decision Guide, and the voice standard for this artifact.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:21:- Rust: `shared/references/hazards/rust.md` and `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md`.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:22:- TypeScript or JavaScript: `shared/references/hazards/typescript.md` and `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md`.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:23:- Python: `shared/references/hazards/python.md` and `shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md`.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:24:- Go: `shared/references/hazards/go.md` and `shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md`.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"shared/schemas/changeset@2.json:18:      \"description\": \"Whether this change is observable to someone outside this repo. See shared/references/delivery/changesets.md for classification rules.\"\nshared/schemas/changeset@2.json:23:      \"description\": \"Version bump this change requires, per the Semver Decision Guide in shared/references/delivery/changesets.md. release-summarizer takes max(semver_impact) across a release's changesets rather than re-deriving it.\"\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:22:        \"shared/references/delivery/changesets.md\",\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:23:        \"shared/references/delivery/commits.md\",\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:24:        \"shared/references/authoring/voice.md\"\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:29:      \"runtime_files\": [\"shared/schemas\", \"shared/harness-authoring.md\", \"shared/references/evaluation/behavioral.md\"]\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:37:      \"runtime_files\": [\"shared/schemas/plan@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/spec@1.json\", \"shared/references/verification/interface-coverage.md\"]\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:48:        \"shared/references/hazards/go.md\",\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:49:        \"shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md\",\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:50:        \"shared/references/hazards/python.md\",\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:51:        \"shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md\",\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:52:        \"shared/references/hazards/rust.md\",\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:53:        \"shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md\",\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:54:        \"shared/references/hazards/typescript.md\",\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:55:        \"shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md\"\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:60:      \"runtime_files\": [\"shared/schemas/arch-audit@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/arch-model@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/finding-report@2.json\", \"shared/schemas/implementation-result@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/implementation-review@2.json\", \"shared/schemas/plan@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/requirement@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/research-report@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/spec@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/verdict@3.json\", \"shared/references/architecture/remediation.md\", \"shared/references/architecture/go.md\", \"shared/references/architecture/python.md\", \"shared/references/architecture/rust.md\", \"shared/references/architecture/typescript.md\", \"shared/references/workspace/conventions.md\"]\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:68:      \"runtime_files\": [\"shared/schemas/implementation-result@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/implementation-review@2.json\", \"shared/schemas/mutation-report@2.json\", \"shared/schemas/plan@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/spec@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/verdict@3.json\", \"shared/schemas/workspace-manifest@1.json\", \"shared/references/authoring/comments.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/go.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md\", \"shared/references/architecture/go.md\", \"shared/references/verification/go.md\", \"shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/python.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md\", \"shared/references/architecture/python.md\", \"shared/references/verification/python.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/rust.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md\", \"shared/references/architecture/rust.md\", \"shared/references/verification/rust.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/typescript.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md\", \"shared/references/architecture/typescript.md\", \"shared/references/verification/typescript.md\", \"shared/references/verification/evidence.md\"]\nshared/hooks/subagent-start.sh:11:  echo \"shared/references/hazards/rust.md\"\nshared/hooks/subagent-start.sh:13:  echo \"shared/references/hazards/typescript.md\"\nshared/hooks/subagent-start.sh:15:  echo \"shared/references/hazards/go.md\"\nshared/hooks/subagent-start.sh:17:  echo \"shared/references/hazards/python.md\"\nshared/references/delivery/commits.md:46:Use active voice and imperative mood. Name the technical outcome in the subject and explain only the non-obvious reason in the body. Remove adjectives that stand in for mechanism or evidence. Full standard: `shared/references/authoring/voice.md`.\nshared/references/delivery/changesets.md:56:Lead with observable consumer impact. Include a reason only when it changes understanding or action. Omit internal agent, file, and implementation detail unless the consumer must know it. State limitations and migration work directly. Full standard: `shared/references/authoring/voice.md`.\nplugins/scribe/skills/architect/SKILL.md:21:`shared/schemas/finding-report@2.json`, `shared/schemas/implementation-review@2.json`, `shared/schemas/implementation-result@1.json`, `shared/schemas/spec@1.json`, and `shared/references/architecture/remediation.md`\nshared/references/hazards/typescript.md:3:Patterns are leads, not findings. Confirm a reachable bad outcome in the target runtime and account for framework behavior. Use `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md` for boundary taxonomies T7 and T10.\nshared/references/hazards/rust.md:3:Patterns are leads, not findings. Confirm a reachable bad outcome in live code and record evidence that rules out the plausible exception. Use `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md` for boundary taxonomies T7 and T10.\nplugins/scribe/README.md:130:`scribe/verify-spec` checks source grounding; `audit-spec` checks internal quality; `audit-architecture` checks system fit. `scribe/architect` loads `shared/references/architecture/remediation.md` for the persisted-model location and language evidence. After Smith verifies the structural change, `audit-architecture` refreshes the model with the new boundary and invariant.\nshared/references/architecture/remediation.md:5:- Load `shared/references/workspace/conventions.md` to locate the persisted architecture model and gated specs.\nshared/references/architecture/remediation.md:6:- Rust: load `shared/references/architecture/rust.md`.\nshared/references/architecture/remediation.md:7:- TypeScript or JavaScript: load `shared/references/architecture/typescript.md`.\nshared/references/architecture/remediation.md:8:- Python: load `shared/references/architecture/python.md`.\nshared/references/architecture/remediation.md:9:- Go: load `shared/references/architecture/go.md`.\nplugins/scribe/agents/arch-auditor.md:19:Load `shared/references/workspace/conventions.md` before searching for the persisted model — it names where the architecture model and gated specs live on disk, and what an absent model does and doesn't prove.\nplugins/scribe/agents/architect.md:19:Load `shared/references/architecture/remediation.md`. It routes to the persisted-model and language evidence required for this design.\nplugins/scribe/agents/auditor.md:19:Load `shared/references/workspace/conventions.md` before checking scope-overlap or boundary-round-trip — it names where other gated specs live on disk and what an empty search there does and doesn't prove.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/scribe/skills/architect/SKILL.md:16:Validate the input against `shared/schemas/finding-report@2.json`, `shared/schemas/implementation-review@2.json`, or `shared/schemas/implementation-result@1.json`. Load `shared/references/architecture/remediation.md`, then the model and language evidence it selects.\nshared/references/verification/implementation-review.md:7:- Rust: load `shared/references/hazards/rust.md` and `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md` for defect checks; load `shared/references/architecture/rust.md` for semantic-model and architecture signals.\nshared/references/verification/implementation-review.md:8:- TypeScript or JavaScript: load `shared/references/hazards/typescript.md` and `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md` for defect checks; load `shared/references/architecture/typescript.md` for semantic-model and architecture signals.\nshared/references/verification/implementation-review.md:9:- Python: load `shared/references/hazards/python.md` and `shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md` for defect checks; load `shared/references/architecture/python.md` for semantic-model and architecture signals.\nshared/references/verification/implementation-review.md:10:- Go: load `shared/references/hazards/go.md` and `shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md` for defect checks; load `shared/references/architecture/go.md` for semantic-model and architecture signals.\nshared/references/verification/implementation-review.md:12:- If the diff adds or changes comments, load `shared/references/authoring/comments.md`.\nshared/references/verification/implementation-review.md:18:- Verification: method choice, boundary coverage, environment assumptions, and external-state freshness follow `shared/references/verification/evidence.md`.\nplugins/navigator/skills/plan/SKILL.md:26:- **Challenge a draft plan** — `challenger` checks coverage, order, specificity, batch size, error handling, and shared-interface siblings. It loads `shared/references/verification/interface-coverage.md` when a contract or implementation changes. Amended plans receive the same review.\nplugins/navigator/agents/challenger.md:19:When a task changes a shared trait, interface, protocol, or one implementation, load `shared/references/verification/interface-coverage.md` before evaluating interface-incompleteness. Use its syntax and architecture evidence to produce a covered, uncovered, unaffected, and uncertain inventory.\nplugins/navigator/agents/challenger.md:72:WHEN a task changes a shared contract or implementation, THE SYSTEM SHALL derive syntactic and semantic candidate implementations from `shared/references/verification/interface-coverage.md` and record their dispositions before evaluating interface-incompleteness.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/navigator/skills/plan/SKILL.md:20:5. Challenge the plan for orphaned criteria, invalid ordering, missing error paths, over-sized batches, test gaps, and shared-interface siblings. When a contract or implementation changes, use `shared/references/verification/interface-coverage.md` to derive syntactic and semantic candidates from live code and architecture. Revise only concrete blockers; cap review churn at two rounds.\nplugins/smith/README.md:101:The reviewer loads `shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md`, which selects the language hazards, architecture smells, and comment standard relevant to the diff.\nplugins/smith/agents/implementer.md:19:Load `shared/references/verification/evidence.md` when the task has boundary, input-space, environment, or external-state risk. Load `shared/references/architecture/boundary-values.md` when a value can be absent, wrong, or stale. Load `shared/references/authoring/comments.md` when the diff changes comments.\nplugins/smith/agents/implementer.md:39:- Writing a doc comment or inline comment that restates the signature or narrates the implementation process instead of stating the contract or non-obvious reason its reader actually needs — see `shared/references/authoring/comments.md`.\nplugins/smith/agents/implementer.md:40:- Choosing a raw-value-plus-boolean shape when the task can produce the safe sum type from `shared/references/architecture/boundary-values.md`.\nplugins/smith/agents/implementer.md:56:WHEN a criterion's value can be absent, wrong, or stale — especially at a process, crate, or serialization boundary — THE SYSTEM SHALL default to the sum-type/discriminated-union/Result shape from `shared/references/architecture/boundary-values.md` rather than a raw value paired with a separate boolean or sentinel.\nplugins/mason/agents/scaffolder.md:72:WHEN placing a runtime reference, THE AGENT SHALL use `shared/references/<concern>/<language>.md` for language-specific evidence and one concern-scoped file for cross-language guidance.\nplugins/mason/agents/evaluation-runner.md:20:Load `shared/references/evaluation/behavioral.md`. Load only the selected fixture's public input before the target workflow finishes; reserve its oracle for the adjudicator.\nplugins/mason/skills/evaluate/SKILL.md:33:- Protocol: `shared/references/evaluation/behavioral.md`\nplugins/mason/agents/auditor.md:63:Runtime references: inspect each file beneath `shared/references/` that the plugin loads directly or reaches through an exact route. Confirm the first directory names the cognitive concern, language-specific evidence uses the language filename, and runtime routes do not depend on a human index. Confirm the guidance states its decision or outcome, limits heuristics with applicability and refutation evidence, avoids prescribing a specific implementation unless correctness or safety requires it, and covers every language or platform it claims. Flag a project-specific type, command, policy, or abstraction presented as universal.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/smith/skills/implement/SKILL.md:19:4. Execute one cohesive subsystem batch. Choose the smallest safe implementation and verification methods from the changed risks and `shared/references/verification/evidence.md`.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/smith/skills/implement/SKILL.md:27:Before reviewing, load `shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md` and the evidence it selects. For each changed defect, assess:\nplugins/smith/agents/mutator.md:19:For Rust workspaces: shared/references/verification/rust.md\nplugins/smith/agents/mutator.md:20:For TypeScript/JavaScript workspaces: shared/references/verification/typescript.md\nplugins/smith/agents/mutator.md:21:For Python workspaces: shared/references/verification/python.md\nplugins/smith/agents/mutator.md:22:For Go workspaces: shared/references/verification/go.md\nharnesses/codex/plugins/mason/skills/evaluate/SKILL.md:10:Use `shared/references/evaluation/behavioral.md` and return `shared/schemas/harness-evaluation@2.json`.\nplugins/mason/README.md:159:- `shared/references/evaluation/behavioral.md` — hidden-oracle evaluation and provenance rules\nplugins/mason/agents/evaluation-adjudicator.md:20:Load `shared/references/evaluation/behavioral.md`, `shared/schemas/evaluation-run@1.json`, `shared/schemas/harness-evaluation@2.json`, and the selected fixture oracle after receiving a valid completed run.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/courier/skills/changeset/SKILL.md:15:2. Read `shared/references/delivery/changesets.md` before choosing `consumer_impact` or `semver_impact`.\nplugins/smith/agents/reviewer.md:19:Load `shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md`. It routes to the language and comment evidence required for this review.\nplugins/smith/agents/reviewer.md:50:WHEN reviewing changed code, THE SYSTEM SHALL apply the hazard and comment references selected by `shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md`.\nplugins/smith/skills/implement/SKILL.md:23:For each subsystem batch, read persisted criteria, implement the smallest safe solution, and choose verification from `shared/references/verification/evidence.md` plus capabilities in `workspace-manifest@1`. Record exact commands, observations, boundaries, and criterion locations in `implementation-result@1`. Commit only with explicit authorization.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/courier/skills/commit/SKILL.md:15:2. Read `shared/references/delivery/commits.md` for type, scope, and voice rules.\nplugins/vanguard/agents/recon.md:19:Load `shared/references/workspace/conventions.md` before mapping `internal_sources` — it names where gated specs live on disk so a relevant spec can be included in the agenda by path, without reading its contents.\nplugins/courier/agents/release-summarizer.md:19:shared/references/delivery/changesets.md\nplugins/courier/README.md:58:| `review-preprocessor` | Review Package Assembler | haiku / low | Bundles the diff, linked spec, test results, and open questions into a structured review package. Does not categorize comments — that's the caller's call, made with `shared/references/delivery/github.md`'s vocabulary. |\nplugins/courier/README.md:103:- `shared/references/delivery/commits.md` — type/scope conventions, commit message rules, voice\nplugins/courier/README.md:104:- `shared/references/delivery/github.md` — PR template, label conventions, review-comment vocabulary, voice\nplugins/courier/README.md:105:- `shared/references/delivery/changesets.md` — changeset format, consumer/semver classification tables, voice\nplugins/courier/README.md:106:- `shared/references/authoring/voice.md` — the full voice standard these three embed a subset of\nplugins/courier/agents/pr-narrator.md:7:  Delegate to this subagent when the user needs a pull request title and body written for a set of staged or committed changes. Input is a git diff and optionally a linked spec@1 or requirement@1. The agent reads the PR template from shared/references/delivery/github.md and writes from the reviewer's perspective — what does a reviewer with zero prior context need to know to approve this confidently? Output is a JSON object with title, body, labels, and a reasoning scratchpad. The body covers what changed, why it was needed, and how to verify correctness. It explains the change's purpose, not a summary of the diff. Labels are inferred from the change type.\nplugins/courier/agents/pr-narrator.md:19:shared/references/delivery/github.md\nplugins/courier/agents/pr-narrator.md:44:  \"body\": \"string (markdown — outcome-led Summary, observed Verification, and only the Risk and Related sections that apply; matches shared/references/delivery/github.md)\",\nplugins/weaver/agents/auditor.md:19:Load `shared/references/workspace/conventions.md` before searching for spec or plan coverage — it names where gated specs and persisted plans live on disk, and what an empty search there does and doesn't prove.\nplugins/courier/agents/changeset-analyzer.md:7:  Delegate to this subagent when you need changeset@2 artifacts produced from a git diff. Input is a git diff, optionally a linked spec@1, and optionally smith's criteria_evidence from the TDD run that produced this diff. A diff spanning multiple independent topics produces one changeset@2 per topic, never one bundled entry — see judgment for how topics are distinguished. For each topic, classifies consumer_impact (behavior-change, new-capability, internal-only) and semver_impact (major, minor, patch, none) per shared/references/delivery/changesets.md's decision table, identifies that topic's own changed files, detects breaking changes, and maps acceptance_criteria IDs. Uses smith's criteria_evidence directly when supplied; otherwise reconstructs best-effort file-level evidence from the diff. Summary detail scales with semver_impact — terse for patch/internal-only, full old-to-new-to-required-action detail for major. Output is one or more changeset@2 objects conforming to shared/schemas/changeset@2.json, routed to pr-narrator or release-summarizer.\nplugins/courier/agents/changeset-analyzer.md:19:shared/references/delivery/changesets.md\nplugins/courier/agents/commit-analyzer.md:7:  Delegate to this subagent when the user has staged git changes and needs a conventional commit message written. Input is the staged diff. The agent reads shared/references/delivery/commits.md for type and scope conventions. Output is a JSON object containing commit_message, type (feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, test, chore, perf, ci, or build), scope (or null), a breaking flag, and a reasoning scratchpad. The commit message explains why the change was made, not what changed — the diff already shows what changed. The reasoning field is a private scratchpad explaining type and scope selection; it is not forwarded downstream.\nplugins/courier/agents/commit-analyzer.md:19:shared/references/delivery/commits.md\nplugins/ranger/README.md:138:| `Cargo.toml` | Rust | `shared/references/hazards/rust.md` and/or `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md`, per agent scope |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:139:| `package.json` | TypeScript / JavaScript | `shared/references/hazards/typescript.md` and/or `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md`, per agent scope |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:140:| `pyproject.toml`, `requirements.txt`, Python files | Python | `shared/references/hazards/python.md` and/or `shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md` |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:141:| `go.mod`, Go files | Go | `shared/references/hazards/go.md` and/or `shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md` |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:149:| `shared/references/hazards/rust.md` | Rust T1-T6, T8, and T9 candidate, confirmation, and refutation evidence | scanner (always), adversary (non-T7/T10 candidates) |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:150:| `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md` | Rust taxonomies T7 and T10 — boundary-tracer's entire scope | boundary-tracer (always), scanner (full scans), adversary (T7/T10 candidates) |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:151:| `shared/references/hazards/typescript.md` | TypeScript/JavaScript T1-T6, T8, and T9 candidate, confirmation, and refutation evidence | scanner (always), adversary (non-T7/T10 candidates) |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:152:| `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md` | TypeScript taxonomies T7 and T10 — boundary-tracer's entire scope | boundary-tracer (always), scanner (full scans), adversary (T7/T10 candidates) |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:153:| `shared/references/hazards/python.md` | Python taxonomies outside T7/T10 | scanner, adversary |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:154:| `shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md` | Python T7/T10 boundary hazards | scanner, boundary-tracer, adversary |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:155:| `shared/references/hazards/go.md` | Go taxonomies outside T7/T10 | scanner, adversary |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:156:| `shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md` | Go T7/T10 boundary hazards | scanner, boundary-tracer, adversary |\nplugins/courier/skills/commit/SKILL.md:21:`shared/references/delivery/commits.md` — type/scope conventions, commit message rules, and the voice standard for this artifact.\nplugins/courier/skills/release/SKILL.md:21:`shared/references/delivery/changesets.md` — the Semver Decision Guide (now machine-enforced via each changeset's `semver_impact`) and Release Notes Generation format.\nplugins/courier/skills/pr/SKILL.md:21:`shared/references/delivery/github.md` — outcome-led PR structure, observed verification, risk disclosure, review voice, labels, and `gh` commands.\nplugins/courier/skills/receive-feedback/SKILL.md:4:  Trigger when the user asks to process or triage incoming review feedback: \"address the feedback\", \"respond to review comments\", \"what do these comments mean\", \"triage this review\". Assembles a review package — diff summary, linked spec, test results, open questions — so the author has full context to respond without re-reading the whole thread. Does not categorize individual comments by priority; that's the caller's judgment call, made with `shared/references/delivery/github.md`'s vocabulary in hand. This is for feedback received on the user's own PR — critiquing someone else's PR is the built-in `code-review` skill's job, not this one.\nplugins/courier/skills/receive-feedback/SKILL.md:11:Bundles a review package — diff summary, linked spec, test results, open questions — so the author can respond without re-reading the whole thread. Delegates entirely to `review-preprocessor`. Mechanical assembly only; `review-preprocessor`'s own judgment explicitly refuses to categorize comment priority, since it has no visibility into whether the underlying code is right — that's what produced the comments in the first place, and it's the caller's call to make, informed by `shared/references/delivery/github.md`'s vocabulary.\nplugins/courier/skills/receive-feedback/SKILL.md:21:`shared/references/delivery/github.md` — the Conventional Comments / Google review-label vocabulary (`praise:`/`nitpick:`/`issue:`/`suggestion:`/`question:` or `Nit:`/`Optional:`/`FYI:`) the caller applies by hand when triaging the assembled package; `review-preprocessor` does not load or apply it.\nplugins/courier/skills/receive-feedback/SKILL.md:26:**Produces**: review package (diff summary, linked spec, test results, open questions) — the caller triages the incoming comments against it using `shared/references/delivery/github.md`'s vocabulary; `review-preprocessor` does not categorize them.\nplugins/courier/skills/post-review/SKILL.md:19:`shared/references/delivery/github.md` — `gh` CLI commands for posting reviews and comments.\nplugins/courier/skills/changeset/SKILL.md:4:  Trigger when the user asks to add a changeset or document a change: \"add a changeset\", \"document this change\", \"what changed here\". Extracts the consumer-facing meaning of a diff: classifies consumer_impact (behavior-change, new-capability, internal-only) and semver_impact (major, minor, patch, none) per shared/references/delivery/changesets.md's decision table, then writes a summary scaled to that classification. A diff spanning multiple independent topics — common on a backlog/catch-up run, not just a single PR — produces one changeset per topic, not one bundled entry. When the change came via smith, pass along implementer's criteria_evidence — changeset-analyzer uses those exact locations instead of reconstructing approximate ones from the diff.\nplugins/courier/skills/changeset/SKILL.md:21:`shared/references/delivery/changesets.md` — changeset format, the Consumer Impact Classification table, the Semver Decision Guide, and the voice standard for this artifact.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:21:- Rust: `shared/references/hazards/rust.md` and `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md`.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:22:- TypeScript or JavaScript: `shared/references/hazards/typescript.md` and `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md`.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:23:- Python: `shared/references/hazards/python.md` and `shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md`.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:24:- Go: `shared/references/hazards/go.md` and `shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md`.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":542},"formatted_output":"shared/schemas/changeset@2.json:18:      \"description\": \"Whether this change is observable to someone outside this repo. See shared/references/delivery/changesets.md for classification rules.\"\nshared/schemas/changeset@2.json:23:      \"description\": \"Version bump this change requires, per the Semver Decision Guide in shared/references/delivery/changesets.md. release-summarizer takes max(semver_impact) across a release's changesets rather than re-deriving it.\"\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:22:        \"shared/references/delivery/changesets.md\",\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:23:        \"shared/references/delivery/commits.md\",\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:24:        \"shared/references/authoring/voice.md\"\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:29:      \"runtime_files\": [\"shared/schemas\", \"shared/harness-authoring.md\", \"shared/references/evaluation/behavioral.md\"]\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:37:      \"runtime_files\": [\"shared/schemas/plan@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/spec@1.json\", \"shared/references/verification/interface-coverage.md\"]\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:48:        \"shared/references/hazards/go.md\",\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:49:        \"shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md\",\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:50:        \"shared/references/hazards/python.md\",\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:51:        \"shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md\",\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:52:        \"shared/references/hazards/rust.md\",\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:53:        \"shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md\",\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:54:        \"shared/references/hazards/typescript.md\",\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:55:        \"shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md\"\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:60:      \"runtime_files\": [\"shared/schemas/arch-audit@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/arch-model@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/finding-report@2.json\", \"shared/schemas/implementation-result@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/implementation-review@2.json\", \"shared/schemas/plan@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/requirement@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/research-report@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/spec@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/verdict@3.json\", \"shared/references/architecture/remediation.md\", \"shared/references/architecture/go.md\", \"shared/references/architecture/python.md\", \"shared/references/architecture/rust.md\", \"shared/references/architecture/typescript.md\", \"shared/references/workspace/conventions.md\"]\nharnesses/codex/catalog.json:68:      \"runtime_files\": [\"shared/schemas/implementation-result@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/implementation-review@2.json\", \"shared/schemas/mutation-report@2.json\", \"shared/schemas/plan@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/spec@1.json\", \"shared/schemas/verdict@3.json\", \"shared/schemas/workspace-manifest@1.json\", \"shared/references/authoring/comments.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/go.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md\", \"shared/references/architecture/go.md\", \"shared/references/verification/go.md\", \"shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/python.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md\", \"shared/references/architecture/python.md\", \"shared/references/verification/python.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/rust.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md\", \"shared/references/architecture/rust.md\", \"shared/references/verification/rust.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/typescript.md\", \"shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md\", \"shared/references/architecture/typescript.md\", \"shared/references/verification/typescript.md\", \"shared/references/verification/evidence.md\"]\nshared/hooks/subagent-start.sh:11:  echo \"shared/references/hazards/rust.md\"\nshared/hooks/subagent-start.sh:13:  echo \"shared/references/hazards/typescript.md\"\nshared/hooks/subagent-start.sh:15:  echo \"shared/references/hazards/go.md\"\nshared/hooks/subagent-start.sh:17:  echo \"shared/references/hazards/python.md\"\nshared/references/delivery/commits.md:46:Use active voice and imperative mood. Name the technical outcome in the subject and explain only the non-obvious reason in the body. Remove adjectives that stand in for mechanism or evidence. Full standard: `shared/references/authoring/voice.md`.\nshared/references/delivery/changesets.md:56:Lead with observable consumer impact. Include a reason only when it changes understanding or action. Omit internal agent, file, and implementation detail unless the consumer must know it. State limitations and migration work directly. Full standard: `shared/references/authoring/voice.md`.\nplugins/scribe/skills/architect/SKILL.md:21:`shared/schemas/finding-report@2.json`, `shared/schemas/implementation-review@2.json`, `shared/schemas/implementation-result@1.json`, `shared/schemas/spec@1.json`, and `shared/references/architecture/remediation.md`\nshared/references/hazards/typescript.md:3:Patterns are leads, not findings. Confirm a reachable bad outcome in the target runtime and account for framework behavior. Use `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md` for boundary taxonomies T7 and T10.\nshared/references/hazards/rust.md:3:Patterns are leads, not findings. Confirm a reachable bad outcome in live code and record evidence that rules out the plausible exception. Use `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md` for boundary taxonomies T7 and T10.\nplugins/scribe/README.md:130:`scribe/verify-spec` checks source grounding; `audit-spec` checks internal quality; `audit-architecture` checks system fit. `scribe/architect` loads `shared/references/architecture/remediation.md` for the persisted-model location and language evidence. After Smith verifies the structural change, `audit-architecture` refreshes the model with the new boundary and invariant.\nshared/references/architecture/remediation.md:5:- Load `shared/references/workspace/conventions.md` to locate the persisted architecture model and gated specs.\nshared/references/architecture/remediation.md:6:- Rust: load `shared/references/architecture/rust.md`.\nshared/references/architecture/remediation.md:7:- TypeScript or JavaScript: load `shared/references/architecture/typescript.md`.\nshared/references/architecture/remediation.md:8:- Python: load `shared/references/architecture/python.md`.\nshared/references/architecture/remediation.md:9:- Go: load `shared/references/architecture/go.md`.\nplugins/scribe/agents/arch-auditor.md:19:Load `shared/references/workspace/conventions.md` before searching for the persisted model — it names where the architecture model and gated specs live on disk, and what an absent model does and doesn't prove.\nplugins/scribe/agents/architect.md:19:Load `shared/references/architecture/remediation.md`. It routes to the persisted-model and language evidence required for this design.\nplugins/scribe/agents/auditor.md:19:Load `shared/references/workspace/conventions.md` before checking scope-overlap or boundary-round-trip — it names where other gated specs live on disk and what an empty search there does and doesn't prove.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/scribe/skills/architect/SKILL.md:16:Validate the input against `shared/schemas/finding-report@2.json`, `shared/schemas/implementation-review@2.json`, or `shared/schemas/implementation-result@1.json`. Load `shared/references/architecture/remediation.md`, then the model and language evidence it selects.\nshared/references/verification/implementation-review.md:7:- Rust: load `shared/references/hazards/rust.md` and `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md` for defect checks; load `shared/references/architecture/rust.md` for semantic-model and architecture signals.\nshared/references/verification/implementation-review.md:8:- TypeScript or JavaScript: load `shared/references/hazards/typescript.md` and `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md` for defect checks; load `shared/references/architecture/typescript.md` for semantic-model and architecture signals.\nshared/references/verification/implementation-review.md:9:- Python: load `shared/references/hazards/python.md` and `shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md` for defect checks; load `shared/references/architecture/python.md` for semantic-model and architecture signals.\nshared/references/verification/implementation-review.md:10:- Go: load `shared/references/hazards/go.md` and `shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md` for defect checks; load `shared/references/architecture/go.md` for semantic-model and architecture signals.\nshared/references/verification/implementation-review.md:12:- If the diff adds or changes comments, load `shared/references/authoring/comments.md`.\nshared/references/verification/implementation-review.md:18:- Verification: method choice, boundary coverage, environment assumptions, and external-state freshness follow `shared/references/verification/evidence.md`.\nplugins/navigator/skills/plan/SKILL.md:26:- **Challenge a draft plan** — `challenger` checks coverage, order, specificity, batch size, error handling, and shared-interface siblings. It loads `shared/references/verification/interface-coverage.md` when a contract or implementation changes. Amended plans receive the same review.\nplugins/navigator/agents/challenger.md:19:When a task changes a shared trait, interface, protocol, or one implementation, load `shared/references/verification/interface-coverage.md` before evaluating interface-incompleteness. Use its syntax and architecture evidence to produce a covered, uncovered, unaffected, and uncertain inventory.\nplugins/navigator/agents/challenger.md:72:WHEN a task changes a shared contract or implementation, THE SYSTEM SHALL derive syntactic and semantic candidate implementations from `shared/references/verification/interface-coverage.md` and record their dispositions before evaluating interface-incompleteness.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/navigator/skills/plan/SKILL.md:20:5. Challenge the plan for orphaned criteria, invalid ordering, missing error paths, over-sized batches, test gaps, and shared-interface siblings. When a contract or implementation changes, use `shared/references/verification/interface-coverage.md` to derive syntactic and semantic candidates from live code and architecture. Revise only concrete blockers; cap review churn at two rounds.\nplugins/smith/README.md:101:The reviewer loads `shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md`, which selects the language hazards, architecture smells, and comment standard relevant to the diff.\nplugins/smith/agents/implementer.md:19:Load `shared/references/verification/evidence.md` when the task has boundary, input-space, environment, or external-state risk. Load `shared/references/architecture/boundary-values.md` when a value can be absent, wrong, or stale. Load `shared/references/authoring/comments.md` when the diff changes comments.\nplugins/smith/agents/implementer.md:39:- Writing a doc comment or inline comment that restates the signature or narrates the implementation process instead of stating the contract or non-obvious reason its reader actually needs — see `shared/references/authoring/comments.md`.\nplugins/smith/agents/implementer.md:40:- Choosing a raw-value-plus-boolean shape when the task can produce the safe sum type from `shared/references/architecture/boundary-values.md`.\nplugins/smith/agents/implementer.md:56:WHEN a criterion's value can be absent, wrong, or stale — especially at a process, crate, or serialization boundary — THE SYSTEM SHALL default to the sum-type/discriminated-union/Result shape from `shared/references/architecture/boundary-values.md` rather than a raw value paired with a separate boolean or sentinel.\nplugins/mason/agents/scaffolder.md:72:WHEN placing a runtime reference, THE AGENT SHALL use `shared/references/<concern>/<language>.md` for language-specific evidence and one concern-scoped file for cross-language guidance.\nplugins/mason/agents/evaluation-runner.md:20:Load `shared/references/evaluation/behavioral.md`. Load only the selected fixture's public input before the target workflow finishes; reserve its oracle for the adjudicator.\nplugins/mason/skills/evaluate/SKILL.md:33:- Protocol: `shared/references/evaluation/behavioral.md`\nplugins/mason/agents/auditor.md:63:Runtime references: inspect each file beneath `shared/references/` that the plugin loads directly or reaches through an exact route. Confirm the first directory names the cognitive concern, language-specific evidence uses the language filename, and runtime routes do not depend on a human index. Confirm the guidance states its decision or outcome, limits heuristics with applicability and refutation evidence, avoids prescribing a specific implementation unless correctness or safety requires it, and covers every language or platform it claims. Flag a project-specific type, command, policy, or abstraction presented as universal.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/smith/skills/implement/SKILL.md:19:4. Execute one cohesive subsystem batch. Choose the smallest safe implementation and verification methods from the changed risks and `shared/references/verification/evidence.md`.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/smith/skills/implement/SKILL.md:27:Before reviewing, load `shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md` and the evidence it selects. For each changed defect, assess:\nplugins/smith/agents/mutator.md:19:For Rust workspaces: shared/references/verification/rust.md\nplugins/smith/agents/mutator.md:20:For TypeScript/JavaScript workspaces: shared/references/verification/typescript.md\nplugins/smith/agents/mutator.md:21:For Python workspaces: shared/references/verification/python.md\nplugins/smith/agents/mutator.md:22:For Go workspaces: shared/references/verification/go.md\nharnesses/codex/plugins/mason/skills/evaluate/SKILL.md:10:Use `shared/references/evaluation/behavioral.md` and return `shared/schemas/harness-evaluation@2.json`.\nplugins/mason/README.md:159:- `shared/references/evaluation/behavioral.md` — hidden-oracle evaluation and provenance rules\nplugins/mason/agents/evaluation-adjudicator.md:20:Load `shared/references/evaluation/behavioral.md`, `shared/schemas/evaluation-run@1.json`, `shared/schemas/harness-evaluation@2.json`, and the selected fixture oracle after receiving a valid completed run.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/courier/skills/changeset/SKILL.md:15:2. Read `shared/references/delivery/changesets.md` before choosing `consumer_impact` or `semver_impact`.\nplugins/smith/agents/reviewer.md:19:Load `shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md`. It routes to the language and comment evidence required for this review.\nplugins/smith/agents/reviewer.md:50:WHEN reviewing changed code, THE SYSTEM SHALL apply the hazard and comment references selected by `shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md`.\nplugins/smith/skills/implement/SKILL.md:23:For each subsystem batch, read persisted criteria, implement the smallest safe solution, and choose verification from `shared/references/verification/evidence.md` plus capabilities in `workspace-manifest@1`. Record exact commands, observations, boundaries, and criterion locations in `implementation-result@1`. Commit only with explicit authorization.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/courier/skills/commit/SKILL.md:15:2. Read `shared/references/delivery/commits.md` for type, scope, and voice rules.\nplugins/vanguard/agents/recon.md:19:Load `shared/references/workspace/conventions.md` before mapping `internal_sources` — it names where gated specs live on disk so a relevant spec can be included in the agenda by path, without reading its contents.\nplugins/courier/agents/release-summarizer.md:19:shared/references/delivery/changesets.md\nplugins/courier/README.md:58:| `review-preprocessor` | Review Package Assembler | haiku / low | Bundles the diff, linked spec, test results, and open questions into a structured review package. Does not categorize comments — that's the caller's call, made with `shared/references/delivery/github.md`'s vocabulary. |\nplugins/courier/README.md:103:- `shared/references/delivery/commits.md` — type/scope conventions, commit message rules, voice\nplugins/courier/README.md:104:- `shared/references/delivery/github.md` — PR template, label conventions, review-comment vocabulary, voice\nplugins/courier/README.md:105:- `shared/references/delivery/changesets.md` — changeset format, consumer/semver classification tables, voice\nplugins/courier/README.md:106:- `shared/references/authoring/voice.md` — the full voice standard these three embed a subset of\nplugins/courier/agents/pr-narrator.md:7:  Delegate to this subagent when the user needs a pull request title and body written for a set of staged or committed changes. Input is a git diff and optionally a linked spec@1 or requirement@1. The agent reads the PR template from shared/references/delivery/github.md and writes from the reviewer's perspective — what does a reviewer with zero prior context need to know to approve this confidently? Output is a JSON object with title, body, labels, and a reasoning scratchpad. The body covers what changed, why it was needed, and how to verify correctness. It explains the change's purpose, not a summary of the diff. Labels are inferred from the change type.\nplugins/courier/agents/pr-narrator.md:19:shared/references/delivery/github.md\nplugins/courier/agents/pr-narrator.md:44:  \"body\": \"string (markdown — outcome-led Summary, observed Verification, and only the Risk and Related sections that apply; matches shared/references/delivery/github.md)\",\nplugins/weaver/agents/auditor.md:19:Load `shared/references/workspace/conventions.md` before searching for spec or plan coverage — it names where gated specs and persisted plans live on disk, and what an empty search there does and doesn't prove.\nplugins/courier/agents/changeset-analyzer.md:7:  Delegate to this subagent when you need changeset@2 artifacts produced from a git diff. Input is a git diff, optionally a linked spec@1, and optionally smith's criteria_evidence from the TDD run that produced this diff. A diff spanning multiple independent topics produces one changeset@2 per topic, never one bundled entry — see judgment for how topics are distinguished. For each topic, classifies consumer_impact (behavior-change, new-capability, internal-only) and semver_impact (major, minor, patch, none) per shared/references/delivery/changesets.md's decision table, identifies that topic's own changed files, detects breaking changes, and maps acceptance_criteria IDs. Uses smith's criteria_evidence directly when supplied; otherwise reconstructs best-effort file-level evidence from the diff. Summary detail scales with semver_impact — terse for patch/internal-only, full old-to-new-to-required-action detail for major. Output is one or more changeset@2 objects conforming to shared/schemas/changeset@2.json, routed to pr-narrator or release-summarizer.\nplugins/courier/agents/changeset-analyzer.md:19:shared/references/delivery/changesets.md\nplugins/courier/agents/commit-analyzer.md:7:  Delegate to this subagent when the user has staged git changes and needs a conventional commit message written. Input is the staged diff. The agent reads shared/references/delivery/commits.md for type and scope conventions. Output is a JSON object containing commit_message, type (feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, test, chore, perf, ci, or build), scope (or null), a breaking flag, and a reasoning scratchpad. The commit message explains why the change was made, not what changed — the diff already shows what changed. The reasoning field is a private scratchpad explaining type and scope selection; it is not forwarded downstream.\nplugins/courier/agents/commit-analyzer.md:19:shared/references/delivery/commits.md\nplugins/ranger/README.md:138:| `Cargo.toml` | Rust | `shared/references/hazards/rust.md` and/or `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md`, per agent scope |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:139:| `package.json` | TypeScript / JavaScript | `shared/references/hazards/typescript.md` and/or `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md`, per agent scope |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:140:| `pyproject.toml`, `requirements.txt`, Python files | Python | `shared/references/hazards/python.md` and/or `shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md` |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:141:| `go.mod`, Go files | Go | `shared/references/hazards/go.md` and/or `shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md` |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:149:| `shared/references/hazards/rust.md` | Rust T1-T6, T8, and T9 candidate, confirmation, and refutation evidence | scanner (always), adversary (non-T7/T10 candidates) |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:150:| `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md` | Rust taxonomies T7 and T10 — boundary-tracer's entire scope | boundary-tracer (always), scanner (full scans), adversary (T7/T10 candidates) |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:151:| `shared/references/hazards/typescript.md` | TypeScript/JavaScript T1-T6, T8, and T9 candidate, confirmation, and refutation evidence | scanner (always), adversary (non-T7/T10 candidates) |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:152:| `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md` | TypeScript taxonomies T7 and T10 — boundary-tracer's entire scope | boundary-tracer (always), scanner (full scans), adversary (T7/T10 candidates) |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:153:| `shared/references/hazards/python.md` | Python taxonomies outside T7/T10 | scanner, adversary |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:154:| `shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md` | Python T7/T10 boundary hazards | scanner, boundary-tracer, adversary |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:155:| `shared/references/hazards/go.md` | Go taxonomies outside T7/T10 | scanner, adversary |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:156:| `shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md` | Go T7/T10 boundary hazards | scanner, boundary-tracer, adversary |\nplugins/courier/skills/commit/SKILL.md:21:`shared/references/delivery/commits.md` — type/scope conventions, commit message rules, and the voice standard for this artifact.\nplugins/courier/skills/release/SKILL.md:21:`shared/references/delivery/changesets.md` — the Semver Decision Guide (now machine-enforced via each changeset's `semver_impact`) and Release Notes Generation format.\nplugins/courier/skills/pr/SKILL.md:21:`shared/references/delivery/github.md` — outcome-led PR structure, observed verification, risk disclosure, review voice, labels, and `gh` commands.\nplugins/courier/skills/receive-feedback/SKILL.md:4:  Trigger when the user asks to process or triage incoming review feedback: \"address the feedback\", \"respond to review comments\", \"what do these comments mean\", \"triage this review\". Assembles a review package — diff summary, linked spec, test results, open questions — so the author has full context to respond without re-reading the whole thread. Does not categorize individual comments by priority; that's the caller's judgment call, made with `shared/references/delivery/github.md`'s vocabulary in hand. This is for feedback received on the user's own PR — critiquing someone else's PR is the built-in `code-review` skill's job, not this one.\nplugins/courier/skills/receive-feedback/SKILL.md:11:Bundles a review package — diff summary, linked spec, test results, open questions — so the author can respond without re-reading the whole thread. Delegates entirely to `review-preprocessor`. Mechanical assembly only; `review-preprocessor`'s own judgment explicitly refuses to categorize comment priority, since it has no visibility into whether the underlying code is right — that's what produced the comments in the first place, and it's the caller's call to make, informed by `shared/references/delivery/github.md`'s vocabulary.\nplugins/courier/skills/receive-feedback/SKILL.md:21:`shared/references/delivery/github.md` — the Conventional Comments / Google review-label vocabulary (`praise:`/`nitpick:`/`issue:`/`suggestion:`/`question:` or `Nit:`/`Optional:`/`FYI:`) the caller applies by hand when triaging the assembled package; `review-preprocessor` does not load or apply it.\nplugins/courier/skills/receive-feedback/SKILL.md:26:**Produces**: review package (diff summary, linked spec, test results, open questions) — the caller triages the incoming comments against it using `shared/references/delivery/github.md`'s vocabulary; `review-preprocessor` does not categorize them.\nplugins/courier/skills/post-review/SKILL.md:19:`shared/references/delivery/github.md` — `gh` CLI commands for posting reviews and comments.\nplugins/courier/skills/changeset/SKILL.md:4:  Trigger when the user asks to add a changeset or document a change: \"add a changeset\", \"document this change\", \"what changed here\". Extracts the consumer-facing meaning of a diff: classifies consumer_impact (behavior-change, new-capability, internal-only) and semver_impact (major, minor, patch, none) per shared/references/delivery/changesets.md's decision table, then writes a summary scaled to that classification. A diff spanning multiple independent topics — common on a backlog/catch-up run, not just a single PR — produces one changeset per topic, not one bundled entry. When the change came via smith, pass along implementer's criteria_evidence — changeset-analyzer uses those exact locations instead of reconstructing approximate ones from the diff.\nplugins/courier/skills/changeset/SKILL.md:21:`shared/references/delivery/changesets.md` — changeset format, the Consumer Impact Classification table, the Semver Decision Guide, and the voice standard for this artifact.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:21:- Rust: `shared/references/hazards/rust.md` and `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md`.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:22:- TypeScript or JavaScript: `shared/references/hazards/typescript.md` and `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md`.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:23:- Python: `shared/references/hazards/python.md` and `shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md`.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:24:- Go: `shared/references/hazards/go.md` and `shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md`.\n"},"started_at_ms":1789063878948,"completed_at_ms":1789063878949}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:11:18.998Z","ordinal":8635,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a08c84-5956-7930-9527-e5b7d5c4d742","call_id":"call_uof1kAfXzi7T65flZDhnqoXp","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 15321)\nTotal output lines: 459\n\n---RESULT 1---\n./docs/codex-marketplace-release-policy.md:53:The fixture is intentionally narrow. Before declaring a workflow change behaviorally equivalent across harnesses, run a representative task through each harness and compare durable JSON artifacts against the same schema and acceptance criteria. Follow [Cross-Harness Behavioral Evaluation](./codex-behavioral-evaluation.md) for the core case, record format, and pass criteria. Do not require identical transcripts, plans, or language; require valid artifacts, traceable evidence, and the intended lifecycle links.\n./ARCHITECTURE.md:406:| Two harnesses produce different prose or reasoning | Not automatically a compatibility failure | Run [`docs/codex-behavioral-evaluation.md`](./docs/codex-behavioral-evaluation.md) and compare valid artifacts, evidence, and acceptance criteria |\n./plugins/smith/agents/reviewer.md:19:Load `shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md`. It routes to the language and comment evidence required for this review.\n./plugins/smith/agents/reviewer.md:50:WHEN reviewing changed code, THE SYSTEM SHALL apply the hazard and comment references selected by `shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md`.\n./plugins/smith/README.md:101:The reviewer loads `shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md`, which selects the language hazards, architecture smells, and comment standard relevant to the diff.\n./tests/test_codex_behavioral_evaluation.py:11:GUIDE_PATH = REPOSITORY_ROOT / \"docs/codex-behavioral-evaluation.md\"\n./tests/test_codex_behavioral_evalu