{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:13:37.669Z","ordinal":8691,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a08c77-4ac1-77a0-808c-4dde87d268d4","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-99d14ff1-6141-4b2c-bcd9-6ea24b95a165","process_id":"63216","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rtk bat --style=plain scripts/check-mermaid.sh && rtk rg -n '^```mermaid|^```$' ARCHITECTURE.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk bat --style=plain scripts/check-mermaid.sh && rtk rg -n '^```mermaid|^```$' ARCHITECTURE.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Extracts every ```mermaid fenced block from every .md file in the repo and\n# renders each through @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli. Reports which files/blocks\n# fail to parse — a diagram with a syntax error still displays as valid\n# markdown, so `git status`/`jq`-style checks never catch this; only an\n# actual render does. Needs Node (npx); no repo dependency required, resolved\n# on demand.\n#\n# Usage: scripts/check-mermaid.sh\n\nset -euo pipefail\nscript_dir=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\n# shellcheck source=lib/report.sh\nsource \"$script_dir/lib/report.sh\"\ncd \"$script_dir/..\"\n\nworkdir=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\ntrap 'rm -rf \"$workdir\"' EXIT\n\n# CI runners run jobs as root, where Chrome refuses to start its sandbox\n# without this flag — passed via a puppeteer config file since mmdc has no\n# CLI flag for it directly. Scoped to CI only (GitHub Actions always sets\n# CI=true): a custom puppeteer config on a local machine can interfere with\n# how mermaid-cli resolves an already-cached Chrome binary, so local runs\n# keep using mmdc's own default resolution, which needs no such override.\nmmdc_args=()\nif [[ \"${CI:-}\" == \"true\" ]]; then\n  puppeteer_config=\"$workdir/puppeteer-config.json\"\n  cat > \"$puppeteer_config\" <<'JSON'\n{\"args\": [\"--no-sandbox\", \"--disable-setuid-sandbox\"]}\nJSON\n  mmdc_args=(-p \"$puppeteer_config\")\nfi\n\nfail=0\ncount=0\n\nwhile IFS= read -r -d '' file; do\n  block_index=0\n  in_block=0\n  block_content=\"\"\n  while IFS= read -r line; do\n    if [[ \"$line\" == '```mermaid' ]]; then\n      in_block=1\n      block_content=\"\"\n      continue\n    fi\n    if [[ $in_block -eq 1 && \"$line\" == '```' ]]; then\n      in_block=0\n      count=$((count + 1))\n      mmd=\"$workdir/block_${count}.mmd\"\n      printf '%s\\n' \"$block_content\" > \"$mmd\"\n      if ! npx --yes @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli -i \"$mmd\" -o \"$workdir/block_${count}.svg\" \"${mmdc_args[@]+\"${mmdc_args[@]}\"}\" > \"$workdir/log_${count}.txt\" 2>&1; then\n        fail=$((fail + 1))\n        echo \"FAIL: $file (block $((block_index + 1)))\"\n        grep -A2 '^Error' \"$workdir/log_${count}.txt\" | head -3 | sed 's/^/    /'\n      fi\n      block_index=$((block_index + 1))\n      continue\n    fi\n    if [[ $in_block -eq 1 ]]; then\n      block_content=\"${block_content}${line}\"$'\\n'\n    fi\n  done < \"$file\"\ndone < <(find . -name '*.md' -not -path './.git/*' -not -path '*/node_modules/*' -not -path '*/target/*' -print0)\n\nreport_check \"$fail\" \"$count\" \\\n  \"mermaid block(s) across the repo, all render cleanly.\" \\\n  \"mermaid block(s) did not render. Fix and re-run.\"\n11:```mermaid\n28:```\n36:```\n43:```\n57:```mermaid\n77:```\n81:```mermaid\n103:```\n153:```mermaid\n170:```\n180:```mermaid\n215:```\n268:```mermaid\n288:```\n315:```mermaid\n340:```\n373:```\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Extracts every ```mermaid fenced block from every .md file in the repo and\n# renders each through @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli. Reports which files/blocks\n# fail to parse — a diagram with a syntax error still displays as valid\n# markdown, so `git status`/`jq`-style checks never catch this; only an\n# actual render does. Needs Node (npx); no repo dependency required, resolved\n# on demand.\n#\n# Usage: scripts/check-mermaid.sh\n\nset -euo pipefail\nscript_dir=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\n# shellcheck source=lib/report.sh\nsource \"$script_dir/lib/report.sh\"\ncd \"$script_dir/..\"\n\nworkdir=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\ntrap 'rm -rf \"$workdir\"' EXIT\n\n# CI runners run jobs as root, where Chrome refuses to start its sandbox\n# without this flag — passed via a puppeteer config file since mmdc has no\n# CLI flag for it directly. Scoped to CI only (GitHub Actions always sets\n# CI=true): a custom puppeteer config on a local machine can interfere with\n# how mermaid-cli resolves an already-cached Chrome binary, so local runs\n# keep using mmdc's own default resolution, which needs no such override.\nmmdc_args=()\nif [[ \"${CI:-}\" == \"true\" ]]; then\n  puppeteer_config=\"$workdir/puppeteer-config.json\"\n  cat > \"$puppeteer_config\" <<'JSON'\n{\"args\": [\"--no-sandbox\", \"--disable-setuid-sandbox\"]}\nJSON\n  mmdc_args=(-p \"$puppeteer_config\")\nfi\n\nfail=0\ncount=0\n\nwhile IFS= read -r -d '' file; do\n  block_index=0\n  in_block=0\n  block_content=\"\"\n  while IFS= read -r line; do\n    if [[ \"$line\" == '```mermaid' ]]; then\n      in_block=1\n      block_content=\"\"\n      continue\n    fi\n    if [[ $in_block -eq 1 && \"$line\" == '```' ]]; then\n      in_block=0\n      count=$((count + 1))\n      mmd=\"$workdir/block_${count}.mmd\"\n      printf '%s\\n' \"$block_content\" > \"$mmd\"\n      if ! npx --yes @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli -i \"$mmd\" -o \"$workdir/block_${count}.svg\" \"${mmdc_args[@]+\"${mmdc_args[@]}\"}\" > \"$workdir/log_${count}.txt\" 2>&1; then\n        fail=$((fail + 1))\n        echo \"FAIL: $file (block $((block_index + 1)))\"\n        grep -A2 '^Error' \"$workdir/log_${count}.txt\" | head -3 | sed 's/^/    /'\n      fi\n      block_index=$((block_index + 1))\n      continue\n    fi\n    if [[ $in_block -eq 1 ]]; then\n      block_content=\"${block_content}${line}\"$'\\n'\n    fi\n  done < \"$file\"\ndone < <(find . -name '*.md' -not -path './.git/*' -not -path '*/node_modules/*' -not -path '*/target/*' -print0)\n\nreport_check \"$fail\" \"$count\" \\\n  \"mermaid block(s) across the repo, all render cleanly.\" \\\n  \"mermaid block(s) did not render. Fix and re-run.\"\n11:```mermaid\n28:```\n36:```\n43:```\n57:```mermaid\n77:```\n81:```mermaid\n103:```\n153:```mermaid\n170:```\n180:```mermaid\n215:```\n268:```mermaid\n288:```\n315:```mermaid\n340:```\n373:```\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":3833},"formatted_output":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Extracts every ```mermaid fenced block from every .md file in the repo and\n# renders each through @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli. Reports which files/blocks\n# fail to parse — a diagram with a syntax error still displays as valid\n# markdown, so `git status`/`jq`-style checks never catch this; only an\n# actual render does. Needs Node (npx); no repo dependency required, resolved\n# on demand.\n#\n# Usage: scripts/check-mermaid.sh\n\nset -euo pipefail\nscript_dir=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\n# shellcheck source=lib/report.sh\nsource \"$script_dir/lib/report.sh\"\ncd \"$script_dir/..\"\n\nworkdir=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\ntrap 'rm -rf \"$workdir\"' EXIT\n\n# CI runners run jobs as root, where Chrome refuses to start its sandbox\n# without this flag — passed via a puppeteer config file since mmdc has no\n# CLI flag for it directly. Scoped to CI only (GitHub Actions always sets\n# CI=true): a custom puppeteer config on a local machine can interfere with\n# how mermaid-cli resolves an already-cached Chrome binary, so local runs\n# keep using mmdc's own default resolution, which needs no such override.\nmmdc_args=()\nif [[ \"${CI:-}\" == \"true\" ]]; then\n  puppeteer_config=\"$workdir/puppeteer-config.json\"\n  cat > \"$puppeteer_config\" <<'JSON'\n{\"args\": [\"--no-sandbox\", \"--disable-setuid-sandbox\"]}\nJSON\n  mmdc_args=(-p \"$puppeteer_config\")\nfi\n\nfail=0\ncount=0\n\nwhile IFS= read -r -d '' file; do\n  block_index=0\n  in_block=0\n  block_content=\"\"\n  while IFS= read -r line; do\n    if [[ \"$line\" == '```mermaid' ]]; then\n      in_block=1\n      block_content=\"\"\n      continue\n    fi\n    if [[ $in_block -eq 1 && \"$line\" == '```' ]]; then\n      in_block=0\n      count=$((count + 1))\n      mmd=\"$workdir/block_${count}.mmd\"\n      printf '%s\\n' \"$block_content\" > \"$mmd\"\n      if ! npx --yes @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli -i \"$mmd\" -o \"$workdir/block_${count}.svg\" \"${mmdc_args[@]+\"${mmdc_args[@]}\"}\" > \"$workdir/log_${count}.txt\" 2>&1; then\n        fail=$((fail + 1))\n        echo \"FAIL: $file (block $((block_index + 1)))\"\n        grep -A2 '^Error' \"$workdir/log_${count}.txt\" | head -3 | sed 's/^/    /'\n      fi\n      block_index=$((block_index + 1))\n      continue\n    fi\n    if [[ $in_block -eq 1 ]]; then\n      block_content=\"${block_content}${line}\"$'\\n'\n    fi\n  done < \"$file\"\ndone < <(find . -name '*.md' -not -path './.git/*' -not -path '*/node_modules/*' -not -path '*/target/*' -print0)\n\nreport_check \"$fail\" \"$count\" \\\n  \"mermaid block(s) across the repo, all render cleanly.\" \\\n  \"mermaid block(s) did not render. Fix and re-run.\"\n11:```mermaid\n28:```\n36:```\n43:```\n57:```mermaid\n77:```\n81:```mermaid\n103:```\n153:```mermaid\n170:```\n180:```mermaid\n215:```\n268:```mermaid\n288:```\n315:```mermaid\n340:```\n373:```\n"},"started_at_ms":1789064017668,"completed_at_ms":1789064017669}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:13:37.711Z","ordinal":8692,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a08c86-772f-7d80-bcf3-5ff2d1380292","call_id":"call_YyvMVVRpFVUEs7TIyRxT5Uxd","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Extracts every ```mermaid fenced block from every .md file in the repo and\n# renders each through @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli. Reports which files/blocks\n# fail to parse — a diagram with a syntax error still displays as valid\n# markdown, so `git status`/`jq`-style checks never catch this; only an\n# actual render does. Needs Node (npx); no repo dependency required, resolved\n# on demand.\n#\n# Usage: scripts/check-mermaid.sh\n\nset -euo pipefail\nscript_dir=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\n# shellcheck source=lib/report.sh\nsource \"$script_dir/lib/report.sh\"\ncd \"$script_dir/..\"\n\nworkdir=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\ntrap 'rm -rf \"$workdir\"' EXIT\n\n# CI runners run jobs as root, where Chrome refuses to start its sandbox\n# without this flag — passed via a puppeteer config file since mmdc has no\n# CLI flag for it directly. Scoped to CI only (GitHub Actions always sets\n# CI=true): a custom puppeteer config on a local machine can interfere with\n# how mermaid-cli resolves an already-cached Chrome binary, so local runs\n# keep using mmdc's own default resolution, which needs no such override.\nmmdc_args=()\nif [[ \"${CI:-}\" == \"true\" ]]; then\n  puppeteer_config=\"$workdir/puppeteer-config.json\"\n  cat > \"$puppeteer_config\" <<'JSON'\n{\"args\": [\"--no-sandbox\", \"--disable-setuid-sandbox\"]}\nJSON\n  mmdc_args=(-p \"$puppeteer_config\")\nfi\n\nfail=0\ncount=0\n\nwhile IFS= read -r -d '' file; do\n  block_index=0\n  in_block=0\n  block_content=\"\"\n  while IFS= read -r line; do\n    if [[ \"$line\" == '```mermaid' ]]; then\n      in_block=1\n      block_content=\"\"\n      continue\n    fi\n    if [[ $in_block -eq 1 && \"$line\" == '```' ]]; then\n      in_block=0\n      count=$((count + 1))\n      mmd=\"$workdir/block_${count}.mmd\"\n      printf '%s\\n' \"$block_content\" > \"$mmd\"\n      if ! npx --yes @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli -i \"$mmd\" -o \"$workdir/block_${count}.svg\" \"${mmdc_args[@]+\"${mmdc_args[@]}\"}\" > \"$workdir/log_${count}.txt\" 2>&1; then\n        fail=$((fail + 1))\n        echo \"FAIL: $file (block $((block_index + 1)))\"\n        grep -A2 '^Error' \"$workdir/log_${count}.txt\" | head -3 | sed 's/^/    /'\n      fi\n      block_index=$((block_index + 1))\n      continue\n    fi\n    if [[ $in_block -eq 1 ]]; then\n      block_content=\"${block_content}${line}\"$'\\n'\n    fi\n  done < \"$file\"\ndone < <(find . -name '*.md' -not -path './.git/*' -not -path '*/node_modules/*' -not -path '*/target/*' -print0)\n\nreport_check \"$fail\" \"$count\" \\\n  \"mermaid block(s) across the repo, all render cleanly.\" \\\n  \"mermaid block(s) did not render. Fix and re-run.\"\n11:```mermaid\n28:```\n36:```\n43:```\n57:```mermaid\n77:```\n81:```mermaid\n103:```\n153:```mermaid\n170:```\n180:```mermaid\n215:```\n268:```mermaid\n288:```\n315:```mermaid\n340:```\n373:```\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08c77-4ac1-77a0-808c-4dde87d268d4","create_time":1789064017.711101}}}
