{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:20:45.483Z","ordinal":8846,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a08c77-4ac1-77a0-808c-4dde87d268d4","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0c3176283919dd68016aa2f4fb1c8c87d095f20014e4676b7e","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"One compatibility edge needs a deliberate exception: `changeset@2` is immutable, and its published field descriptions contain the old guide path. Rewriting those two strings would violate the repository’s commit guard; inventing `changeset@3` solely for a moved documentation link would create needless contract churn. I’m preserving the schema bytes and recording that exact legacy-path exception in the new validator, while every live Courier route uses the new path."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1789064443125,"completed_at_ms":1789064445483}}
