{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:37:06.798Z","ordinal":9165,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a08c9b-f76e-7123-99b5-518b498c2a57","call_id":"call_R1J1zeJiPi9iENXewUdM7U1j","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---RESULT 1 (exit 0)---\nshared/scripts/validate-wiring.sh:87:    if echo \"$ALL_PRODUCED\" | grep -qw \"$schema\"; then\ndocs/adr/003-cognitive-mode-separation.md:8:Early plugin agents combined scanning and analysis in a single invocation — a single agent would grep for hazards and then assess whether each match was a real bug. This produced agents that were worse at both jobs: the scanner filtered matches because they \"looked harmless,\" creating false negatives the downstream agent could never recover; the analyst had insufficient depth because it was also doing exhaustive enumeration. The alternative considered was one agent per cognitive mode.\nshared/schemas/candidate@1.json:33:      \"description\": \"The grep pattern that produced this match — for traceability\"\nplugins/mason/agents/auditor.md:55:No authoring-time refs: use your search tool to grep each agent body AND each `SKILL.md` in the plugin for `shared/agent-best-practices.md`. That file is for mason authors writing agents, not for agents to consult at runtime. A reference inside an agent body is always a fail. A reference inside a `SKILL.md` is a fail everywhere except `mason`'s own `scaffold-plugin` and `scaffold-subagent` skills, whose actual job is authoring agents per that guide — this is the one legitimate use, not a precedent for other plugins.\nshared/constitution.md:58:WHEN executing shell operations, THE SYSTEM SHALL prioritize modern CLI tools (ripgrep `rg`, `fd`, `bat`, `jq`, `delta`, `eza`) over legacy builtins (`grep`, `find`, `sed`, `cat`).\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:34:Run every hazard taxonomy grep pattern from the loaded reference against every live file and emit a candidate@1 entry for each match, so the adversary has a complete set of candidates to work with.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:38:The scan is complete when every grep pattern from every applicable taxonomy has been run against every file in live_files, and every match has produced a candidate entry.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:46:Use your search tool to run each grep pattern from the loaded hazard reference against live files. For each match, use your file reading tool to read surrounding code (enough to populate excerpt and taxonomy fields). Do not scan dead_files.\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---RESULT 2 (exit 0)---\nplugins/courier/README.md:58:| `review-preprocessor` | Review Package Assembler | haiku / low | Bundles the diff, linked spec, test results, and open questions into a structured review package. Does not categorize comments — that's the caller's call, made with `shared/references/delivery/github.md`'s vocabulary. |\nplugins/courier/README.md:103:- `shared/references/delivery/commits.md` — type/scope conventions, commit message rules, voice\nplugins/courier/README.md:104:- `shared/references/delivery/github.md` — PR template, label conventions, review-comment vocabulary, voice\nplugins/courier/README.md:105:- `shared/references/delivery/changesets.md` — changeset format, consumer/semver classification tables, voice\nplugins/courier/README.md:106:- `shared/references/authoring/voice.md` — the full voice standard these three embed a subset of\nharnesses/codex/plugins/scribe/skills/architect/SKILL.md:16:Validate the input against `shared/schemas/finding-report@2.json`, `shared/schemas/implementation-review@2.json`, or `shared/schemas/implementation-result@1.json`. Load `shared/references/architecture/remediation.md`, then the model and language evidence it selects.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/courier/skills/commit/SKILL.md:15:2. Read `shared/references/delivery/commits.md` for type, scope, and voice rules.\nshared/agent-best-practices.md:20:Read `shared/references/<concern>/<file>.md` before doing anything else.\nshared/agent-best-practices.md:21:[Only present when the agent uses a shared reference file for its phase.]\nshared/agent-best-practices.md:70:Read `shared/references/hazards/rust.md` before scanning Rust code. Use its\nshared/agent-best-practices.md:228:To prevent context bloat, deliver tool preferences and language taxonomies dynamically via lifecycle hooks (`shared/hooks/`):\nshared/agent-best-practices.md:269:- `shared/references/<concern>/*.md` — **runtime**. Agents load these on demand via `<load_first>`.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/navigator/skills/plan/SKILL.md:20:5. Challenge the plan for orphaned criteria, invalid ordering, missing error paths, over-sized batches, test gaps, and shared-interface siblings. When a contract or implementation changes, use `shared/references/verification/interface-coverage.md` to derive syntactic and semantic candidates from live code and architecture. Revise only concrete blockers; cap review churn at two rounds.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/courier/skills/changeset/SKILL.md:15:2. Read `shared/references/delivery/changesets.md` before choosing `consumer_impact` or `semver_impact`.\nARCHITECTURE.md:30:Agents pull reference files themselves using their file reading tool. The host never pre-loads them.\nARCHITECTURE.md:143:Unavailable or disproportionate checks become explicit coverage gaps; invoking a tool without a relevant oracle proves nothing. Rust, TypeScript/JavaScript, Python, and Go references suggest compatible tools without making one command mandatory.\nARCHITECTURE.md:244:**Progressive context loading** — each agent loads only the reference file for its cognitive concern.\nARCHITECTURE.md:247:- Never load all reference files into all agents — attention degrades when the context window contains material the agent won't use\nARCHITECTURE.md:249:**Reference guidance** — runtime references improve judgment without replacing it.\nARCHITECTURE.md:251:- Applicability, refutation, and disposition keep repository preferences from becoming universal defects or fixes\nARCHITECTURE.md:372:    └── shared/references/<concern>/*.md    # Materialized only when a native skill declares it\nARCHITECTURE.md:388:| Reference integrity | `tests/test_reference_integrity.py` | Non-concern paths, broken exact paths, or runtime references with no caller |\nplugins/weaver/README.md:45:| `weaver/audit-backlog` | Cross-references all open requirements against specs and implementation files — gaps, coverage, duplicates | `auditor` |\nplugins/weaver/README.md:58:| `auditor` | Requirement Coverage Auditor | sonnet / medium | Cross-references requirement@1 objects against specs, persisted plans, and implementation files for coverage and duplicates. Runs at full-backlog scope (`audit-backlog`) or single-requirement scope (`connect-requirement`) — same agent, same output shape, different input size. |\nCONTRIBUTING.md:101:- [ ] Declares a `<load_first>` block naming the specific `shared/references/` file for this agent's phase\nCONTRIBUTING.md:102:- [ ] Does not load reference files outside its cognitive mode (scanner loads hazards, not smells)\nCONTRIBUTING.md:103:- [ ] Places references under the cognitive concern; uses language filenames only for language-specific evidence\nCONTRIBUTING.md:180:- [ ] New references live under the reader's concern, have a real caller, and update `shared/references/README.md` when they introduce a concern\nCONTRIBUTING.md:187:- [ ] `plugin.json` version bumped (see `shared/references/delivery/changesets.md`)\nCONTRIBUTING.md:199:- **Pull, don't inject:** subagents load `shared/references/` on demand; the host does not preload them.\nCONTRIBUTING.md:204:- **Diagrams:** follow `shared/references/authoring/diagrams.md` when Mermaid materially clarifies a relationship.\nCONTRIBUTING.md:230:# Enforce the 120-line cap and report dense references for prose review.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/smith/skills/implement/SKILL.md:19:4. Execute one cohesive subsystem batch. Choose the smallest safe implementation and verification methods from the changed risks and `shared/references/verification/evidence.md`.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/smith/skills/implement/SKILL.md:27:Before reviewing, load `shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md` and the evidence it selects. For each changed defect, assess:\nAGENTS.md:15:- [**`shared/references/tooling/cli.md`**](./shared/references/tooling/cli.md): Capability-aware preferences for modern CLI tools, with repository-native commands and safe fallbacks taking priority.\nAGENTS.md:47:4. **Progressive context loading** — one `<load_first>` block per agent, naming only the reference file for its cognitive phase.\nplugins/smith/README.md:101:The reviewer loads `shared/references/verification/implementation-review.md`, which selects the language hazards, architecture smells, and comment standard relevant to the diff.\nharnesses/codex/plugins/mason/skills/evaluate/SKILL.md:10:Use `shared/references/evaluation/behavioral.md` and return `shared/schemas/harness-evaluation@2.json`.\nplugins/scribe/README.md:130:`scribe/verify-spec` checks source grounding; `audit-spec` checks internal quality; `audit-architecture` checks system fit. `scribe/architect` loads `shared/references/architecture/remediation.md` for the persisted-model location and language evidence. After Smith verifies the structural change, `audit-architecture` refreshes the model with the new boundary and invariant.\nplugins/ranger/README.md:136:| File found | Language | Hazard reference loaded |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:138:| `Cargo.toml` | Rust | `shared/references/hazards/rust.md` and/or `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md`, per agent scope |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:139:| `package.json` | TypeScript / JavaScript | `shared/references/hazards/typescript.md` and/or `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md`, per agent scope |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:140:| `pyproject.toml`, `requirements.txt`, Python files | Python | `shared/references/hazards/python.md` and/or `shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md` |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:141:| `go.mod`, Go files | Go | `shared/references/hazards/go.md` and/or `shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md` |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:149:| `shared/references/hazards/rust.md` | Rust T1-T6, T8, and T9 candidate, confirmation, and refutation evidence | scanner (always), adversary (non-T7/T10 candidates) |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:150:| `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md` | Rust taxonomies T7 and T10 — boundary-tracer's entire scope | boundary-tracer (always), scanner (full scans), adversary (T7/T10 candidates) |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:151:| `shared/references/hazards/typescript.md` | TypeScript/JavaScript T1-T6, T8, and T9 candidate, confirmation, and refutation evidence | scanner (always), adversary (non-T7/T10 candidates) |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:152:| `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md` | TypeScript taxonomies T7 and T10 — boundary-tracer's entire scope | boundary-tracer (always), scanner (full scans), adversary (T7/T10 candidates) |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:153:| `shared/references/hazards/python.md` | Python taxonomies outside T7/T10 | scanner, adversary |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:154:| `shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md` | Python T7/T10 boundary hazards | scanner, boundary-tracer, adversary |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:155:| `shared/references/hazards/go.md` | Go taxonomies outside T7/T10 | scanner, adversary |\nplugins/ranger/README.md:156:| `shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md` | Go T7/T10 boundary hazards | scanner, boundary-tracer, adversary |\nharnesses/codex/plugins/mason/skills/scaffold-plugin/SKILL.md:25:- Which runtime references need outcome, applicability, evidence, refutation, and disposition guidance. Do not universalize one codebase's preference or omit a named language or platform.\nREADME.md:290:Runtime guides live in `shared/references/`. Paths start with the decision an agent is making; language is the filename only when the evidence is language-specific. Agents load exact files during execution, not this index at startup.\nREADME.md:301:| `tooling/` | Repository tool preferences |\nREADME.md:303:See [`shared/references/README.md`](./shared/references/README.md) for the maintainer map.\nREADME.md:321:│   ├── references/               ← Runtime-pullable domain guides (split by concern)\nplugins/mason/README.md:109:| `<load_first>` correctness | Present whenever an agent's goal implies a lookup it can't do from memory; its named reference file actually resolves |\nplugins/mason/README.md:118:| Reference quality | Runtime references state outcome, applicability, evidence, refutation, and disposition; project preferences are not universalized; claimed language/platform coverage is complete |\nplugins/mason/README.md:151:- **Declared context** — runtime references and schemas are explicit, focused, and packaged for each harness\nplugins/mason/README.md:159:- `shared/references/evaluation/behavioral.md` — hidden-oracle evaluation and provenance rules\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---RESULT 3 (exit 0)---\nactual: ['architecture', 'authoring', 'delivery', 'evaluation', 'hazards', 'tooling', 'verification', 'workspace']\nmatch: True\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---RESULT 4 (exit 0)---\ntest_each_runtime_reference_has_a_runtime_caller (tests.test_reference_integrity.ReferenceIntegrityTests) ... ok\ntest_exact_reference_paths_exist (tests.test_reference_integrity.ReferenceIntegrityTests) ... ok\ntest_reference_paths_are_concern_first (tests.test_reference_integrity.ReferenceIntegrityTests) ... ok\ntest_catalog_and_native_source_trees_have_exact_plugin_parity (tests.test_codex_native_sources.CodexNativeSourceTests) ... ok\ntest_delegating_skills_select_packaged_role_cards (tests.test_codex_native_sources.CodexNativeSourceTests) ... ok\ntest_each_native_runtime_reference_is_declared_for_materialization (tests.test_codex_native_sources.CodexNativeSourceTests) ... ok\ntest_every_authored_native_file_is_identical_in_the_release_bundle (tests.test_codex_native_sources.CodexNativeSourceTests) ... ok\ntest_mason_materializes_the_cross_harness_authoring_guide (tests.test_codex_native_sources.CodexNativeSourceTests) ... ok\ntest_native_manifests_and_skill_frontmatter_meet_the_release_contract (tests.test_codex_native_sources.CodexNativeSourceTests) ... ok\ntest_native_skill_sets_match_claude_source_skill_sets (tests.test_codex_native_sources.CodexNativeSourceTests) ... ok\ntest_root_discovery_manifest_points_at_the_generated_bundle (tests.test_codex_native_sources.CodexNativeSourceTests) ... ok\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nRan 11 tests in 0.108s\n\nOK\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08c9a-83b9-7301-a5a4-1fe2b35b276e","create_time":1789065426.798293}}}
