{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:37:26.970Z","ordinal":9178,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0c3176283919dd68016aa2f8e19b7c87d08f74fb86930ec6a4","status":"completed","call_id":"call_9Pk3ydAT3uRNwwc9RwG6Ow6V","name":"exec","input":"const results = await Promise.all([\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk rg -n --glob '!dist/**' --glob '!**/CHANGELOG.md' '\\\\*-hazards|hazards-t7-t10|python-\\\\*|go-\\\\*|rust-\\\\*|typescript-\\\\*|smells\\\\.md|tooling\\\\.md|implementation-review\\\\.md|architecture-remediation\\\\.md|boundary-value-shapes\\\\.md|interface-implementers\\\\.md' plugins harnesses shared README.md ARCHITECTURE.md CONTRIBUTING.md AGENTS.md docs\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":30000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk rg -n -U '<load_first>[\\\\s\\\\S]*?</load_first>' plugins --glob '*.md'\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":40000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk rg -n --glob '!dist/**' --glob '!**/CHANGELOG.md' 'grep_pattern|grep pattern|pattern matching|pattern-matching' plugins/ranger harnesses/codex/plugins/ranger shared/references/hazards shared/schemas/candidate@1.json docs/pipeline-walkthrough.md README.md ARCHITECTURE.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":30000})\n]); for (let i=0;i<results.length;i++) text(`---RESULT ${i+1} (exit ${results[i].exit_code})---\\n${results[i].output}`);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08c9a-83b9-7301-a5a4-1fe2b35b276e","create_time":1789065436.257062}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:37:27.077Z","ordinal":9179,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a08c9a-83b9-7301-a5a4-1fe2b35b276e","session_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","root_turn_id":"01a08c9a-83b9-7301-a5a4-1fe2b35b276e","response_id":"resp_0c3176283919dd68016aa2f8dc05f487d08e8bbb085f4ab460","usage":{"input_tokens":204348,"cached_input_tokens":198784,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":534,"reasoning_output_tokens":163,"total_tokens":204882},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1737177,"cached_input_tokens":1715072,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":4981,"reasoning_output_tokens":2185,"total_tokens":1742158},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":135609297,"cached_input_tokens":132785408,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":591633,"reasoning_output_tokens":197307,"total_tokens":136200930}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:37:27.121Z","ordinal":9180,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a08c9a-83b9-7301-a5a4-1fe2b35b276e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a561296a-3169-4029-a297-c1b2bd1afcf1","process_id":"83133","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rtk rg -n --glob '!dist/**' --glob '!**/CHANGELOG.md' 'grep_pattern|grep pattern|pattern matching|pattern-matching' plugins/ranger harnesses/codex/plugins/ranger shared/references/hazards shared/schemas/candidate@1.json docs/pipeline-walkthrough.md README.md ARCHITECTURE.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk rg -n --glob '!dist/**' --glob '!**/CHANGELOG.md' 'grep_pattern|grep pattern|pattern matching|pattern-matching' plugins/ranger harnesses/codex/plugins/ranger shared/references/hazards shared/schemas/candidate@1.json docs/pipeline-walkthrough.md README.md ARCHITECTURE.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"ARCHITECTURE.md:240:- A scanner (exhaustive pattern matching, no filtering) and an adversary (default-to-skepticism, requires a concrete failing scenario) cannot share a mental mode — combining them produces an agent worse at both\nREADME.md:239:- A scanner (exhaustive pattern matching, no filtering) and an adversary (default-to-skepticism, requires a concrete failing scenario) cannot share a mental mode — combining them produces an agent worse at both\nshared/schemas/candidate@1.json:31:    \"grep_pattern\": {\nshared/schemas/candidate@1.json:33:      \"description\": \"The grep pattern that produced this match — for traceability\"\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:34:Run every hazard taxonomy grep pattern from the loaded reference against every live file and emit a candidate@1 entry for each match, so the adversary has a complete set of candidates to work with.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:38:The scan is complete when every grep pattern from every applicable taxonomy has been run against every file in live_files, and every match has produced a candidate entry.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:46:Use your search tool to run each grep pattern from the loaded hazard reference against live files. For each match, use your file reading tool to read surrounding code (enough to populate excerpt and taxonomy fields). Do not scan dead_files.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:58:    \"grep_pattern\": \"string\"\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"ARCHITECTURE.md:240:- A scanner (exhaustive pattern matching, no filtering) and an adversary (default-to-skepticism, requires a concrete failing scenario) cannot share a mental mode — combining them produces an agent worse at both\nREADME.md:239:- A scanner (exhaustive pattern matching, no filtering) and an adversary (default-to-skepticism, requires a concrete failing scenario) cannot share a mental mode — combining them produces an agent worse at both\nshared/schemas/candidate@1.json:31:    \"grep_pattern\": {\nshared/schemas/candidate@1.json:33:      \"description\": \"The grep pattern that produced this match — for traceability\"\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:34:Run every hazard taxonomy grep pattern from the loaded reference against every live file and emit a candidate@1 entry for each match, so the adversary has a complete set of candidates to work with.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:38:The scan is complete when every grep pattern from every applicable taxonomy has been run against every file in live_files, and every match has produced a candidate entry.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:46:Use your search tool to run each grep pattern from the loaded hazard reference against live files. For each match, use your file reading tool to read surrounding code (enough to populate excerpt and taxonomy fields). Do not scan dead_files.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:58:    \"grep_pattern\": \"string\"\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":417},"formatted_output":"ARCHITECTURE.md:240:- A scanner (exhaustive pattern matching, no filtering) and an adversary (default-to-skepticism, requires a concrete failing scenario) cannot share a mental mode — combining them produces an agent worse at both\nREADME.md:239:- A scanner (exhaustive pattern matching, no filtering) and an adversary (default-to-skepticism, requires a concrete failing scenario) cannot share a mental mode — combining them produces an agent worse at both\nshared/schemas/candidate@1.json:31:    \"grep_pattern\": {\nshared/schemas/candidate@1.json:33:      \"description\": \"The grep pattern that produced this match — for traceability\"\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:34:Run every hazard taxonomy grep pattern from the loaded reference against every live file and emit a candidate@1 entry for each match, so the adversary has a complete set of candidates to work with.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:38:The scan is complete when every grep pattern from every applicable taxonomy has been run against every file in live_files, and every match has produced a candidate entry.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:46:Use your search tool to run each grep pattern from the loaded hazard reference against live files. For each match, use your file reading tool to read surrounding code (enough to populate excerpt and taxonomy fields). Do not scan dead_files.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:58:    \"grep_pattern\": \"string\"\n"},"started_at_ms":1789065447121,"completed_at_ms":1789065447121}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:37:27.122Z","ordinal":9181,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a08c9a-83b9-7301-a5a4-1fe2b35b276e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-4a27c3cc-9f36-4ccd-98c3-77c26c080311","process_id":"51144","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rtk rg -n -U '<load_first>[\\s\\S]*?</load_first>' plugins --glob '*.md'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk rg -n -U '<load_first>[\\s\\S]*?</load_first>' plugins --glob '*.md'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"plugins/scribe/agents/arch-auditor.md:18:<load_first>\nplugins/scribe/agents/arch-auditor.md:19:Load `shared/references/workspace/conventions.md` before searching for the persisted model — it names where the architecture model and gated specs live on disk, and what an absent model does and doesn't prove.\nplugins/scribe/agents/arch-auditor.md:20:</load_first>\nplugins/navigator/agents/challenger.md:18:<load_first>\nplugins/navigator/agents/challenger.md:19:When a task changes a shared trait, interface, protocol, or one implementation, load `shared/references/verification/interface-coverage.md` before evaluating interface-incompleteness. Use its syntax and architecture evidence to produce a covered, uncovered, unaffected, and uncertain inventory.\nplugins/navigator/agents/challenger.md:20:</load_first>\nplugins/smith/agents/implementer.md:18:<load_first>\nplugins/smith/agents/implementer.md:19:Load `shared/references/verification/evidence.md` when the task has boundary, input-space, environment, or external-state risk. Load `shared/references/architecture/boundary-values.md` when a value can be absent, wrong, or stale. Load `shared/references/authoring/comments.md` when the diff changes comments.\nplugins/smith/agents/implementer.md:20:</load_first>\nplugins/scribe/agents/architect.md:18:<load_first>\nplugins/scribe/agents/architect.m