0:</load_first>\nplugins/scribe/agents/architect.md:18:<load_first>\nplugins/scribe/agents/architect.md:19:Load `shared/references/architecture/remediation.md`. It routes to the persisted-model and language evidence required for this design.\nplugins/scribe/agents/architect.md:20:</load_first>\nplugins/scribe/agents/auditor.md:18:<load_first>\nplugins/scribe/agents/auditor.md:19:Load `shared/references/workspace/conventions.md` before checking scope-overlap or boundary-round-trip — it names where other gated specs live on disk and what an empty search there does and doesn't prove.\nplugins/scribe/agents/auditor.md:20:</load_first>\nplugins/ranger/agents/adversary.md:18:<load_first>\nplugins/ranger/agents/adversary.md:19:Check the input candidate@1's `taxonomy` field first, then load only what that one taxonomy needs:\nplugins/ranger/agents/adversary.md:20:- taxonomy is T7 or T10: load the matching `*-hazards-t7-t10.md`\nplugins/ranger/agents/adversary.md:21:- any other taxonomy: load the matching `*-hazards.md`\nplugins/ranger/agents/adversary.md:22:Select Rust, TypeScript/JavaScript, Python, or Go from `workspace-manifest@1.language_files`. Never load two language packs for one candidate.\nplugins/ranger/agents/adversary.md:23:</load_first>\nplugins/ranger/agents/boundary-tracer.md:19:<load_first>\nplugins/ranger/agents/boundary-tracer.md:20:Load the matching `*-hazards-t7-t10.md` for the candidate language declared in\nplugins/ranger/agents/boundary-tracer.md:21:`workspace-manifest@1.language_files`: Rust, TypeScript/JavaScript, Python, or Go.\nplugins/ranger/agents/boundary-tracer.md:22:Load one language pack per candidate. Do not load the full hazards file.\nplugins/ranger/agents/boundary-tracer.md:23:</load_first>\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:18:<load_first>\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:19:Full scan: load both files for each detected language:\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:20:\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:21:- Rust: `shared/references/hazards/rust.md` and `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md`.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:22:- TypeScript or JavaScript: `shared/references/hazards/typescript.md` and `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md`.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:23:- Python: `shared/references/hazards/python.md` and `shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md`.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:24:- Go: `shared/references/hazards/go.md` and `shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md`.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:25:\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:26:Focused scan: load only the applicable file from that list; T7 and T10 use the boundary file.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:27:</load_first>\nplugins/smith/agents/mutator.md:18:<load_first>\nplugins/smith/agents/mutator.md:19:For Rust workspaces: shared/references/verification/rust.md\nplugins/smith/agents/mutator.md:20:For TypeScript/JavaScript workspaces: shared/references/verification/typescript.md\nplugins/smith/agents/mutator.md:21:For Python workspaces: shared/references/verification/python.md\nplugins/smith/agents/mutator.md:22:For Go workspaces: shared/references/verification/go.md\nplugins/smith/agents/mutator.md:23:</load_first>\nplugins/weaver/agents/auditor.md:18:<load_first>\nplugins/weaver/agents/auditor.md:19:Load `shared/references/workspace/conventions.md` before searching for spec or plan coverage — it names where gated specs and persisted plans live on disk, and what an empty search there does and doesn't prove.\nplugins/weaver/agents/auditor.md:20:</load_first>\nplugins/mason/agents/evaluation-runner.md:19:<load_first>\nplugins/mason/agents/evaluation-runner.md:20:Load `shared/references/evaluation/behavioral.md`. Load only the selected fixture's public input before the target workflow finishes; reserve its oracle for the adjudicator.\nplugins/mason/agents/evaluation-runner.md:21:</load_first>\nplugins/courier/agents/changeset-analyzer.md:18:<load_first>\nplugins/courier/agents/changes