e the plan mechanically.\",\nplugins/navigator/agents/estimator.md:7:  Delegate to this subagent when a plan@1 exists and you need a rough effort estimate before committing to execution. Input is a plan@1 JSON object. The agent produces a per-task time estimate in minutes, marks each task as parallelizable or sequential, lists blocking dependencies by task ID, and produces a total_minutes sum with explicit assumptions. The implementer is assumed to have full codebase context but no domain knowledge of the feature being built. A task is marked parallelizable only if it has no dependency on any other task in the current plan. All assumptions affecting the estimate are listed explicitly in an assumptions array. Output is a JSON object with total_minutes, a tasks array, and assumptions.\nplugins/navigator/agents/estimator.md:23:Given a plan@1, produce a per-task time estimate in minutes for a competent developer who has full codebase context but no domain knowledge of the feature. Identify which tasks can run in parallel and which must run sequentially. Surface every assumption that affects the estimates.\nshared/schemas/plan@1.json:5:  \"description\": \"A sequenced implementation plan. Every task is bite-sized, with an implementation approach, exact code, the tests proving each criterion, and a commit message.\",\nshared/schemas/plan@1.json:46:            \"description\": \"Ordered steps. Each step is one action. Code steps include exact code. Test steps include exact command and expected output.\"\n"},"started_at_ms":1789065508898,"completed_at_ms":1789065508899}}
