{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:38:43.270Z","ordinal":9228,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a08c9a-83b9-7301-a5a4-1fe2b35b276e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-aae131e6-8fa4-4c2c-a4a8-5e924f230a91","process_id":"67276","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rtk rg -n --glob '!dist/**' --glob '!**/CHANGELOG.md' '\\b(38|39|40|41|42|43|44) (agent|file)|all [0-9]+ agents|one-reference-file' README.md AGENTS.md CONTRIBUTING.md ARCHITECTURE.md docs plugins shared harnesses/codex"],"cwd":"file:///Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk rg -n --glob '!dist/**' --glob '!**/CHANGELOG.md' '\\b(38|39|40|41|42|43|44) (agent|file)|all [0-9]+ agents|one-reference-file' README.md AGENTS.md CONTRIBUTING.md ARCHITECTURE.md docs plugins shared harnesses/codex"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"docs/adr/006-constitution-section-five-part-structure.md:9:`constitution.md`'s Static Prompt Prefix Invariant and `agent-best-practices.md` §7 both claimed every agent prompt shared an identical static header for prompt-cache reuse. In practice no agent file had one — each of the 38 agent bodies started directly with `<backstory>` (or a `<load_first>` block), meaning the \"identical header\" was aspirational, not real, and rules meant to be ecosystem-wide (trust boundaries, output economy, reader-scoped writing, abstract tool language) were either copy-pasted with wording drift into whichever agents happened to need them, or silently absent elsewhere. A literal fix — identical content at the true start of every prompt — conflicted with two existing rules: the 4-part structure being described as exhaustive (\"not 5 sections\"), and EARS notation being confined to `<output>` only, which meant shared EARS content had no section that was both first and permitted to hold it.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"docs/adr/006-constitution-section-five-part-structure.md:9:`constitution.md`'s Static Prompt Prefix Invariant and `agent-best-practices.md` §7 both claimed every agent prompt shared an identical static header for prompt-cache reuse. In practice no agent file had one — each of the 38 agent bodies started directly with `<backstory>` (or a `<load_first>` block), meaning the \"identical header\" was aspirational, not real, and rules meant to be ecosystem-wide (trust boundaries, output economy, reader-scoped writing, abstract tool language) were either copy-pasted with wording drift into whichever agents happened to need them, or silently absent elsewhere. A literal fix — identical content at the true start of every prompt — conflicted with two existing rules: the 4-part structure being described as exhaustive (\"not 5 sections\"), and EARS notation being confined to `<output>` only, which meant shared EARS content had no section that was both first and permitted to hold it.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":875},"formatted_output":"docs/adr/006-constitution-section-five-part-structure.md:9:`constitution.md`'s Static Prompt Prefix Invariant and `agent-best-practices.md` §7 both claimed every agent prompt shared an identical static header for prompt-cache reuse. In practice no agent file had one — each of the 38 agent bodies started directly with `<backstory>` (or a `<load_first>` block), meaning the \"identical header\" was aspirational, not real, and rules meant to be ecosystem-wide (trust boundaries, output economy, reader-scoped writing, abstract tool language) were either copy-pasted with wording drift into whichever agents happened to need them, or silently absent elsewhere. A literal fix — identical content at the true start of every prompt — conflicted with two existing rules: the 4-part structure being described as exhaustive (\"not 5 sections\"), and EARS notation being confined to `<output>` only, which meant shared EARS content had no section that was both first and permitted to hold it.\n"},"started_at_ms":1789065523270,"completed_at_ms":1789065523270}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:38:43.291Z","ordinal":9229,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a08c9a-83b9-7301-a5a4-1fe2b35b276e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-bf8cf7c8-2b55-4362-8271-eab638d5a685","process_id":"9645","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rtk jq -r '.plugins[] | [.id,.version,.description] | @tsv' marketplace.json && rtk rg -n '^\\*\\*Stage:.*\\*\\*Version:' plugins/*/README.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk jq -r '.plugins[] | [.id,.version,.description] | @tsv' marketplace.json && rtk rg -n '^\\*\\*Stage:.*\\*\\*Version:' plugins/*/README.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"mason\t3.2.2\tBuild, audit, and behaviorally evaluate plugins; design shared schemas and scaffold conformant agents. Skills: scaffold-plugin, audit-plugin, design-schema, scaffold-subagent, evaluate.\nranger\t3.2.2\tBug hunting for Rust, TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, and Go. Confirms reachable defects, searches semantic siblings, and routes structural families for architectural correction.\nsentinel\t2.1.1\tCross-cutting verification gate. Confirms that any stage artifact meets its criteria before the next stage begins. One skill, one recon-verify-judge pipeline, reused unchanged against any artifact type.\nweaver\t3.0.3\tNeed definition plugin. Captures and structures requirements before implementation begins. Integrates with GitHub Issues by default; extensible to Linear, Jira, or any issue tracker that produces the requirement@1 schema. Skills: capture-need, clarify-requirement, prioritize-backlog, connect-requirement, audit-backlog.\nvanguard\t2.0.2\tResearch plugin. Investigates questions and requirements to build a documented evidence base before committing to a solution direction. Produces research-report@1 for consumption by scribe (spec).\nscribe\t3.3.2\tSpecification plugin. Turns requirements and research reports into unambiguous, testable specs. Checks specs against a persisted whole-system architecture model. Detects spec drift against actual code. Skills: draft-spec, verify-spec, spec-drift, audit-spec, audit-architecture, gate-spec, correct-spec, architect.\nmuse\t1.0.1\tComponent specification plugin. Turns UI/design intent into unambiguous, testable component specs — props, variants, per-state behavior, and accessibility criteria as testable propositions, gated before planning. Audits the spec, not the implementation — see ranger's accessibility hazard taxonomy for code-level scanning.\nnavigator\t2.3.2\tPlanning plugin. Decomposes specs into sequenced, bite-sized implementation plans with an implementation approach, exact code as a baseline, and the tests proving each criterion — no write-test-first mandate. Tasks are sized to compilation boundaries, not a clock-time estimate. No TBDs. A developer with zero domain context can execute the plan mechanically.\nsmith\t2.4.2\tImplementation plugin. Executes tested plan batches, verifies risk at real boundaries, searches semantic defect siblings, and escalates shared model or architecture gaps.\ncourier\t3.0.3\tShipping plugin. Shepherds completed code through commit, PR creation, review response, and changeset documentation. Skills: commit, pr, changeset, receive-feedback, post-review, release.\n\nplugins/sentinel/README.md:3:**Stage:** Gate · **Output:** `verdict@3` · **Version:** 2.1.1\nplugins/weaver/README.md:3:**Stage:** Need · **Output:** `requirement@1` · **Version:** 3.0.3\nplugins/navigator/README.md:3:**Stage:** Plan · **Output:** `plan@1` · **Version:** 2.3.2\nplugins/muse/README.md:3:**Stage:** Design · **Output:** `spec@1` · **Version:** 1.0.1\nplugins/scribe/README.md:3:**Stage:** Spec · **Output:** `spec@1` · **Version:** 3.3.2\nplugins/ranger/README.md:3:**Stage:** Cross-cutting · **Output:** `finding-report@2` · **Version:** 3.2.2\nplugins/mason/README.md:3:**Stage:** Meta · **Output:** plugin artifacts and evaluations · **Version:** 3.2.2\nplugins/smith/README.md:3:**Stage:** Code · **Output:** code, `implementation-review@2`, `verdict@3` · **Version:** 2.4.2\nplugins/vanguard/README.md:3:**Stage:** Research · **Output:** `research-report@1` · **Version:** 2.0.2\nplugins/courier/README.md:3:**Stage:** Ship · **Output:** `release-artifact@2` · **Version:** 3.0.3\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"mason\t3.2.2\tBuild, audit, and behaviorally evaluate plugins; design shared schemas and scaffold conformant agents. Skills: scaffold-plugin, audit-plugin, design-schema, scaffold-subagent, evaluate.\nranger\t3.2.2\tBug hunting for Rust, TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, and Go. Confirms reachable defects, searches semantic siblings, and routes structural families for architectural correction.\nsentinel\t2.1.1\tCross-cutting verification gate. Confirms that any stage artifact meets its criteria before the next stage begins. One skill, one recon-verify-judge pipeline, reused unchanged against any artifact type.\nweaver\t3.0.3\tNeed definition plugin. Captures and structures requirements before implementation begins. Integrates with GitHub Issues by default; extensible to Linear, Jira, or any issue tracker that produces the requirement@1 schema. Skills: capture-need, clarify-requirement, prioritize-backlog, connect-requirement, audit-backlog.\nvanguard\t2.0.2\tResearch plugin. Investigates questions and requirements to build a documented evidence base before committing to a solution direction. Produces research-report@1 for consumption by scribe (spec).\nscribe\t3.3.2\tSpecification plugin. Turns requirements and research reports into unambiguous, testable specs. Checks specs against a persisted whole-system architecture model. Detects spec drift against actual code. Skills: draft-spec, verify-spec, spec-drift, audit-spec, audit-architecture, gate-spec, correct-spec, architect.\nmuse\t1.0.1\tComponent specification plugin. Turns UI/design intent into unambiguous, testable component specs — props, variants, per-state behavior, and accessibility criteria as testable propositions, gated before planning. Audits the spec, not the implementation — see ranger's accessibility hazard taxonomy for code-level scanning.\nnavigator\t2.3.2\tPlanning plugin. Decomposes specs into sequenced, bite-sized implementation plans with an implementation approach, exact code as a baseline, and the tests proving each criterion — no write-test-first mandate. Tasks are sized to compilation boundaries, not a clock-time estimate. No TBDs. A developer with zero domain context can execute the plan mechanically.\nsmith\t2.4.2\tImplementation plugin. Executes tested plan batches, verifies risk at real boundaries, searches semantic defect siblings, and escalates shared model or architecture gaps.\ncourier\t3.0.3\tShipping plugin. Shepherds completed code through commit, PR creation, review response, and changeset documentation. Skills: commit, pr, changeset, receive-feedback, post-review, release.\n\nplugins/sentinel/README.md:3:**Stage:** Gate · **Output:** `verdict@3` · **Version:** 2.1.1\nplugins/weaver/README.md:3:**Stage:** Need · **Output:** `requirement@1` · **Version:** 3.0.3\nplugins/navigator/README.md:3:**Stage:** Plan · **Output:** `plan@1` · **Version:** 2.3.2\nplugins/muse/README.md:3:**Stage:** Design · **Output:** `spec@1` · **Version:** 1.0.1\nplugins/scribe/README.md:3:**Stage:** Spec · **Output:** `spec@1` · **Version:** 3.3.2\nplugins/ranger/README.md:3:**Stage:** Cross-cutting · **Output:** `finding-report@2` · **Version:** 3.2.2\nplugins/mason/README.md:3:**Stage:** Meta · **Output:** plugin artifacts and evaluations · **Version:** 3.2.2\nplugins/smith/README.md:3:**Stage:** Code · **Output:** code, `implementation-review@2`, `verdict@3` · **Version:** 2.4.2\nplugins/vanguard/README.md:3:**Stage:** Research · **Output:** `research-report@1` · **Version:** 2.0.2\nplugins/courier/README.md:3:**Stage:** Ship · **Output:** `release-artifact@2` · **Version:** 3.0.3\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":2333},"formatted_output":"mason\t3.2.2\tBuild, audit, and behaviorally evaluate plugins; design shared schemas and scaffold conformant agents. Skills: scaffold-plugin, audit-plugin, design-schema, scaffold-subagent, evaluate.\nranger\t3.2.2\tBug hunting for Rust, TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, and Go. Confirms reachable defects, searches semantic siblings, and routes structural families for architectural correction.\nsentinel\t2.1.1\tCross-cutting verification gate. Confirms that any stage artifact meets its criteria before the next stage begins. One skill, one recon-verify-judge pipeline, reused unchanged against any artifact type.\nweaver\t3.0.3\tNeed definition plugin. Captures and structures requirements before implementation begins. Integrates with GitHub Issues by default; extensible to Linear, Jira, or any issue tracker that produces the requirement@1 schema. Skills: capture-need, clarify-requirement, prioritize-backlog, connect-requirement, audit-backlog.\nvanguard\t2.0.2\tResearch plugin. Investigates questions and requirements to build a documented evidence base before committing to a solution direction. Produces research-report@1 for consumption by scribe (spec).\nscribe\t3.3.2\tSpecification plugin. Turns requirements and research reports into unambiguous, testable specs. Checks specs against a persisted whole-system architecture model. Detects spec drift against actual code. Skills: draft-spec, verify-spec, spec-drift, audit-spec, audit-architecture, gate-spec, correct-spec, architect.\nmuse\t1.0.1\tComponent specification plugin. Turns UI/design intent into unambiguous, testable component specs — props, variants, per-state behavior, and accessibility criteria as testable propositions, gated before planning. Audits the spec, not the implementation — see ranger's accessibility hazard taxonomy for code-level scanning.\nnavigator\t2.3.2\tPlanning plugin. Decomposes specs into sequenced, bite-sized implementation plans with an implementation approach, exact code as a baseline, and the tests proving each criterion — no write-test-first mandate. Tasks are sized to compilation boundaries, not a clock-time estimate. No TBDs. A developer with zero domain context can execute the plan mechanically.\nsmith\t2.4.2\tImplementation plugin. Executes tested plan batches, verifies risk at real boundaries, searches semantic defect siblings, and escalates shared model or architecture gaps.\ncourier\t3.0.3\tShipping plugin. Shepherds completed code through commit, PR creation, review response, and changeset documentation. Skills: commit, pr, changeset, receive-feedback, post-review, release.\n\nplugins/sentinel/README.md:3:**Stage:** Gate · **Output:** `verdict@3` · **Version:** 2.1.1\nplugins/weaver/README.md:3:**Stage:** Need · **Output:** `requirement@1` · **Version:** 3.0.3\nplugins/navigator/README.md:3:**Stage:** Plan · **Output:** `plan@1` · **Version:** 2.3.2\nplugins/muse/README.md:3:**Stage:** Design · **Output:** `spec@1` · **Version:** 1.0.1\nplugins/scribe/README.md:3:**Stage:** Spec · **Output:** `spec@1` · **Version:** 3.3.2\nplugins/ranger/README.md:3:**Stage:** Cross-cutting · **Output:** `finding-report@2` · **Version:** 3.2.2\nplugins/mason/README.md:3:**Stage:** Meta · **Output:** plugin artifacts and evaluations · **Version:** 3.2.2\nplugins/smith/README.md:3:**Stage:** Code · **Output:** code, `implementation-review@2`, `verdict@3` · **Version:** 2.4.2\nplugins/vanguard/README.md:3:**Stage:** Research · **Output:** `research-report@1` · **Version:** 2.0.2\nplugins/courier/README.md:3:**Stage:** Ship · **Output:** `release-artifact@2` · **Version:** 3.0.3\n"},"started_at_ms":1789065523291,"completed_at_ms":1789065523291}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:38:43.338Z","ordinal":9230,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a08c9d-708a-7cd3-bb4c-fbaa0730a85d","call_id":"call_ql2BqWvf3aDK3dk34BluDZUP","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---RESULT 1 (exit 0)---\ndocs/adr/006-constitution-section-five-part-structure.md:9:`constitution.md`'s Static Prompt Prefix Invariant and `agent-best-practices.md` §7 both claimed every agent prompt shared an identical static header for prompt-cache reuse. In practice no agent file had one — each of the 38 agent bodies started directly with `<backstory>` (or a `<load_first>` block), meaning the \"identical header\" was aspirational, not real, and rules meant to be ecosystem-wide (trust boundaries, output economy, reader-scoped writing, abstract tool language) were either copy-pasted with wording drift into whichever agents happened to need them, or silently absent elsewhere. A literal fix — identical content at the true start of every prompt — conflicted with two existing rules: the 4-part structure being described as exhaustive (\"not 5 sections\"), and EARS notation being confined to `<output>` only, which meant shared EARS content had no section that was both first and permitted to hold it.\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---RESULT 2 (exit 0)---\nCONTRIBUTING.md:180:- [ ] New references live under the reader's concern, have a real caller, and update `shared/references/README.md` when they introduce a concern\nREADME.md:303:See [`shared/references/README.md`](./shared/references/README.md) for the maintainer map.\nshared/schemas/changeset@2.json:18:      \"description\": \"Whether this change is observable to someone outside this repo. See shared/references/changesets.md for classification rules.\"\nshared/schemas/changeset@2.json:23:      \"description\": \"Version bump this change requires, per the Semver Decision Guide in shared/references/changesets.md. release-summarizer takes max(semver_impact) across a release's changesets rather than re-deriving it.\"\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---RESULT 3 (exit 0)---\ndocs/adr/003-cognitive-mode-separation.md:8:Early plugin agents combined scanning and analysis in a single invocation — a single agent would grep for hazards and then assess whether each match was a real bug. This produced agents that were worse at both jobs: the scanner filtered matches because they \"looked harmless,\" creating false negatives the downstream agent could never recover; the analyst had insufficient depth because it was also doing exhaustive enumeration. The alternative considered was one agent per cognitive mode.\nplugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:34:Run every hazard taxonomy grep pattern from the loaded reference against every live file and emit a candidate@1 entry for each match, so the adversary has a complete set of candidates to work with.\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---RESULT 4 (exit 0)---\nmason\t3.2.2\tBuild, audit, and behaviorally evaluate plugins; design shared schemas and scaffold conformant agents. Skills: scaffold-plugin, audit-plugin, design-schema, scaffold-subagent, evaluate.\nranger\t3.2.2\tBug hunting for Rust, TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, and Go. Confirms reachable defects, searches semantic siblings, and routes structural families for architectural correction.\nsentinel\t2.1.1\tCross-cutting verification gate. Confirms that any stage artifact meets its criteria before the next stage begins. One skill, one recon-verify-judge pipeline, reused unchanged against any artifact type.\nweaver\t3.0.3\tNeed definition plugin. Captures and structures requirements before implementation begins. Integrates with GitHub Issues by default; extensible to Linear, Jira, or any issue tracker that produces the requirement@1 schema. Skills: capture-need, clarify-requirement, prioritize-backlog, connect-requirement, audit-backlog.\nvanguard\t2.0.2\tResearch plugin. Investigates questions and requirements to build a documented evidence base before committing to a solution direction. Produces research-report@1 for consumption by scribe (spec).\nscribe\t3.3.2\tSpecification plugin. Turns requirements and research reports into unambiguous, testable specs. Checks specs against a persisted whole-system architecture model. Detects spec drift against actual code. Skills: draft-spec, verify-spec, spec-drift, audit-spec, audit-architecture, gate-spec, correct-spec, architect.\nmuse\t1.0.1\tComponent specification plugin. Turns UI/design intent into unambiguous, testable component specs — props, variants, per-state behavior, and accessibility criteria as testable propositions, gated before planning. Audits the spec, not the implementation — see ranger's accessibility hazard taxonomy for code-level scanning.\nnavigator\t2.3.2\tPlanning plugin. Decomposes specs into sequenced, bite-sized implementation plans with an implementation approach, exact code as a baseline, and the tests proving each criterion — no write-test-first mandate. Tasks are sized to compilation boundaries, not a clock-time estimate. No TBDs. A developer with zero domain context can execute the plan mechanically.\nsmith\t2.4.2\tImplementation plugin. Executes tested plan batches, verifies risk at real boundaries, searches semantic defect siblings, and escalates shared model or architecture gaps.\ncourier\t3.0.3\tShipping plugin. Shepherds completed code through commit, PR creation, review response, and changeset documentation. Skills: commit, pr, changeset, receive-feedback, post-review, release.\n\nplugins/sentinel/README.md:3:**Stage:** Gate · **Output:** `verdict@3` · **Version:** 2.1.1\nplugins/weaver/README.md:3:**Stage:** Need · **Output:** `requirement@1` · **Version:** 3.0.3\nplugins/navigator/README.md:3:**Stage:** Plan · **Output:** `plan@1` · **Version:** 2.3.2\nplugins/muse/README.md:3:**Stage:** Design · **Output:** `spec@1` · **Version:** 1.0.1\nplugins/scribe/README.md:3:**Stage:** Spec · **Output:** `spec@1` · **Version:** 3.3.2\nplugins/ranger/README.md:3:**Stage:** Cross-cutting · **Output:** `finding-report@2` · **Version:** 3.2.2\nplugins/mason/README.md:3:**Stage:** Meta · **Output:** plugin artifacts and evaluations · **Version:** 3.2.2\nplugins/smith/README.md:3:**Stage:** Code · **Output:** code, `implementation-review@2`, `verdict@3` · **Version:** 2.4.2\nplugins/vanguard/README.md:3:**Stage:** Research · **Output:** `research-report@1` · **Version:** 2.0.2\nplugins/courier/README.md:3:**Stage:** Ship · **Output:** `release-artifact@2` · **Version:** 3.0.3\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08c9a-83b9-7301-a5a4-1fe2b35b276e","create_time":1789065523.338799}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:38:43.339Z","ordinal":9231,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"token_count","info":{"total_token_usage":{"input_tokens":134692383,"cached_input_tokens":131882752,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":559841,"reasoning_output_tokens":199119,"total_tokens":135252224},"last_token_usage":{"input_tokens":217295,"cached_input_tokens":214784,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":586,"reasoning_output_tokens":148,"total_tokens":217881},"model_context_window":258400},"rate_limits":{"limit_id":"codex","limit_name":null,"primary":{"used_percent":61.0,"window_minutes":10080,"resets_at":1789436456},"secondary":null,"credits":{"has_credits":false,"unlimited":false,"balance":"0"},"individual_limit":null,"spend_control_reached":null,"plan_type":"prolite","rate_limit_reached_type":null}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:39:40.789Z","ordinal":9232,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a08c9a-83b9-7301-a5a4-1fe2b35b276e","session_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","root_turn_id":"01a08c9a-83b9-7301-a5a4-1fe2b35b276e","response_id":"resp_0c3176283919dd68016aa2f933a19087d0a997e7feded78de0","usage":{"input_tokens":217918,"cached_input_tokens":217088,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2998,"reasoning_output_tokens":0,"total_tokens":220916},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":3231042,"cached_input_tokens":3194112,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":10820,"reasoning_output_tokens":3997,"total_tokens":3241862},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":137103162,"cached_input_tokens":134264448,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":597472,"reasoning_output_tokens":199119,"total_tokens":137700634}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:39:40.799Z","ordinal":9233,"type":"compacted","payload":{"compaction_response_id":"resp_0c3176283919dd68016aa2f933a19087d0a997e7feded78de0","first_window_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-8408eea684cf","guardian_history":[{"content":[{"text":"I think we have some ongoing changes here right?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a086d4-4225-7fc1-85b1-e90f61d94abb","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788968452.64512,"turn_id":"01a086d4-405a-7e52-9524-a1761266da60"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Also, looking through our agent and skill docs we seem to have wordy prose in bullets which seems to be against our best practices no? Should some of these be broken up in sub-bullets? Is there a better way to organize things for better agent understanding?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a086d5-d773-7f23-a35a-5eeffd8f7a09","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788968556.403109,"turn_id":"01a086d5-d723-7841-9cc6-6e2838635983"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"The current changes should be related to looking for sibling defects and making sure that we consider semantic models and the architecture when looking at defects. If we found multiple considering patterns and what in the model and architecture could be missing that leaves room for these defects","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a086d6-dc3a-7470-b4dd-36a1ec036533","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788968623.162783,"turn_id":"01a086d5-d723-7841-9cc6-6e2838635983"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"We should lean on succinct and direct wording where possible without losing context. Would that help reduce some of the wordiness? We should avoid filler words and unecessary words when simpler and smaller phrases communicate the meaning and intent. How do we guide as such?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a086db-a500-7543-bff0-43683795c3a4","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788968936.704888,"turn_id":"01a086db-a445-7040-9235-c49f09f7349f"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Let's make the guidance and constitution changes and then tackle all of the improvements neceessary, applying this new guidance and constitution to the existing files along with accounting for sibblings, etc","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a086de-fde2-7711-9063-3aba846f7411","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788969156.066345,"turn_id":"01a086de-fd71-7c21-80b9-a036e4ae6eb7"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Some of these read like step by step too much, is that too prescriptive?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a086f0-f734-7ee0-92cb-799ded4e8c8d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788970334.004558,"turn_id":"01a086de-fd71-7c21-80b9-a036e4ae6eb7"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Are we losing some calls to the reference files in all of this? Is this a problem?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08702-0297-7231-b64a-b7df2e282026","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788971451.031161,"turn_id":"01a086de-fd71-7c21-80b9-a036e4ae6eb7"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Any more tweaks or improvements?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0871e-8e0e-79d0-ae73-7d7d09ad3eb7","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788973321.742119,"turn_id":"01a0871e-8ce4-7751-835b-cd43333c7c07"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Let's do that please","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08736-ac01-7500-9092-90473da98e21","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788974902.273279,"turn_id":"01a08736-ab43-7413-9675-c6fb9640c637"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Can we update docs and changelog to update?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08746-5b30-7800-b85a-b182f67f83cf","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788975930.160281,"turn_id":"01a08746-58ca-7ee2-b3ab-a45e43515705"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Let's prep and push a release","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0874e-22cf-71f3-939d-746e33a2b05d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788976440.015354,"turn_id":"01a0874e-1fe2-7811-a0f5-11dd27177d9a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"yes","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0876b-66f4-7f61-9a4e-4cb600293740","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788978358.004292,"turn_id":"01a0876b-6520-79d0-bf92-6ce575103990"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"do it","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08774-f894-7f23-88f2-833f05210b33","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788978985.108383,"turn_id":"01a08774-f7f4-7351-8c26-4473a878c2c6"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Can you read through this: https://danluu.com/agentic-testing/ and understand the methodology and issues outlined?\n\nThen review our callisto sessions from codex and claude looking for places where we did better than luu outline and where we failed just as much. Can we see if we're doing better with our plugins?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08781-c19f-7ab1-a295-ccc6077e34c3","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788979823.007717,"turn_id":"01a08781-c0dc-7360-be2f-39c7fedbf019"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"You might have to keep in mind what versions were available of our plugins at the time of the session too, lots has changed. We might be able to\n  see improvement over time.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08785-6af9-7452-8478-460d8775e293","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788980062.969926,"turn_id":"01a08781-c0dc-7360-be2f-39c7fedbf019"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Have you look at callisto sessions dating back to the past 30-45 days to see progress over time? How does it correlate to changes in our plugins over that time-period?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08791-f5fa-7980-bf02-81982d449441","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788980884.98625,"turn_id":"01a08791-f541-73d1-bfae-acc0ddfc3204"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"I fixed the entire login issue","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08797-873b-78f0-84cf-221e7319e405","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788981249.851112,"turn_id":"01a08797-86ce-7402-86fc-a28c8d7a7e20"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Entire should be logged in for the callisto folder, no?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0879c-2558-70f0-94e7-de77228d5f17","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788981552.472461,"turn_id":"01a0879a-11d2-7102-9864-546a98a6cc23"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Ok, pickup the work then and if not possible to use entire then look through sessions yourself. We have local sessions no?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a087a0-552e-7393-ac06-fed0288e95f8","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788981826.86281,"turn_id":"01a087a0-5473-71e2-9fe3-e5f72a7ea39d"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Let's do what we can with just the sessions. Any further analysis we can do?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a087aa-5d4d-7642-a999-59ff3e6dae0b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788982484.301592,"turn_id":"01a087aa-5c60-7322-a1d4-dc034d402d62"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Let's do that examination please","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a087c3-2c14-7903-986b-5bca64218fb1","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788984110.100166,"turn_id":"01a087c3-2a1e-7401-ac78-e33107544865"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Some feedback from claude but take it with a large grain of salt. It had not access to our sessions like you did.\n\n2. The semantic-sibling search is the part most likely to be theater. Luu's formal-methods finding was that agents technically invoke a tool but prove trivial/irrelevant properties. \"Search for semantic siblings — same domain responsibility expressed differently\" is a much harder, fuzzier ask than syntactic grep, and the schema's only real guardrail is requiring evidence and a match count (including zero). That forces the agent to claim it searched, but doesn't verify the search was any good — an agent could report \"matches\": 0 with a thin evidence string and pass schema validation while having done a shallow pass. Given Luu's finding that agents' shallow-but-plausible-looking outputs are the dominant failure mode, I'd want a spot-check mechanism here — e.g., have exit-gate independently re-run the semantic search on a sample of families rather than trusting reviewer's self-report, the same way exit-gate already refuses to trust remediator's description of a fix.\n\n3. Nothing addresses proptest/fuzzing-style structured input exploration, which Luu found was one of the few things that reliably added value (via shrinking). This ecosystem's testing story is entirely mutation-testing + example-based tests; there's no equivalent of \"generate structured random inputs and shrink the failing case\" anywhere in smith. If bug-prone logic in a target codebase is best caught by property-based exploration rather than hand-written examples, this pipeline has no lever for it at all — mutation testing only tells you your existing tests are weak, not that you're missing a whole input-space region no example covers.\n\n4. Watch the token/instruction-economy tradeoff you're actively making. The new Instruction Economy section is a good instinct (Luu found bloated official skills reread ~20k tokens/run for no benefit), but it's now in tension with the constitution's own byte-identical \u003cconstitution\u003e block being repeated in all ~40 agents — that block itself hasn't been trimmed by the new economy rule, and every new EARS rule added there (there are now ~15 sections) grows what's cached and reread by every single agent regardless of relevance to its phase. Worth an audit pass: does every agent actually need every constitution clause, or has it become the same kind of \"comprehensive reference nobody trims\" problem the economy rule was written to prevent elsewhere?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a087c7-1873-7a02-879e-f8fce74d0494","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788984367.219512,"turn_id":"01a087c3-2a1e-7401-ac78-e33107544865"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Let's make sure we're not overly prescriptive and also consider that we also write TS a lot and our plugins might be used against python and go codebases too","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a087ce-f06e-7460-be93-34d49147a41e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788984881.262262,"turn_id":"01a087ce-eeb8-74a0-aea4-60bb82f6f940"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"We can leverage tools and commands if available and where it makes sense for the language guide things like mutation and prop testing","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a087d1-4a60-7801-b759-52f260d98771","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788985035.360925,"turn_id":"01a087d1-48bb-7660-8fef-ad5c19c0b2c8"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"How should we take everything that you learned from the session analysis along with our discussions for a comprehensive improvement? Any new agents, skills, reference, etc?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a087d2-b36f-7721-9554-40780375539b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788985127.791537,"turn_id":"01a087d2-b201-7051-9899-bf9f14c38cf7"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Let's implement it??","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08818-66ae-76b2-b7d9-58b8daeabf58","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788989695.662938,"turn_id":"01a08818-6426-7061-ab53-205171fe211d"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Let's update readme, architecture, changelogs, etc for the top-level and plugins. Make sure codex and claude are in sync","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08865-9ebc-7d60-b48a-8acbb180fc9e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788994756.284925,"turn_id":"01a08865-9e02-7b01-8a4b-5f20e2531b6d"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"What user configurations?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08879-cbe6-7362-a4be-55a4db8105f0","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788996078.566357,"turn_id":"01a08879-caae-7d03-8dad-03827171d03c"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Let's push those up right?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0887a-339e-78b3-b509-46d8a74ae233","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788996105.118702,"turn_id":"01a0887a-3350-7563-ad9f-f57b510c960d"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"yes","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0887f-1916-7bd3-a852-eda75af1947c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788996426.00687,"turn_id":"01a0887f-18bb-7f43-97ff-08ec26d52898"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Do we need the release PR then? If you pushed?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08882-e2d2-78e2-953a-ec7e49b81b37","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788996674.258793,"turn_id":"01a08882-e273-79d1-b80b-b2e355b0ebda"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Why do we have conflicts??","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08887-c5c5-71f3-a7ce-af12588c366d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788996994.501882,"turn_id":"01a08887-c2ff-7270-b824-a5f6fa5fe6d3"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Just create the PR for me also","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08887-eba0-7ba1-9829-0ebc2daff551","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788997004.192221,"turn_id":"01a08887-c2ff-7270-b824-a5f6fa5fe6d3"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Just fix it","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08888-202a-72e1-aae4-479d09def21b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788997017.642437,"turn_id":"01a08887-c2ff-7270-b824-a5f6fa5fe6d3"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"https://github.com/orin-dx/agent-plugins/pull/8","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08888-8fd1-7d43-a01d-56a8e34b5943","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788997046.225813,"turn_id":"01a08887-c2ff-7270-b824-a5f6fa5fe6d3"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"We have a PR","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08888-9004-7e73-b8eb-18cd85258b96","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788997046.276377,"turn_id":"01a08887-c2ff-7270-b824-a5f6fa5fe6d3"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Let's make it a high quality PR description and title","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08888-fcd4-7893-8b40-c4cbb705b2f0","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788997074.132753,"turn_id":"01a08887-c2ff-7270-b824-a5f6fa5fe6d3"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"good","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08891-13e7-73b0-8ebe-d305f4556e9f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788997604.327279,"turn_id":"01a08891-1338-7cd1-af6f-01f8bee88790"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Can we make sure all our mermaid diagrams are up-to-date and follow the same modern look and feel?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a088a2-572f-72d2-a97e-9af8ccd93fbe","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788998735.663714,"turn_id":"01a088a2-565a-7a51-af8b-6d8ef6bc5083"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Push to main","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a088b4-b2fa-7220-9b71-c2813b9cae4c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788999938.810244,"turn_id":"01a088a2-565a-7a51-af8b-6d8ef6bc5083"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Do we need to make our GH template much better?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a088ba-20dd-7d42-9cf5-906a2c831ae9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789000294.62178,"turn_id":"01a088ba-2028-7c71-b1ef-640cfaa343ef"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"In the references?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a088ba-5ff3-7a40-b258-d29674cc5f2f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789000310.7712,"turn_id":"01a088ba-2028-7c71-b1ef-640cfaa343ef"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Does documentation voice guide well for succinct, friendly? eng focused in apporpriate places and user focus where user-first? Devoid of AI slop, filler words and wordy prose?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a088bc-6e18-7f83-9f8c-e551184c5d27","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789000445.46466,"turn_id":"01a088bc-6dc6-7191-8ad3-173e3f6d6267"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Any other improvements we can make to references that grounds them in guidance and outcomes vs prescritiveness and prose heavy guidance?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a088bd-6ef7-7541-b377-ea90f27eff31","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789000511.223005,"turn_id":"01a088bc-6dc6-7191-8ad3-173e3f6d6267"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"we value radical candor too btw from our agents, in our docs, etc","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a088bd-cbe2-7723-b0ec-923e2478e8b0","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789000535.010288,"turn_id":"01a088bc-6dc6-7191-8ad3-173e3f6d6267"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"do it","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a088c6-497f-77c2-86ea-89d5c2008408","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789001091.455649,"turn_id":"01a088c6-48bb-7040-a264-83f7cdb1775a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"6ott7021!","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0892d-e3d2-7070-8d92-9b0ad927bbfb","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789007881.170933,"turn_id":"01a088c6-48bb-7040-a264-83f7cdb1775a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Create changesets and a PR","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08942-ab55-7923-bd3e-33a3701c8f49","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789009242.965495,"turn_id":"01a08942-aaa6-70d0-9a29-9e5a737952eb"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Yes, make the pr","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08c63-17a0-7540-9a52-b5b035a30d40","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789061699.488269,"turn_id":"01a08c63-15f4-7e83-8640-aa486d938a84"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Should we organize the references a bit? The folder is getting pretty large. What pattern should we organize around?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08c6c-2c80-7713-883c-f228e31e1b93","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789062294.656634,"turn_id":"01a08c6c-2bb7-7db0-a8c0-517545c5865e"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"What's best for the AI? separate by patterns or languages + patterns or somethign else?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08c71-9078-7840-aaee-0b4ad14188b8","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789062647.928132,"turn_id":"01a08c71-8fcb-7971-9d86-01ba35f02d09"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"That sounds reasonable","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08c75-f642-79c0-8f9d-ccd764797485","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789062936.130629,"turn_id":"01a08c75-f598-75f0-bd16-352bac96f99c"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Already merged that PR right?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08c76-9928-77d1-b708-f6d53fc709fe","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789062977.83233,"turn_id":"01a08c76-9731-72a1-b5ac-463278dd7699"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Ok, let's tackle the changs in the next one right?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08c77-4c58-7f11-9290-4a448e7c5bcb","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789063023.704587,"turn_id":"01a08c77-4ac1-77a0-808c-4dde87d268d4"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"call_id":"call_XA0UobhHHx2XewnsCGZ3mK56","id":"ctc_0c3176283919dd68016aa2f4f13ad487d0bd99824397c8fc1f","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk git diff -- shared/schemas/changeset@2.json dist/codex/plugins/courier/shared/schemas/changeset@2.json dist/codex/plugins/mason/shared/schemas/changeset@2.json\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":12000}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789064398.197645,"turn_id":"01a08c77-4ac1-77a0-808c-4dde87d268d4"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_XA0UobhHHx2XewnsCGZ3mK56","id":"ctco_01a08c8c-d34f-73a2-890c-6736e47980e6","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789064434.511352,"turn_id":"01a08c77-4ac1-77a0-808c-4dde87d268d4"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"dist/codex/plugins/courier/shared/schemas/changeset@2.json | 4 ++--\n dist/codex/plugins/mason/shared/schemas/changeset@2.json   | 4 ++--\n shared/schemas/changeset@2.json                            | 4 ++--\n 3 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)\n\nChanges:\n\ndist/codex/plugins/courier/shared/schemas/changeset@2.json\n@@ -15,12 +15,12 @@\n     \"consumer_impact\": {\n       \"type\": \"string\",\n       \"enum\": [\"behavior-change\", \"new-capability\", \"internal-only\"],\n-      \"description\": \"Whether this change is observable to someone outside this repo. See shared/references/changesets.md for classification rules.\"\n+      \"description\": \"Whether this change is observable to someone outside this repo. See shared/references/delivery/changesets.md for classification rules.\"\n     },\n     \"semver_impact\": {\n       \"type\": \"string\",\n       \"enum\": [\"major\", \"minor\", \"patch\", \"none\"],\n-      \"description\": \"Version bump this change requires, per the Semver Decision Guide in shared/references/changesets.md. release-summarizer takes max(semver_impact) across a release's changesets rather than re-deriving it.\"\n+      \"description\": \"Version bump this change requires, per the Semver Decision Guide in shared/references/delivery/changesets.md. release-summarizer takes max(semver_impact) across a release's changesets rather than re-deriving it.\"\n     },\n     \"files_changed\": {\n       \"type\": \"array\",\n  +2 -2\n\ndist/codex/plugins/mason/shared/schemas/changeset@2.json\n@@ -15,12 +15,12 @@\n     \"consumer_impact\": {\n       \"type\": \"string\",\n       \"enum\": [\"behavior-change\", \"new-capability\", \"internal-only\"],\n-      \"description\": \"Whether this change is observable to someone outside this repo. See shared/references/changesets.md for classification rules.\"\n+      \"description\": \"Whether this change is observable to someone outside this repo. See shared/references/delivery/changesets.md for classification rules.\"\n     },\n     \"semver_impact\": {\n       \"type\": \"string\",\n       \"enum\": [\"major\", \"minor\", \"patch\", \"none\"],\n-      \"description\": \"Version bump this change requires, per the Semver Decision Guide in shared/references/changesets.md. release-summarizer takes max(semver_impact) across a release's changesets rather than re-deriving it.\"\n+      \"description\": \"Version bump this change requires, per the Semver Decision Guide in shared/references/delivery/changesets.md. release-summarizer takes max(semver_impact) across a release's changesets rather than re-deriving it.\"\n     },\n     \"files_changed\": {\n       \"type\": \"array\",\n  +2 -2\n\nshared/schemas/changeset@2.json\n@@ -15,12 +15,12 @@\n     \"consumer_impact\": {\n       \"type\": \"string\",\n       \"enum\": [\"behavior-change\", \"new-capability\", \"internal-only\"],\n-      \"description\": \"Whether this change is observable to someone outside this repo. See shared/references/changesets.md for classification rules.\"\n+      \"description\": \"Whether this change is observable to someone outside this repo. See shared/references/delivery/changesets.md for classification rules.\"\n     },\n     \"semver_impact\": {\n       \"type\": \"string\",\n       \"enum\": [\"major\", \"minor\", \"patch\", \"none\"],\n-      \"description\": \"Version bump this change requires, per the Semver Decision Guide in shared/references/changesets.md. release-summarizer takes max(semver_impact) across a release's changesets rather than re-deriving it.\"\n+      \"description\": \"Version bump this change requires, per the Semver Decision Guide in shared/references/delivery/changesets.md. release-summarizer takes max(semver_impact) across a release's changesets rather than re-deriving it.\"\n     },\n     \"files_changed\": {\n       \"type\": \"array\",\n  +2 -2\n","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0c3176283919dd68016aa2f4f5214087d0b0255cf7c6ccf319","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08c77-4ac1-77a0-808c-4dde87d268d4"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"One compatibility edge needs a deliberate exception: `changeset@2` is immutable, and its published field descriptions contain the old guide path. Rewriting those two strings would violate the repository’s commit guard; inventing `changeset@3` solely for a moved documentation link would create needless contract churn. I’m preserving the schema bytes and recording that exact legacy-path exception in the new validator, while every live Courier route uses the new path.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_0c3176283919dd68016aa2f4fb1c8c87d095f20014e4676b7e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"create_time":1789064436.246809,"turn_id":"01a08c77-4ac1-77a0-808c-4dde87d268d4"},"phase":"commentary","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"call_id":"call_5fO9ZYtgJtX5MsmSycYYvH2m","id":"ctc_0c3176283919dd68016aa2f4fd792887d0a005dbdaf046a9d5","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/schemas/changeset@2.json\\n@@\\n-      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether this change is observable to someone outside this repo. See shared/references/delivery/changesets.md for classification rules.\\\"\\n+      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether this change is observable to someone outside this repo. See shared/references/changesets.md for classification rules.\\\"\\n@@\\n-      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Version bump this change requires, per the Semver Decision Guide in shared/references/delivery/changesets.md. release-summarizer takes max(semver_impact) across a release's changesets rather than re-deriving it.\\\"\\n+      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Version bump this change requires, per the Semver Decision Guide in shared/references/changesets.md. release-summarizer takes max(semver_impact) across a release's changesets rather than re-deriving it.\\\"\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/tests/test_reference_reachability.py\\n@@\\n AUTHORING_ONLY = {\\n@@\\n }\\n+# Published schemas are byte-immutable. Keep narrow exceptions for exact paths\\n+# embedded before a reference move; live skill and agent routes must still use\\n+# current paths and pass the checks below.\\n+IMMUTABLE_PATH_EXCEPTIONS = {\\n+    (\\\"shared/schemas/changeset@2.json\\\", \\\"shared/references/changesets.md\\\"),\\n+}\\n@@\\n             for reference in REFERENCE_PATH.findall(contents):\\n+                source_name = source.relative_to(REPOSITORY_ROOT).as_posix()\\n+                if (source_name, reference) in IMMUTABLE_PATH_EXCEPTIONS:\\n+                    continue\\n                 if not (REPOSITORY_ROOT / reference).is_file():\\n-                    broken.append(f\\\"{source.relative_to(REPOSITORY_ROOT)} -\u003e {reference}\\\")\\n+                    broken.append(f\\\"{source_name} -\u003e {reference}\\\")\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789064436.246809,"turn_id":"01a08c77-4ac1-77a0-808c-4dde87d268d4"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_5fO9ZYtgJtX5MsmSycYYvH2m","id":"ctco_01a08c8d-1b7c-7182-bdf3-1e89d7a717f4","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789064452.988446,"turn_id":"01a08c77-4ac1-77a0-808c-4dde87d268d4"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{}","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0c3176283919dd68016aa2f506993887d0ab783914130b88c2","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08c77-4ac1-77a0-808c-4dde87d268d4"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_6Fe04lshr6TGkPcTCJY06VxD","id":"ctc_0c3176283919dd68016aa2f507a41c87d09bdf642d864bcba2","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk python3 tools/build-codex-marketplace.py\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins\",\"yield_time_ms\":30000,\"max_output_tokens\":12000,\"sandbox_permissions\":\"require_escalated\",\"justification\":\"May I regenerate the Codex bundle after restoring the immutable published schema bytes?\",\"prefix_rule\":[\"python3\",\"tools/build-codex-marketplace.py\"]}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789064453.620365,"turn_id":"01a08c77-4ac1-77a0-808c-4dde87d268d4"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom