{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:40:49.801Z","ordinal":9295,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a08c9a-83b9-7301-a5a4-1fe2b35b276e","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0c3176283919dd68016aa2f9a84c1487d09aa417d0116459be","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Not fully. The branch is close, but it is not ready to commit yet.\n\nMaterial issues:\n\n- Broken Sentinel schema link: [SKILL.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/sentinel/skills/gate/SKILL.md:57).\n- Ranger still names the removed `*-hazards.md` and `*-hazards-t7-t10.md` patterns in [adversary.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/agents/adversary.md:20) and [boundary-tracer.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/agents/boundary-tracer.md:20).\n- Ranger’s [scanner.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:34) requires literal grep patterns, but some reorganized references now describe search signals rather than commands.\n- Progressive-loading guidance incorrectly says one reference file or path. Some agents legitimately select a small set of focused references. This affects [AGENTS.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/AGENTS.md:47), [ARCHITECTURE.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/ARCHITECTURE.md:244), [constitution.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/constitution.md:72), and [Mason’s README](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/mason/README.md:109).\n- [Courier’s README](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/courier/README.md:56) uses the ambiguous bare pointer `changesets.md`.\n- The immutable [changeset@2 schema](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/schemas/changeset@2.json:18) still embeds the retired path. The test currently exempts it, so that compatibility decision needs an explicit resolution rather than silently passing.\n- Navigator’s Claude guidance remains more prescriptive than its Codex counterpart—exact code, mechanical execution, and “zero domain context.” That is broader policy drift and should be corrected separately from the reference move.\n\nEverything else checked out:\n\n- All 40 tests pass.\n- Codex materialization is current.\n- Plugin versions agree across manifests, READMEs, changelogs, and the marketplace.\n- `git diff --check` passes.\n- No other broken local Markdown links were found.\n\nThe green tests currently miss semantic/wildcard pointers, which is itself worth fixing. I recommend repairing the reference and documentation issues in this branch, strengthening the integrity test, and handling Navigator plus any schema-version migration as a focused follow-up."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1789065640343,"completed_at_ms":1789065649801}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:40:49.804Z","ordinal":9296,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0c3176283919dd68016aa2f9a84c1487d09aa417d0116459be","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Not fully. The branch is close, but it is not ready to commit yet.\n\nMaterial issues:\n\n- Broken Sentinel schema link: [SKILL.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/sentinel/skills/gate/SKILL.md:57).\n- Ranger still names the removed `*-hazards.md` and `*-hazards-t7-t10.md` patterns in [adversary.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/agents/adversary.md:20) and [boundary-tracer.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/agents/boundary-tracer.md:20).\n- Ranger’s [scanner.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md:34) requires literal grep patterns, but some reorganized references now describe search signals rather than commands.\n- Progressive-loading guidance incorrectly says one reference file or path. Some agents legitimately select a small set of focused references. This affects [AGENTS.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/AGENTS.md:47), [ARCHITECTURE.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/ARCHITECTURE.md:244), [constitution.md](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/constitution.md:72), and [Mason’s README](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/mason/README.md:109).\n- [Courier’s README](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/courier/README.md:56) uses the ambiguous bare pointer `changesets.md`.\n- The immutable [changeset@2 schema](/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/schemas/changeset@2.json:18) still embeds the retired path. The test currently exempts it, so that compatibility decision needs an explicit resolution rather than silently passing.\n- Navigator’s Claude guidance remains more prescriptive than its Codex counterpart—exact code, mechanical execution, and “zero domain context.” That is broader policy drift and should be corrected separately from the reference move.\n\nEverything else checked out:\n\n- All 40 tests pass.\n- Codex materialization is current.\n- Plugin versions agree across manifests, READMEs, changelogs, and the marketplace.\n- `git diff --check` passes.\n- No other broken local Markdown links were found.\n\nThe green tests currently miss semantic/wildcard pointers, which is itself worth fixing. I recommend repairing the reference and documentation issues in this branch, strengthening the integrity test, and handling Navigator plus any schema-version migration as a focused follow-up."}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08c9a-83b9-7301-a5a4-1fe2b35b276e","create_time":1789065619.819216,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
