{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:16:23.686Z","ordinal":9357,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0c3176283919dd68016aa301dd6ec887d0b3bc9fcd081a0b4f","status":"completed","call_id":"call_QQRqENGxguKrktZZuwl9ZsSh","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/sentinel/skills/gate/SKILL.md\\n@@\\n-- [Verdict Schema](../../../shared/schemas/verdict@3.json)\\n+- [Verdict Schema](../../../../shared/schemas/verdict@3.json)\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/agents/adversary.md\\n@@\\n-Check the input candidate@1's `taxonomy` field first, then load only what that one taxonomy needs:\\n-- taxonomy is T7 or T10: load the matching `*-hazards-t7-t10.md`\\n-- any other taxonomy: load the matching `*-hazards.md`\\n-Select Rust, TypeScript/JavaScript, Python, or Go from `workspace-manifest@1.language_files`. Never load two language packs for one candidate.\\n+Check the input candidate@1's `taxonomy`, then load one file for its language:\\n+\\n+- Rust: `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md` for T7 or T10; otherwise `shared/references/hazards/rust.md`.\\n+- TypeScript or JavaScript: `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md` for T7 or T10; otherwise `shared/references/hazards/typescript.md`.\\n+- Python: `shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md` for T7 or T10; otherwise `shared/references/hazards/python.md`.\\n+- Go: `shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md` for T7 or T10; otherwise `shared/references/hazards/go.md`.\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/agents/boundary-tracer.md\\n@@\\n-Load the matching `*-hazards-t7-t10.md` for the candidate language declared in\\n-`workspace-manifest@1.language_files`: Rust, TypeScript/JavaScript, Python, or Go.\\n-Load one language pack per candidate. Do not load the full hazards file.\\n+Load one boundary reference for the candidate language:\\n+\\n+- Rust: `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md`.\\n+- TypeScript or JavaScript: `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md`.\\n+- Python: `shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md`.\\n+- Go: `shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md`.\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md\\n@@\\n-My job is exhaustiveness, not accuracy — that responsibility belongs to the adversary. I have seen scanners that tried to be clever, that skipped matches because they looked harmless at a glance, that filtered out patterns because the surrounding code seemed fine. Every one of those decisions was a false negative that the adversary never got a chance to refute. A miss at this stage is permanent. I emit everything the patterns match against live files, and I let the adversary do its job.\\n+My job is exhaustive candidate collection, not verdicts. A candidate omitted here never reaches the adversary, so I preserve every applicable signal from the loaded references.\\n@@\\n-Run every hazard taxonomy grep pattern from the loaded reference against every live file and emit a candidate@1 entry for each match, so the adversary has a complete set of candidates to work with.\\n+Apply every hazard signal and search expression from the loaded references to every live file. Emit each match as `candidate@1` so the adversary receives the complete candidate set.\\n@@\\n-The scan is complete when every grep pattern from every applicable taxonomy has been run against every file in live_files, and every match has produced a candidate entry.\\n+The scan is complete when every applicable taxonomy signal has been searched across every file in `live_files` and every match has produced a candidate entry.\\n@@\\n-Use your search tool to run each grep pattern from the loaded hazard reference against live files. For each match, use your file reading tool to read surrounding code (enough to populate excerpt and taxonomy fields). Do not scan dead_files.\\n+Use your search tool to translate each signal into a repository-appropriate search expression. Preserve an explicit reference search when provided. For each match, use your file reading tool to capture enough surrounding code for the excerpt and taxonomy fields. Do not scan `dead_files`.\\n@@\\n-    \\\"grep_pattern\\\": \\\"string\\\"\\n+    \\\"grep_pattern\\\": \\\"string (search expression used; legacy field name)\\\"\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/courier/README.md\\n@@\\n-| `changeset-analyzer` | Changeset Extractor | sonnet / medium | Classifies `consumer_impact` and `semver_impact` from a git diff per the decision table in `changesets.md`, then produces a `changeset@2` whose summary detail scales with that classification. |\\n+| `changeset-analyzer` | Changeset Extractor | sonnet / medium | Classifies `consumer_impact` and `semver_impact` from a git diff per `shared/references/delivery/changesets.md`, then produces a `changeset@2` whose summary detail scales with that classification. |\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/courier/agents/changeset-analyzer.md\\n@@\\n-Beyond that: the changeset succeeds when each summary is written for a consumer assessing whether that specific change affects them, at the level of detail its semver_impact earns. Classify consumer_impact and semver_impact from the decision table in changesets.md — do not guess a bump that \\\"feels right\\\"; if a diff matches no row cleanly, pick the more conservative (higher) bump and say why in reasoning.\\n+Beyond that: the changeset succeeds when each summary is written for a consumer assessing whether that specific change affects them, at the level of detail its semver_impact earns. Classify consumer_impact and semver_impact from `shared/references/delivery/changesets.md`; if no row fits cleanly, choose the more conservative bump and explain why in `reasoning`.\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/AGENTS.md\\n@@\\n-4. **Progressive context loading** — one `<load_first>` block per agent, naming only the reference file for its cognitive phase.\\n+4. **Progressive context loading** — one `<load_first>` block per agent, naming only the focused references needed for its cognitive phase.\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/ARCHITECTURE.md\\n@@\\n-**Progressive context loading** — each agent loads only the reference file for its cognitive concern.\\n+**Progressive context loading** — each agent loads only the focused references needed for its cognitive concern.\\n \\n-- A `<load_first>` block names one exact path. The first directory identifies the concern; a language filename narrows language-specific evidence.\\n+- A `<load_first>` block names each exact path it may load. The first directory identifies the concern; a language filename narrows language-specific evidence.\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/CONTRIBUTING.md\\n@@\\n-- [ ] Declares a `<load_first>` block naming the specific `shared/references/` file for this agent's phase\\n+- [ ] Declares one `<load_first>` block naming only the focused `shared/references/` files needed for this agent's phase\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/mason/README.md\\n@@\\n-| `<load_first>` correctness | Present whenever an agent's goal implies a lookup it can't do from memory; its named reference file actually resolves |\\n+| `<load_first>` correctness | Present whenever an agent's goal requires a lookup; every named reference resolves and belongs to its cognitive phase |\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/constitution.md\\n@@\\n-WHEN an agent requires a shared reference file, it SHALL load only the file for its cognitive phase — not all reference files.\\n+WHEN an agent requires shared references, it SHALL load only the focused files needed for its cognitive phase — not all reference files.\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/README.md\\n@@\\n-Runtime guides live in `shared/references/`. Paths start with the decision an agent is making; language is the filename only when the evidence is language-specific. Agents load exact files during execution, not this index at startup.\\n+Shared guides live in `shared/references/`. Paths start with the decision they support; language is the filename only when evidence is language-specific. Runtime instructions load exact files, while maintainers use the index and authoring-only guides directly.\\n@@\\n-│   ├── references/               ← Runtime-pullable domain guides (split by concern)\\n+│   ├── references/               ← Runtime and authoring guides, split by concern\\n*** Update File: /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/tests/test_reference_integrity.py\\n@@\\n import re\\n import unittest\\n from pathlib import Path\\n+from urllib.parse import unquote\\n@@\\n REFERENCE_PATH = re.compile(r\\\"shared/references/[A-Za-z0-9@._/-]+\\\\.md\\\")\\n+MARKDOWN_LINK = re.compile(r\\\"!?\\\\[[^\\\\]]*\\\\]\\\\(([^)]+)\\\\)\\\")\\n+REFERENCE_LINK = re.compile(r\\\"^\\\\s*\\\\[[^\\\\]]+\\\\]:\\\\s+(\\\\S+)\\\", re.MULTILINE)\\n+RETIRED_REFERENCE_NAME = re.compile(\\n+    r\\\"(?:\\\\*|rust|typescript|python|go)-hazards(?:-t7-t10)?\\\\.md|(?<!/)changesets\\\\.md\\\"\\n+)\\n@@\\n def is_runtime_caller(path: Path) -> bool:\\n@@\\n     return parts[:3] == (\\\"harnesses\\\", \\\"codex\\\", \\\"plugins\\\") and \\\"skills\\\" in parts\\n+\\n+\\n+def local_markdown_target(raw_target: str) -> str | None:\\n+    target = raw_target.strip()\\n+    if target.startswith(\\\"<\\\") and \\\">\\\" in target:\\n+        target = target[1 : target.index(\\\">\\\")]\\n+    else:\\n+        target = target.split(maxsplit=1)[0]\\n+    if not target or target.startswith(\\\"#\\\") or \\\"://\\\" in target or target.startswith(\\\"mailto:\\\"):\\n+        return None\\n+    return unquote(target.split(\\\"#\\\", 1)[0].split(\\\"?\\\", 1)[0])\\n@@\\n     def test_exact_reference_paths_exist(self) -> None:\\n@@\\n         self.assertEqual(broken, [])\\n+\\n+    def test_local_markdown_links_resolve(self) -> None:\\n+        broken: list[str] = []\\n+        for source, contents in self.sources.items():\\n+            if source.suffix != \\\".md\\\":\\n+                continue\\n+            raw_targets = MARKDOWN_LINK.findall(contents) + REFERENCE_LINK.findall(contents)\\n+            for raw_target in raw_targets:\\n+                target = local_markdown_target(raw_target)\\n+                if target is None:\\n+                    continue\\n+                resolved = (source.parent / target).resolve()\\n+                if not resolved.exists():\\n+                    source_name = source.relative_to(REPOSITORY_ROOT).as_posix()\\n+                    broken.append(f\\\"{source_name} -> {target}\\\")\\n+        self.assertEqual(broken, [])\\n+\\n+    def test_retired_or_ambiguous_reference_names_are_absent(self) -> None:\\n+        stale = [\\n+            f\\\"{source.relative_to(REPOSITORY_ROOT).as_posix()} -> {match.group(0)}\\\"\\n+            for source, contents in self.sources.items()\\n+            for match in RETIRED_REFERENCE_NAME.finditer(contents)\\n+        ]\\n+        self.assertEqual(stale, [])\\n*** End Patch\";\nconst result = await tools.apply_patch(patch);\ntext(result);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08cbd-ae2c-7ca0-9da8-fdd13eaa77fa","create_time":1789067717.153861}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:16:23.698Z","ordinal":9358,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a08cbd-ae2c-7ca0-9da8-fdd13eaa77fa","session_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","root_turn_id":"01a08cbd-ae2c-7ca0-9da8-fdd13eaa77fa","response_id":"resp_0c3176283919dd68016aa301c4f03487d0a8ef7e0504f368c8","usage":{"input_tokens":69023,"cached_input_tokens":65024,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3643,"reasoning_output_tokens":972,"total_tokens":72666},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":264685,"cached_input_tokens":228864,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":7451,"reasoning_output_tokens":3398,"total_tokens":272136},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":137567209,"cached_input_tokens":134668416,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":607996,"reasoning_output_tokens":203944,"total_tokens":138175205}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:16:24.713Z","ordinal":9359,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a086d4-219f-74e1-8171-83f651770f25","turn_id":"01a08cbd-ae2c-7ca0-9da8-fdd13eaa77fa","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-74102f0b-7197-4ca0-ae7c-5b56e90f5f28","changes":{"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/mason/README.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -108,3 +108,3 @@\n | 5-part body structure | Agent body has: constitution (byte-identical to the rest of the ecosystem), backstory, goal, judgment, output, in that order, with an optional `<load_first>` immediately after constitution — no success_criteria, no role sections, EARS only in constitution/output |\n-| `<load_first>` correctness | Present whenever an agent's goal implies a lookup it can't do from memory; its named reference file actually resolves |\n+| `<load_first>` correctness | Present whenever an agent's goal requires a lookup; every named reference resolves and belongs to its cognitive phase |\n | Orchestration completeness | Every status an agent's own output can emit has a routing entry in its plugin's SKILL.md, or is documented as terminal |\n","move_path":null},"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/AGENTS.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -46,3 +46,3 @@\n 3. **EARS in output only** — WHEN/IF/WHILE/WHERE notation belongs only in `<output>` contracts and never-do rules.\n-4. **Progressive context loading** — one `<load_first>` block per agent, naming only the reference file for its cognitive phase.\n+4. **Progressive context loading** — one `<load_first>` block per agent, naming only the focused references needed for its cognitive phase.\n 5. **Schema-first handoffs** — define `shared/schemas/<name>@<version>.json` before writing the agent that produces it.\n","move_path":null},"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/README.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -289,3 +289,3 @@\n \n-Runtime guides live in `shared/references/`. Paths start with the decision an agent is making; language is the filename only when the evidence is language-specific. Agents load exact files during execution, not this index at startup.\n+Shared guides live in `shared/references/`. Paths start with the decision they support; language is the filename only when evidence is language-specific. Runtime instructions load exact files, while maintainers use the index and authoring-only guides directly.\n \n@@ -320,3 +320,3 @@\n │   ├── schemas/                  ← Versioned inter-agent JSON schemas\n-│   ├── references/               ← Runtime-pullable domain guides (split by concern)\n+│   ├── references/               ← Runtime and authoring guides, split by concern\n │   └── agent-best-practices.md  ← Authoring-time principles\n","move_path":null},"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/ARCHITECTURE.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -243,5 +243,5 @@\n \n-**Progressive context loading** — each agent loads only the reference file for its cognitive concern.\n+**Progressive context loading** — each agent loads only the focused references needed for its cognitive concern.\n \n-- A `<load_first>` block names one exact path. The first directory identifies the concern; a language filename narrows language-specific evidence.\n+- A `<load_first>` block names each exact path it may load. The first directory identifies the concern; a language filename narrows language-specific evidence.\n - Never load all reference files into all agents — attention degrades when the context window contains material the agent won't use\n","move_path":null},"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/sentinel/skills/gate/SKILL.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -56,3 +56,3 @@\n <framework_references>\n-- [Verdict Schema](../../../shared/schemas/verdict@3.json)\n+- [Verdict Schema](../../../../shared/schemas/verdict@3.json)\n </framework_references>\n","move_path":null},"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/agents/adversary.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -18,6 +18,8 @@\n <load_first>\n-Check the input candidate@1's `taxonomy` field first, then load only what that one taxonomy needs:\n-- taxonomy is T7 or T10: load the matching `*-hazards-t7-t10.md`\n-- any other taxonomy: load the matching `*-hazards.md`\n-Select Rust, TypeScript/JavaScript, Python, or Go from `workspace-manifest@1.language_files`. Never load two language packs for one candidate.\n+Check the input candidate@1's `taxonomy`, then load one file for its language:\n+\n+- Rust: `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md` for T7 or T10; otherwise `shared/references/hazards/rust.md`.\n+- TypeScript or JavaScript: `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md` for T7 or T10; otherwise `shared/references/hazards/typescript.md`.\n+- Python: `shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md` for T7 or T10; otherwise `shared/references/hazards/python.md`.\n+- Go: `shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md` for T7 or T10; otherwise `shared/references/hazards/go.md`.\n </load_first>\n","move_path":null},"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/agents/boundary-tracer.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -19,5 +19,8 @@\n <load_first>\n-Load the matching `*-hazards-t7-t10.md` for the candidate language declared in\n-`workspace-manifest@1.language_files`: Rust, TypeScript/JavaScript, Python, or Go.\n-Load one language pack per candidate. Do not load the full hazards file.\n+Load one boundary reference for the candidate language:\n+\n+- Rust: `shared/references/hazards/rust-boundaries.md`.\n+- TypeScript or JavaScript: `shared/references/hazards/typescript-boundaries.md`.\n+- Python: `shared/references/hazards/python-boundaries.md`.\n+- Go: `shared/references/hazards/go-boundaries.md`.\n </load_first>\n","move_path":null},"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/courier/README.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -55,3 +55,3 @@\n | `commit-analyzer` | Commit Author | haiku / low | Reads staged diff and produces a conventional commit message explaining why, not what. |\n-| `changeset-analyzer` | Changeset Extractor | sonnet / medium | Classifies `consumer_impact` and `semver_impact` from a git diff per the decision table in `changesets.md`, then produces a `changeset@2` whose summary detail scales with that classification. |\n+| `changeset-analyzer` | Changeset Extractor | sonnet / medium | Classifies `consumer_impact` and `semver_impact` from a git diff per `shared/references/delivery/changesets.md`, then produces a `changeset@2` whose summary detail scales with that classification. |\n | `pr-narrator` | PR Author | sonnet / medium | Writes a PR title and body from the reviewer's perspective — zero prior context assumed. |\n","move_path":null},"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/courier/agents/changeset-analyzer.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -40,3 +40,3 @@\n \n-Beyond that: the changeset succeeds when each summary is written for a consumer assessing whether that specific change affects them, at the level of detail its semver_impact earns. Classify consumer_impact and semver_impact from the decision table in changesets.md — do not guess a bump that \"feels right\"; if a diff matches no row cleanly, pick the more conservative (higher) bump and say why in reasoning.\n+Beyond that: the changeset succeeds when each summary is written for a consumer assessing whether that specific change affects them, at the level of detail its semver_impact earns. Classify consumer_impact and semver_impact from `shared/references/delivery/changesets.md`; if no row fits cleanly, choose the more conservative bump and explain why in `reasoning`.\n \n","move_path":null},"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/constitution.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -71,3 +71,3 @@\n \n-WHEN an agent requires a shared reference file, it SHALL load only the file for its cognitive phase — not all reference files.\n+WHEN an agent requires shared references, it SHALL load only the focused files needed for its cognitive phase — not all reference files.\n \n","move_path":null},"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -29,3 +29,3 @@\n <backstory>\n-My job is exhaustiveness, not accuracy — that responsibility belongs to the adversary. I have seen scanners that tried to be clever, that skipped matches because they looked harmless at a glance, that filtered out patterns because the surrounding code seemed fine. Every one of those decisions was a false negative that the adversary never got a chance to refute. A miss at this stage is permanent. I emit everything the patterns match against live files, and I let the adversary do its job.\n+My job is exhaustive candidate collection, not verdicts. A candidate omitted here never reaches the adversary, so I preserve every applicable signal from the loaded references.\n </backstory>\n@@ -33,3 +33,3 @@\n <goal>\n-Run every hazard taxonomy grep pattern from the loaded reference against every live file and emit a candidate@1 entry for each match, so the adversary has a complete set of candidates to work with.\n+Apply every hazard signal and search expression from the loaded references to every live file. Emit each match as `candidate@1` so the adversary receives the complete candidate set.\n </goal>\n@@ -37,3 +37,3 @@\n <judgment>\n-The scan is complete when every grep pattern from every applicable taxonomy has been run against every file in live_files, and every match has produced a candidate entry.\n+The scan is complete when every applicable taxonomy signal has been searched across every file in `live_files` and every match has produced a candidate entry.\n \n@@ -45,3 +45,3 @@\n <output>\n-Use your search tool to run each grep pattern from the loaded hazard reference against live files. For each match, use your file reading tool to read surrounding code (enough to populate excerpt and taxonomy fields). Do not scan dead_files.\n+Use your search tool to translate each signal into a repository-appropriate search expression. Preserve an explicit reference search when provided. For each match, use your file reading tool to capture enough surrounding code for the excerpt and taxonomy fields. Do not scan `dead_files`.\n \n@@ -57,3 +57,3 @@\n     \"excerpt\": \"string (the matched line and immediate context)\",\n-    \"grep_pattern\": \"string\"\n+    \"grep_pattern\": \"string (search expression used; legacy field name)\"\n   }\n","move_path":null},"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/CONTRIBUTING.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -100,3 +100,3 @@\n ### Progressive context loading\n-- [ ] Declares a `<load_first>` block naming the specific `shared/references/` file for this agent's phase\n+- [ ] Declares one `<load_first>` block naming only the focused `shared/references/` files needed for this agent's phase\n - [ ] Does not load reference files outside its cognitive mode (scanner loads hazards, not smells)\n","move_path":null},"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/tests/test_reference_integrity.py":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -7,2 +7,3 @@\n from pathlib import Path\n+from urllib.parse import unquote\n \n@@ -12,2 +13,7 @@\n REFERENCE_PATH = re.compile(r\"shared/references/[A-Za-z0-9@._/-]+\\.md\")\n+MARKDOWN_LINK = re.compile(r\"!?\\[[^\\]]*\\]\\(([^)]+)\\)\")\n+REFERENCE_LINK = re.compile(r\"^\\s*\\[[^\\]]+\\]:\\s+(\\S+)\", re.MULTILINE)\n+RETIRED_REFERENCE_NAME = re.compile(\n+    r\"(?:\\*|rust|typescript|python|go)-hazards(?:-t7-t10)?\\.md|(?<!/)changesets\\.md\"\n+)\n TEXT_SUFFIXES = {\".json\", \".md\", \".py\", \".sh\", \".yaml\", \".yml\"}\n@@ -60,2 +66,13 @@\n \n+def local_markdown_target(raw_target: str) -> str | None:\n+    target = raw_target.strip()\n+    if target.startswith(\"<\") and \">\" in target:\n+        target = target[1 : target.index(\">\")]\n+    else:\n+        target = target.split(maxsplit=1)[0]\n+    if not target or target.startswith(\"#\") or \"://\" in target or target.startswith(\"mailto:\"):\n+        return None\n+    return unquote(target.split(\"#\", 1)[0].split(\"?\", 1)[0])\n+\n+\n class ReferenceIntegrityTests(unittest.TestCase):\n@@ -79,2 +96,26 @@\n \n+    def test_local_markdown_links_resolve(self) -> None:\n+        broken: list[str] = []\n+        for source, contents in self.sources.items():\n+            if source.suffix != \".md\":\n+                continue\n+            raw_targets = MARKDOWN_LINK.findall(contents) + REFERENCE_LINK.findall(contents)\n+            for raw_target in raw_targets:\n+                target = local_markdown_target(raw_target)\n+                if target is None:\n+                    continue\n+                resolved = (source.parent / target).resolve()\n+                if not resolved.exists():\n+                    source_name = source.relative_to(REPOSITORY_ROOT).as_posix()\n+                    broken.append(f\"{source_name} -> {target}\")\n+        self.assertEqual(broken, [])\n+\n+    def test_retired_or_ambiguous_reference_names_are_absent(self) -> None:\n+        stale = [\n+            f\"{source.relative_to(REPOSITORY_ROOT).as_posix()} -> {match.group(0)}\"\n+            for source, contents in self.sources.items()\n+            for match in RETIRED_REFERENCE_NAME.finditer(contents)\n+        ]\n+        self.assertEqual(stale, [])\n+\n     def test_reference_paths_are_concern_first(self) -> None:\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/sentinel/skills/gate/SKILL.md\nM /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/agents/adversary.md\nM /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/agents/boundary-tracer.md\nM /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/ranger/agents/scanner.md\nM /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/courier/README.md\nM /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/courier/agents/changeset-analyzer.md\nM /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/AGENTS.md\nM /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/ARCHITECTURE.md\nM /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/CONTRIBUTING.md\nM /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/plugins/mason/README.md\nM /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/shared/constitution.md\nM /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/README.md\nM /Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins/tests/test_reference_integrity.py\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1789067783972,"completed_at_ms":1789067784713}}
